(Phnom Penh): At the Cambodian Red Cross Headquarters on Thursday, October 30, 2019, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, received a working delegation from the Red Cross Foundation in Beijing led by Ms. Zhao Jingling, Director General of the Cambodian Red Cross. Yes, Beijing Red City.
This is my first visit to Cambodia to learn about the possibilities of cooperation with the Cambodian Red Cross.
During the meeting, the First Deputy Secretary-General brought the remarks of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who greeted the delegation and reminded them of the relationship between the Cambodian Red Cross and the Chinese Red Cross. Starting from 2001.
She recalled that in 2002, His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen visited the Red Cross in Beijing, when the two national associations signed an agreement.
In the past, the Cambodian Red Cross has also cooperated with the Red Cross branch of Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region of China, and this cooperation has been implemented in the branches of the Cambodian Red Cross in some provinces in the country.
