Mr. Kem Rathviseth's remarks were made this morning, October 30, 2019, on the occasion of organizing a forum for dialogue between the Civil Society Forum and the Union of Unions and Communities in Phnom Penh under the theme "Strengthening Work "Cooperation between civil society organizations and Phnom Penh achieves the goal of sustainable development in Cambodia."
Through 24 forums already held in the provinces and in Phnom Penh, he noted that civil society organizations, non-governmental organizations, community associations and unions have the opportunity to listen and understand important topics and have Raise many questions and suggestions that have challenges or concerns in performing the work.
The President of the Civil Society Forum also claimed that in this forum, civil society organizations, unions, and community associations were given the opportunity to participate without any restrictions, all of which are important fruits of the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo. Hun Sen has a vision to strengthen the partnership between civil society organizations and the Royal Government.
He further assessed that as the Civil Society Forum organizes more frequent discussions and consultations, it will hear the challenges and will be able to better address issues with the NGOs operating in Cambodia. He added that all civil society organizations and unions can carry out their duties smoothly in accordance with the law without any restrictions.
