During the working visit, Dr. Donald Kaberuka will also meet with Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance at the Ministry of Economy and Finance. The procession of the monks of the Mekong region in the five Buddhist countries ends in a tumultuous end in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): After more than 10 days of marching from Chiang Rai, Thailand through Laos, Vietnam and Burma, Typhoon Hayatra along the Mekong River in Cambodia, Thailand, Laos, Vietnam and Myanmar has been completed. In Siem Reap province, on the morning of October 30, 2019, there was a procession and counting of more than 300 monks in front of the Royal Palace near the Banana Shrine.
Monks and Buddhists from the five countries participating in the procession also held a rally in front of Angkor Wat on the morning of October 31 before parting ways to completely close the procession.
The large annual religious procession of the five countries, which Cambodia hosts in closing, was initiated by the Po Khaya Chalay Institute 980, Thailand, with the cooperation of Buddhists in each country. The pilgrimage left Thailand on October 14, passing through five countries in a row before ending in Cambodia on October 31, 2019.
Mr. Supha Chhay Virak Phu Chung, Secretary General of the Po Khayalay 980 Institute, said that in 2019, his institute and its allies in the Mekong region were successful in organizing this event for the second time to promote Buddhism. The march was held for more than 2,000 kilometers, in addition to spreading Buddhism to strengthen ties between the five countries.
Mr. Supha Chhay Riraphuchong added that many senior leaders were invited to attend the closing ceremony of the Hayatra ceremony, while the welcome from the Cambodian Buddhists was also large, which means that Cambodia still adheres to the ceremony. .
He added that this is the second time that his team and allies in the Mekong region have joined forces to organize this major event, which runs from October 14 to 30, with a Dharma tour. The friendship of the five countries with a distance of more than 2,000 kilometers.
As the organizer of this event, he continued that the pilgrimage across the Mekong countries, ending in the territory of Angkor, Siem Reap province, gathered the Buddhists of the five countries to become one bundle to connect unity, friendship, good relations and learn about each other's culture. Including interests in various fields, including business and tourism, which prove the development, prosperity and peace.
It should be noted that the second Buddhist pilgrimage event will be officially closed this Wednesday evening under the presidency of Samdech Preah Akka Moha, the patriarch Dr. Tep Vong and Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh at Sofitel, then there will be Prayer ceremony at Angkor Wat temple as well.
Chbar Ampov District Governor Leads a Cleanup Team on Hun Sen Prek Pra Primary and Secondary School
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Cheng Monira, Governor of Chbar Ampov District, this morning, October 30, 2019, led the officers under the supervision of the Khan, the Khan Security Force and teachers, students to clean the environment and spray mosquito nets in the area. Hun Sen Prek Pra Primary and Secondary School.
On that occasion, Mr. Cheng Monira said that the work to clean the environment now is to prepare all students to enter the new school year, which will take place from November 1, 2019 onwards.
He added that the school is a nursery for general knowledge and education, morality, virtue and behavior to all students. Good school, good environment is also a favorite place for students to study. The school's current environmental clean-up efforts include: clearing rubbish, weeding the school grounds and spraying mosquito nets everywhere in and around the classroom.
Recently, District Governor Cheng Monira donated toys and equipment for Hun Sen Prek Pra Primary and Secondary School children and continued to build a small football field on campus for students to play sports.
The Chbar Ampov district governor also called on the board of directors of all schools in Chbar Ampov district to work to clean the campus and classrooms before the opening day of the new school year.
