Cambodia, Laos and Myanmar hold meeting to strengthen protection of migrant workers in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): The Second Consultation Meeting of Technical Leaders of Cambodia, Laos and Myanmar (CLM) on the Role of Deputies to Strengthen the Protection of Migrant Workers under the chairmanship of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior; Chairman of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking in Siem Reap this morning, October 30, 2019.
Samdech Krala Hom thanked for the participation of the delegations of the three countries, Cambodia, Laos and Myanmar, and all national and international guests in the consultation meeting of senior technical officials on the "role of sending countries in the protection of migrant workers". But held in Siem Reap Angkor, Siem Reap, the Kingdom of Cambodia.
"Our three countries are neighboring countries, have similar cultures, share the same border with Thailand, and our people have been coming to work in Thailand, both legally and illegally," he said. Lots of rules, crowds. "Some have been facing a lot of problems in the migration process from leaving the workplace to returning."
And each country has its own set of standards and procedures for implementation, and there are both strengths and weaknesses. Therefore, discussions to find a suitable standard for the three countries are necessary to improve the safety and interests of workers, as well as to reduce the risks during migration and the negative impact on workers, their families and our society. .
In addition, the "Global Covenant on Safe, orderly and legal migration" adopted in Morocco in December 2018 is also an important tool that all member countries need to promote in order to protect migrant workers. From all forms of trafficking and exploitation at all stages of migration as well.
