CCHR issues press release after launching "Cambodian Committee on Press Freedom Assessment"
(Phnom Penh): The Union of Federation of Cambodian Journalists (UCJJ) has issued an official press release following the initiative to establish the Cambodian Committee for the Evaluation of Press Freedom (CIMA) as a new writing mechanism. Assessment report on the situation and space of press freedom in Cambodia.
The Cambodian Committee for the Evaluation of Freedom of the Press is based on the results of the Second Congress of the United Nations on October 12, 2019.
This is the first time in the history of journalism in Cambodia that a self-assessment mechanism has been set up to reflect the truth, to dare to acknowledge the facts, to improve, as well as to ask all stakeholders to work together to improve the quality of the press to improve the space. Greater freedom in Cambodia makes the press more important in the democratic process and contributes to the development of a prosperous, harmonious and sustainable society.
It should be noted that SIMA's members include: Union of Media Federations, Media Clubs, Media Coalition, Media Unions, Media Associations, Press Heads, Editor-in-Chief, Teachers, Journalists, Media Elders and Legal Entities. Evaluate press freedom in the form of signing a memorandum of understanding to form an alliance and start work.
