Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay receives immortality at the age of 106
Please be informed that Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay was born on Wednesday, the 7th day of the lunar month of Chhnang Thao in the Buddhist era 2457, corresponding to the Christian era 1914 in Thoung village, Thoung commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province. His father is Acharya Lak and his mother is Su Ouch. He has 10 siblings, 7 brothers and 3 sisters, and is the fifth son in the family.
When he was 12 years old, his parents sent him to become a monk in the presence of Rev. El Kom and his parents sent him to study the Dharma in the presence of Rev. Moham M. at Wat Preah Puth Mean Bon in Phnom Penh. Later, he went to live at Wat Ounalom to continue his studies until he was 19 years old, before leaving the seminary to serve his parents.
* Qualifications and composition
The work of Samdech Las Lay has compiled 13 dharma books and built many achievements in Wat Sansom Kosal. In the 1960s, Samdech Preah Thommalikhet received a certificate of appointment as a lecturer from Samdech Huot Tat, a superintendent of Buddhist studies, a diploma in pedagogy and a certificate issued by the Ministry of Cult and the title of Preah Khou Saphiroth, appointed by Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath.
On September 17, 1985, he received a letter of commendation from the People's Revolutionary Committee of Phnom Penh and a letter of commendation from Phnom Penh Hospital.
Appointed Preah Thommalikhet to preside over the Trinity Church from the Council for the Defense of the Motherland of Cambodia.
In 1995, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk signed a Royal Decree appointing Samdech Preah Thommalikhet.
In 2001, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk was awarded the Royal Medal of the Kingdom of Cambodia at the rank of Major General.
On August 24, 2002, Lok Chumteav Bun Rany Hun Sen presented a letter of thanks to Samdech for his financial support to the Cambodian Red Cross.
On December 5, 2002, Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipady Tep Vong appointed Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay as a sub-committee of Meanchey district, Phnom Penh.
Knowledge and language that can communicate: The knowledge that Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay has is French, can read Thai, can speak Pali and Samlang. Samdech knows the discipline of Patimok, runs his mouth and knows the scriptures of Vutotoy, as well as orders expertly from Preah Dhammalikhet Moeng Ses, President of the Thera Assembly, Sangha (from the old society) as a teacher.
