Stung Russey Chrum Krom Hydropower Project is a Outstanding Achievement of China-Cambodia Peaceful Cooperation
(Phnom Penh): China and Cambodia are close and friendly neighbors. The relationship between our two countries is close and full of deep emotions. 61 years after the establishment of diplomatic relations, the two countries have always supported and understood each other.
In recent years, under the strategic guidance of the two countries' top leaders and under the joint efforts of the people of the two countries, through the establishment of the Belt and Road, the traditional friendship between China and Cambodia has grown steadily. And bilateral relations have reached the best stage in history.
The hydropower station is divided into two parts, 8 km apart. The hydropower project is a BOT (Build-Operate-Transfer) project invested by China Huatian Group Co., Ltd., which started construction in April 2010 and started production in December 2013. The average annual is 1199 million kilowatt hours.
Le Jianhua, director general of the hydropower station, said the station's annual electricity consumption used to exceed 30% of all domestic electricity. 2014-2018 The average annual electricity generation of 20% of the total electricity generation in Cambodia has greatly reduced the electricity shortage and contributed significantly to economic and social development.
Our Hydropower Station is the only hydropower station in Cambodia that has passed the test of water storage to the normal water line and is fully operational at the same time. Immediately after starting the business, implement the process model: remote control, no one to remember the operation and monitor the production process by the Internet.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced at the completion ceremony of the construction of the hydropower station that the Royal Government will reduce the price of electricity for housing from 2015 because the hydropower project can provide about 1 billion kilowatt hours every year. . Currently, the price of electricity for households in Cambodia has dropped to about $ 0.16 per kilowatt hour.
People have become unaffordable, do not dare to use, have easy and reliable access to electricity, quality of life has greatly improved, people are happier in daily life.
