(Hanoi-Vietnam): For the future direction of 2019-2020, the Cambodian Armed Forces and the Vietnamese Armed Forces have agreed to further strengthen friendship and cooperation on border management and protection based on mechanisms and National and international legal framework and human resource training.
The agreement was reached on October 29, 2019, on the occasion of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Commander of the Cambodian Army, leading a delegation of the Army. The annual meeting on border management and protection cooperation 2019-2020 with the Border Guard Command of the Ministry of Defense of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam in Hanoi.
The two sides reviewed the results of cooperation on border management and protection in 2019 and set the direction for 2020.
The two sides praised the positive results of past cooperation between the two countries' armies, which have made significant contributions to maintaining peace, stability, public order and security along the border, which is conducive to boosting economic and trade ties. Mutual karma and facilitate the living conditions of the people of the two countries ensure peace and opportunities for economic development together.
These results are the result of close cooperation between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Command and the Vietnam Border Guard Command based on the spirit of friendship, understanding and mutual trust with the support of the Ministry of National Defense. Of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Defense of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, as well as the participation of the people of both countries.
At the end of the meeting, the two sides signed the minutes of the bilateral meeting and exchanged souvenirs in a happy, friendly and cooperative atmosphere.
