Minister of Agriculture: Cambodian farmers are changing their habits from production to serve their needs to production for export
(Siem Reap): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on October 29, 2019, highlighted that in 2018, Cambodia produced more than 10 million tons of rice, more than 5 million tons of rice for export and import. Produced a total of 4 million tons of agricultural products.
Mr. Veng Sakhon stated that the goal of agricultural development is to promote agricultural growth and increase the export of quality and safe agricultural products by improving agricultural productivity, increasing value added and expanding market competition, and maintaining a balance of Use agricultural land and ensure sustainable management of forest and fishery resources.
The Minister of Agriculture added that progress in the agricultural sector has promoted Cambodia to become one of the top 10 rice exporters and the fifth largest exporter of organic rice to the European market.
All of this clearly indicates that Cambodian farmers are shifting from production to serve their needs to intensive production to export production and international competition due to high market demand. This is the additional confirmation of Minister Veng Sakhon.
The Minister added that, with the excellent support of development partners, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has established the National Principles and Symbols of Good Agricultural Practices of Cambodia (CamGAP) as a national standard, which is a set of rules and regulations. Can confirm both the quality and safety of agricultural products, especially on vegetables and fruits.
At the same time, in order to promote integrated measures for crop management and food security, the Minister advised the General Department of Agriculture and relevant units to continue good cooperation with national and international organizations and development partners to promote sustainable agriculture and food security. Focusing on:
First, to promote the implementation of integrated crop management measures to diversify crops, especially the cultivation of vegetables that have a competitive advantage to replace imports, with consideration and guidance to encourage farmers as well as all farming communities to implement properly. Intelligent techniques in cultivation, water management, management and application of fertilizers and pesticides.
In particular, select high-yielding varieties suitable for agriculture, environment, climate change, meet market demand and use good pure seeds to obtain high yields, good quality and high prices in the market, taking into account the modernization. Strong digital media (E-Extension) in conjunction with integrated crop management programs is essential.
Fourth, to promote the development of model farms and strengthen the management of farming communities by encouraging and strengthening the capacity of farming communities to produce on a large scale with standardization by implementing contract agricultural production mechanisms.
