Hungarian President János ÁDER expressed his deep gratitude to the President of the Senate for his warm welcome to the delegation. Hungarian President János ÁDER informed the President of the Senate that this was the first time in his history that he had paid an official visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia, especially 30 years after the visit of the head of state of Hungary. Cambodia since 1999.
János ÁDER said that in the 30-year history of Hungary and Cambodia, the progress of the two countries was similar. The development and progress of Cambodia has made great strides in public administration reform, especially the legislature has played an important role in passing laws.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum expressed his pleasure to see the friendly relations and cooperation between the people and the two countries have been continuously improving. This progress is reflected in the exchange of visits between top leaders, senior leaders, professional leaders in the ministries and institutions of the two countries, as well as a reflection of mutual support in the framework of international cooperation. Also.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum confirmed that his official visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia and the visit of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Hungary and to attend the 3rd Budapest Summit on Water October 15, 2019 in Budapest is a new opportunity and paves the way for the prosperity of friendship and cooperation in all fields of the two countries.
