The announcement of the position to help protect the EBA for Cambodia was made during Mr. Yanos Ader's meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the Peace Palace on the afternoon of October 28, 2019.
During his first visit to Cambodia, Yanos Ader expressed his admiration for Cambodia's growth and development. He saw that Cambodia's growth was a significant contribution to the preferential treatment of goods on the European market.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, during the meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the President announced that he did not support the plan to withdraw the EBA from Cambodia.
The Hungarian president, who also served as a member of the European Parliament, claimed that as a member of the European Union, he would do everything possible to protect the preferential treatment of Cambodian goods in the European market.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the President of Hungary for providing justice for Cambodia and helping to protect Cambodia in order to maintain this preferential system.
This initiative does not mean that the EU will start suspending the tariff system immediately or automatically, it is just the time to start the formal consultation process. Cambodia has six months to debate and explain the reasons to the European Commission.
If the European Commission does not accept Cambodia's explanation and still decides to suspend the preferential treatment, it will take 18 months from the start date (February 12, 2019) until it comes into force. In other words, Cambodian goods continue to be imported into the EU duty-free for more than a year before a new decision is made.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has declared that this European decision is extremely unfair, as this shows that the European Union has openly rejected the remarkable progress that Cambodia has made.
(Svay Rieng): The humanitarian work of the volunteer doctor team, Mr. HUN Many, is respected and valued by the people in the capitals and provinces throughout Cambodia from the free examination and treatment with the donation of medicine. Provides medical care to patients in urban and remote areas, as well as enhances the health sector.
