Minister Veng Sakhon Inspects Koh Ker Agricultural Research and Development Station in Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, and his colleagues, on the afternoon of October 28, 2019, inspected the Koh Ker Agricultural Research and Development Station, a satellite station of the Cambodian Agricultural Research and Development Institute (CARDI). ) Located in Svay Pat village, Romdos commune, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province.
He said that the remaining area of more than 70 hectares is a forest sanctuary, which the Ministry decided not to clear and expand to keep it as a conservation forest. The infrastructure around the station is 1 office building, 1 staff building with 5 rooms, 1 warehouse, 2 reservoirs, 1 irrigation system and 1 ancient pond which is managed and maintained by 7 officials. People.
Examining the actual situation and progress of Koh Ker Agricultural Research and Development Station, Minister Veng Sakhon praised the efforts, perseverance and strong will to research, produce, preserve and develop agricultural varieties effectively.
In order to make the station more prosperous, he also provided some recommendations and activities that the officials of the station of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province, and especially the Agricultural Research and Development Institute of Cambodia to implement, such as:
First, to update and continue experimental research on crops with high market potential.
Second, continue to maintain the building, equipment, especially the land and the forest of the station, which is a state property to survive.
Third, the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries shall cooperate with the Cambodian Agricultural Research and Development Institute to increase technical support and cooperation to the Koh Kert Agricultural Research and Development Station.
Fourth, to promote agricultural modernization in research, experimentation, cultivation and harvesting.
Fifth, should increase cooperation with the private sector in research and production of crop varieties to connect with market demand. Missing British woman on Koh Rong not found yet, authorities continue to operate with the use of dogs and all measures
(Preah Sihanouk): A 21-year-old British woman who went missing on Koh Rong, Preah Sihanouk Province as of the evening of October 28, 2019 has not been found yet, despite the joint use of force by the authorities. 200 people even use dogs, since yesterday and until today.
The British woman disappeared at 3:30 am on October 24, 2019 at a party on Koh Rong beach with a male and female friend who had just met before leaving for Koh Rong. .
Immediately after the disappearance, authorities and law enforcement forces under the leadership of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, and General Thong Lim, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, used more than 200 people, along with equipment and fishing boats, to search throughout the day, October 27. Yesterday and to this day, still not found.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chuon Narin told Fresh News that law enforcement forces were divided into targets, both in the water and in the forest, but had not been found as of this evening.
According to the preliminary assessment and conclusion, the victim may have drowned, however, wait to complete the operation and find the victim first.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor Kouch Chamroeun confirmed that the 21-year-old British woman entered Cambodia through Bavet Pass in Svay Rieng Province on October 15 or 16, leaving Vietnam because her father worked there. That.
Arriving in Phnom Penh, she stayed at a hotel with another girlfriend who came from Vietnam, and on the 19th arrived in Sihanoukville, and in the evening they both traveled to Koh Rong when boarding a boat. Six other new friends, including three boys, and when they arrived in Koh Rong, organized a party called "Waiting for the sunrise" from 5 pm to 9 am before continuing to Koh Rong Samloem The next day, October 25.
The Preah Sihanouk provincial governor added that before disappearing at 3:30 a.m., at 3:23 p.m., she was filming on her cell phone, which authorities found with a small backpack on a rock next to the beach. Sit during the party.
According to the assessment of the provincial police commissioner, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun concluded as a preliminary step that the woman may drown, however, both authorities and authorities have taken all measures to bring the dog to search, but still Not found as of this evening.
