(Phnom Penh): On Saturday-Sunday this weekend, the big annual event "National Job and Productivity 2019" will be organized as a convenient gathering place for employers, education providers, job seekers. And workers in job opportunities, recruitment and sharing of labor market information.
In addition, the exhibition event will bring a national productivity workshop under the theme "Productivity Strategies for Cambodia - Paving the Way for Global Competitiveness", which will share experiences by well-known national and international speakers at the same time as the exhibition event. This too.
It should be noted that this exhibition is organized by the National Employment Agency of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training in collaboration with the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Phnom Penh and the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia (GMAC) for two days, Saturday - Sunday, 02-03 November 2019 from 8 am to 8 pm at the Koh Pich Trade and Exhibition Center.
A total of more than 20,000 job opportunities will be provided by more than 150 large companies / enterprises from key sectors such as: banks and microfinance institutions, construction, hotels and hospitality, telecommunications, vocational education and training, manufacturing and Private recruitment agency in a total of 300 booths.
In addition to access to tens of thousands of job opportunities, participants will receive information on current and future recruitment plans and policies, curricula, scholarships, courses and skills development programs.
The National Job and Productivity Fair 2019 is to promote the Royal Government of Cambodia's labor forum mechanism as stated in the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 to improve the employment sector and labor market information in Cambodia, especially to provide a wide range of opportunities for the workforce. Skilled and unskilled to get a better job, save time, reduce costs and get a higher income.
In addition, the National Job and Productivity Fair also contributes to bridging the gap between supply and demand of skills in the labor market, as well as making it easier for young people to enter the labor market to get a job after graduating from higher education. Or technical and professional skills. This large exhibition is expected to attract more than 30,000 visitors, mostly students, youth, job seekers and workers from all walks of life.
Therefore, to get good job opportunities and understanding about increasing productivity, please all young people, students, job seekers and workers to visit and do not forget to bring your resume (CV) to apply for a job directly with Employers who are in need of recruiting.
