Nearly 10,000 Cambodian women married to Korean men
Such high numbers of divorces do not just happen to Cambodian women, they are a common trend in Korean male society taking foreign wives.
Korean diplomats and journalists say most divorces are caused by Korean cultural factors that require the wife to speak Korean, prepare food for the three husbands (morning, afternoon and evening) and help care for the parents-in-law. Etc. These are inversion to the new lifestyle of some Asian women today who prefer to eat out or want more family freedom.
Regarding the search for foreign wives, the Korean government has revealed that in recent years, Vietnamese women have become popular, with about 6,000 Vietnamese women marrying Korean men each year.
A survey of 920 wives in 2018 showed that 42% had experienced domestic violence perpetrated by their husbands. And recently, violence against a 36-year-old Vietnamese woman in front of her children forced the Korean government to issue a new law banning Korean men with a history of violence against their wives from marrying new foreign women. No.
In addition to the ban, the Korean government has turned a blind eye to the opportunity for foreign men to have more foreign wives in order to balance the growth of new people with old ones.
South Korea is currently facing two social problems: First, more women than men, they do not want to get married and do not want to have children. Second, Korean men in rural areas find it difficult to fall in love with women of the same religion due to gaps in knowledge, employment and income. This is the reason why most Korean men in the countryside have been targeted by young men, which is why they are turning to foreign women until they reach Eastern Europe.
In addition to the above factors, Korean men also often look for foreign women because it costs less than ten thousand dollars to get a wife, compared to marrying a Korean woman alone costs an average of nearly $ 100,000.
