Achieving the goal "no one is forgotten".
He added that visually impaired people have the highest percentage of total disability in Cambodia, and this high rate has increased due to the increase in various disabilities and the number of people with disabilities in Cambodia has been Increased every year for various reasons such as old age, stroke, diabetes, autism and Parkinson's disease, which is projected to increase.
The remarks of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, were made at the workshop "Input Collection Consultation to Reach the Marxist Treaty" on October 28, 2019 at the Phnom Penh Hotel with the participation of Officials from relevant ministries, institutions and NGOs.
It should be noted that Cambodia signed the Marrakesh Treaty at its June 28, 2013 meeting and was one of only two ASEAN member countries to sign the treaty. After the signing, Cambodia has not yet ratified the treaty, but Cambodia is determined to ratify it in order to fully fulfill all the rights of all persons with disabilities. And all kinds.
