Every year, the Francophone Constitutional Court (ACCF) convenes its standing committee meetings in its permanent member states.
In particular, for 2019, the Constitutional Council of the Kingdom of Cambodia is honored to be convened by the Standing Committee of the Francophone Constitutional Court Association to hold its first meeting as a member of the Standing Committee of the Francophone Constitutional Court Association (ACCF). This is also the first meeting of the ACCF in Asia since its inception.
The Francophone Constitutional Court (ACCF), which was renamed ACCPUF in 2019, was established in 1997 on the initiative of the Constitutional Council of France. The Constitutional Council of the Kingdom of Cambodia became a member of the Francophone Constitutional Court (ACCF) in 1998.
The Francophone Constitutional Court (ACCF) currently has a total of 48 member countries, all of which speak French.
