According to a press release issued by the Council for the Development of Cambodia on October 28, 2019, Minister Chiang Yanara informed the new Ambassador of the Federal Republic of Germany that the Royal Government has achieved many important political and security achievements. , Social order and socio-economic development.
The Minister continued that the Royal Government continues to maintain good macroeconomic stability and achieve high and sustainable economic growth of more than 7% per year for the last two decades, while the per capita income has increased by more than 1, $ 450 in 2017. This has made Cambodia a low-middle-income country.
In particular, in 2018, economic growth reached 7.5 percent, the highest growth in the last 10 years and about 7.1 percent in 2019 due to the strengthening of the private sector, tourism and construction, as well as the efforts of Royal Government to improve the business environment.
He added that per capita income increased to $ 1,568 in 2018 and continued to increase to about $ 1,679 in 2019. The poverty rate has been reduced to below 10 percent and the income gap among the population is low through the distribution of the fruits of growth to all sections of the population.
The new Ambassador of the Federal Republic of Germany, Christian Berger, expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the economic growth and development that Cambodia has achieved and the ambitious goal of transforming Cambodia into a high-middle-income country. By 2030 and high-income countries by 2050.
At the same time, the new Ambassador also pledged to continue and strengthen development cooperation with Cambodia by expanding its coverage to other strategic areas.
The German side has pledged 48.60 million euros ($ 54.40 million) for 2019-2020, including 30 million euros in concessional loans for rural road infrastructure development and 18 grants. 60 million euros. Including concessional loans announced at the end of 2018 of 30 million euros for the power distribution system, the total financing amount has increased to 78.60 million euros.
It should be noted that Sam Rainsy, the leader of the illegal rebel group, announced his return to Cambodia on November 9, 2019 to overthrow the legitimate Royal Government of Cambodia led by the Cambodian People's Party through mass forces. . With this announcement, he called for and announced funding to encourage the army to secede and oppose the Royal Government, as well as call for the King to abdicate.
