Thousands of parents, students and guests attend 2019 World Intellectuals Conference
(Phnom Penh): More than 2,000 parents, students and guests attended the 5th World Intellectuals Conference held at Sofitel Phnom Penh.
The World Intellectuals Conference was established in 2015 by IDP Education, the world's leading international education service provider. Nowadays, the World Intellectuals Conference organizes this event every year, which is one of the most important forums for international education and networking opportunities in Cambodia.
Mao Sreng, Director of IDP Education in Cambodia, said that the 5th World Intellectuals Conference is the largest event today, focusing on study and scholarship options.
The Education and Employment Fair also includes a panel discussion with experts, alumni from abroad, scholarship representatives and representatives from embassies and civil society. The forums focus on topics that provide comprehensive knowledge on skills development, career goals and international study options that help students and parents better plan for future study.
