Mr. Hun Manet: Strong Khmer does not depend on foreign companies, it depends on strong Khmer companies
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hun Manet said that as Cambodia grows, the company must grow, our potential is to grow. Strong Khmer does not depend on strong foreign companies, it depends on strong Khmer companies.
Mr. Hun Manet said, "The Cambodian private sector is very strong as a factor to contribute to the real Cambodian economy, because Cambodian companies do not go anywhere because our country, contrary to foreign investment, they can go to other countries, but "Even though Cambodia has the ability to expand to other countries, it will not abandon its homeland, because all sectors of Cambodia must be strong and self-governing."
Mr. Hun Manet added that the measurement of the growth of each company is not different from the country, we look at two points, first, the growth that focuses on the figures and results, and second, the level of development that focuses on two main factors: Human factors and working conditions, which are important factors in ensuring the sustainability of the growth of companies, the private sector and the nation.
He stressed that the company needs employees who are healthy, capable, knowledgeable and responsible, and the president has the ability and ethics to lead the company to success and together for the success of the private sector, private sector success, the country's economy. We succeed. This is the main foundation and contribution of the CEO Master Club and the management of all companies.
He said that in fact, developed countries in the world with strong economic growth, they are rich in entrepreneurs who have the ability to lead and manage their business to national standards and can absorb profits from Everywhere in the world enters their country, which strengthens the national economy.
"The Royal Government of Cambodia has always considered the private sector as the engine of economic growth and a real partner in the development of the country," he said. "The progress of the private sector is a joint venture of the nation to address the major challenges facing the private sector, as well as promote the sustainable growth potential and resilience of Cambodia's long-term process."
Dr. Sok Siphana said that in the current context of Cambodia, we see that the evolution of entrepreneurs in our country has a strong speed and influence. In Asia, a peaceful and economically strong region, this is one of the factors to give all entrepreneurs the opportunity to be more influential, have more vision going forward.
Legal Awareness: Accidental Murder
For this week, Fresh News Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, would like to raise the topic related to "Unintentional Murder" to explain to the people as follows:
In the spirit of Article 207 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, "Unintentional homicide" is an act that causes the death of another person by:
* First: negligence, carelessness or laziness. * Second: Violation of security duties or obligations required by law.
In the above sense, the word "negligence" is forgetfulness, lack of seriousness, stigma by the perpetrator. "Inattentive" refers to acts that are caused by unpreparedness by daydreaming. "Violation of security duties or obligations required by law" is non-compliance with the provisions of the internal regulations of any institution or enterprise or is non-compliance with the law. .
The above offenses are punishable by imprisonment from 2 to 5 years and a fine of 10 million to 25 million riels if committed in any of the following cases:
A. Driving without a driver's license or having a driver's license but not in accordance with the type of vehicle. In an intoxicated state with an alcohol content of 0.40 mg per liter of air or 0.80 g per liter of blood or more. Caused many deaths. Escape from the scene in order to avoid responsibility.
Overall, the crime of involuntary manslaughter is enshrined in the 2009 Penal Code, the 2015 Road Traffic Law, or any other special law of the Kingdom of Cambodia that explicitly provides for the punishment and punishment of offenders. Arising from the negligence, negligence or lack of care of that person.
