(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pak Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, said that food is a message of culture, identity, living in the area to national and international tourists. Food is a tourism product or service and a market share of tourism.
Mr. Pak Sokhom said, "Cambodia has a lot of potential for national cultural heritage and intangible and intangible heritage that has not been organized and widely disseminated to the world, such as food." "As you all know, tourism and food are essentially related in at least two areas, including food as tourism products or tourism services and food as part of the tourism market."
He said that in the composition of tourism services, food contributes to the formation of memories for tourists from the destination, which means that food is a messenger of culture, identity, local living to national and international tourism.
He added that along with the high growth of the world tourism sector, the World Tourism Organization has paid more attention to the contribution of achieving the goal of developing new tourism products and promoting food tourism as a traditional food. Abundant in the region to attract the growth of national and international tourism and get food and accommodation for longer.
He said that the tourism sector has contributed to the promotion, preservation and conservation of the country's cultural and natural resources, reducing global warming and supporting sustainable national development. Tourism is an important catalyst for peace, globalization, regional integration and the effective dissemination of nations and peoples.
He said that this is reflected in the growth of international tourists in the world in 2018 to 1.4 billion people at a growth rate of 6%, contributing to the creation of up to 10% of total employment, generating total revenue. $ 1.7 trillion, equivalent to 10% of the world's gross domestic product.
