Results of the Cabinet meeting on October 25
(Phnom Penh): The Council of Ministers on October 25, 2019 yesterday opened its plenary session under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Yesterday's Cabinet meeting was an important meeting to review and approve important work that is particularly relevant to the state process and the lives of the people to ensure the growth and development of the nation. And better living conditions of the people.
The work that was reviewed and decided yesterday is: 1- The draft law on finance for management in 2020 and 2- The draft law on the payment of the general state budget for management in 2018.
In addition to the two draft laws, at yesterday's meeting, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced the implementation of two strategies, including a strategy on public investment management system reform 2019-2025 and a strategy on public debt management. 2019-2023.
In addition to the above work, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also decided to revoke Cintri's waste management and collection rights to Phnom Penh Capital Hall to wait for the selection of at least four new companies.
The Prime Minister also decided to remove the garbage service from the electricity bill from January 1, 2020.
Issues focusing on how licensing and fees paid by telecom companies should also be considered, as these companies claim that they should rely solely on their telecommunications business revenue. . But the court said they must be based on the total revenue of the business, including sales of mobile phones and other revenue.
Ministry of Labor Reveals Results of Reduction of Factory Strikes and Demonstrations and More Tips to Reduce This Problem
(Central): At the Closing Ceremony of the Training of Trainers on the Right to Strike and Demonstrate Peacefully, Mr. Mong Kimheng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, presented the results of efforts to reduce strikes and demonstrations in factories across the country and Revealed more tips to reduce this problem less and less.
The closing ceremony was held on October 25, 2019 at the Police Academy of Cambodia, in which Mr. Mong Kimheng said that in 2018, the Ministry of Labor conducted 9,350 labor inspections and limited the number. 1,051 enterprises were fined 100 enterprises and sued 4 enterprises.
"The decline in the number of strikes and demonstrations is due to a number of factors, such as better working conditions, more effective labor inspections and labor disputes, and better understanding and enforcement of laws by employers and workers," he said. "Better and more mature employers and workers in professional relations."
Mr. Mong Kimheng's recommendations to the participants include:
1: Continue to share knowledge about the right to strike and demonstrate peacefully in accordance with national and international regulations to other police officers through the provision of training.
2. Use the knowledge gained from this training as a basis to carry out their roles and responsibilities with patience and high responsibility, avoid using violence or any actions that are contrary to the provisions of the law in force.
3. Continue to cooperate with relevant institutions by sharing information as soon as possible to prevent, prevent and resolve strikes and demonstrations that have occurred or will occur in a timely manner.
The Secretary of State requested the Ministry of Interior, the National Police, the Cambodian Police Academy, the International Labor Organization and the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia to continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Labor in organizing the training. To police officers in the provinces. Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang Continues to Hold Public Forum with Residents of 3 Other Sangkats in Dangkor District
