Two more suspects arrested in connection with 39 bodies found in UK
LONDON (Reuters) - British police on Friday said they had arrested two more people on suspicion of involvement in the case of 39 bodies found in a container truck. This is according to a quote from CNA on Friday night, October 25, 2019.
The two suspects were identified as a 38-year-old man and a woman living in Warrington, northwest England. They were arrested by British police on charges of conspiracy to commit human trafficking and murder of 39 people. Another suspect, a 25-year-old container truck driver, is also in custody for murder.
