(Phnom Penh): On October 25, 2019, the Certification Ceremony of Trainers and Local Unions was held under the chairmanship of Mr. Prak Chanthoeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, Representative of Dr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training.
Mr. Prak Chanthoeun commended the organization of this important event and thanked the leadership of the National Assembly of the Cambodian National Trade Union for its decision to establish a training program for trainers and capacity building for local unions and union activists of the National Assembly. National Union of Cambodia (NACC) to strengthen the capacity to understand the laws, procedures for resolving labor disputes and good relations between employers and workers.
The Secretary of State added that through the implementation of the National Social Protection Policy Framework and the high recommendations of the Prime Minister in the programs to meet with workers and people in the past, workers have received many new benefits. More practical, such as examination and treatment at public hospitals for childbirth for workers, etc.
At the same time, the Ministry has been focusing on strengthening harmony in industrial relations by strengthening the role of the Commission on Resolving Strikes and Demonstrations in all fields and strengthening the mechanism for resolving labor disputes, both individual and collective labor disputes. Disputes continue until the court has jurisdiction.
Mr. Som Oun confirmed that the NACC's plan for 2019 is to train 17 more trainers, union leaders in 200 to 240 factories. For the participants who attended the closing ceremony of the first certification course, there were a total of 87 participants, including 17 new trainers, trainees as leaders and 2 union activists equal to 54 from 22 factories, 6 members of the Education Committee and 10 members of the NACC.
Mr. Som Oun revealed that the National Union Congress of Cambodia already has a plan to organize the Ok Ambok program on November 9 to protect the nation, religion, the King under the shadow of Samdech Techo peace, in the territory of Kambol district, which will have workers and More than 2,000 people participated.
He also called on all workers to participate in the celebration of Ok Ambok on November 9, 2019 at the location of houses, rented houses or other locations that can be done in the spirit of maintaining and supporting the tradition. Khmer traditions support peace and national development.
