China ready to ask US to lift tariffs on agricultural products
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Senior US and Chinese trade officials will discuss plans to allow China to buy more agricultural products from the United States on Friday, but Beijing is expected to ask Washington to cancel them. Tariffs on tariffs, as well as some tariffs imposed on Chinese goods. This is according to a quote from Reuters on Friday afternoon, October 25, 2019.
Donald Trump has now agreed to only repeal the Oct. 15 tariff plan on $ 250 billion worth of Chinese goods, while the two sides have agreed on a number of issues, including the purchase of US agricultural products. Increase the openness of the Chinese financial services market, increase protection of intellectual property and monetary issues.
However, before the first phase of the deal can become a reality, Beijing is expected to ask Washington to abandon its $ 156 billion tariff plan, which will take effect on May 15. Dec. In addition, China is likely to try to demand that the United States lift tariffs to 15 percent on $ 125 billion worth of Chinese goods, which was implemented on September 1.
