National Anti-Drug Authority: Law enforcement officers play an important role in helping drug addicts get treatment
(Phnom Penh): Major General Lim Tong Huot, Director of the Department of Legislation, Education and Rehabilitation of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, said that law enforcement officers have an important role to play in helping drug addicts receive treatment.
He said this on October 25, 2019 on the occasion of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, in collaboration with KHANA, organized a workshop on the management and prevention of opioid use for law enforcement officers.
On that occasion, both Kunal Kecher, Deputy Director of the Indian Coalition for AIDS and Chuob Sok Chamroeun, Executive Director of KHANA, said that the support of law enforcement officials and local authorities is very important to support you. Use of drugs for health care and overdose of opium or heroin causes the death of an addict.
Lt. Gen. Lim Tong Huot thanked the Phnom Penh Municipal Drug Control Committee for its active contribution to the fight against drugs, to bring peace to local people, to reduce violence and other crimes. .
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Lim Tong Huot also requested the local authorities, Khans, Sangkats, especially law enforcement officers to help manage users clearly, cooperate with parents and guardians, and encourage drug addicts to receive treatment for drug addicts in Health centers, referral hospitals and national hospitals.
Russia's Defense Ministry announced on Friday that about 300 Russian troops from units stationed in Russia's Chechen region had arrived in Syria to carry out special tasks. They will launch operations to help ensure the safety of the Syrian people and maintain security, order and patrol designated areas, and to help withdraw Kurdish forces and their weapons to a distance of at least 30 kilometers. From the Syrian-Turkish border.
The move comes after an agreement was reached between Russian President Vladimir Putin and Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan on Turkish military operations in northern Syria. Under the agreement, Russian troops and Syrian government border guards will be deployed along the Syrian border with Turkey to facilitate the movement of Kurdish fighters and their weapons from there.
Kurdish forces are set to withdraw at least 30 kilometers from the Syrian-Turkish border, while Turkey wants to establish a 30-kilometer security zone. On October 9, Turkey launched a military operation aimed at ousting Kurdish forces and ISIS terrorists from northern Syria near its border.
