(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Phal, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, this morning, October 25, 2019, chaired the first meeting to prepare a draft law to amend the law on immigration and amend the relevant legal documents. The meeting was held at the Ministry of Interior.
Speaking to reporters after the meeting, Dr. Sok Phal, the chairman of the drafting team, said that the immigration law is an important law to control foreigners of all nationalities living in Cambodia more. Transparency and fairness in accordance with the rule of law.
Mr. Sok Phal emphasized that the new draft law or amendment to the law on immigration was made to strengthen the effectiveness of the management of all foreigners, reflecting the current context of Cambodia, while the existing law is still valid. Some gaps.
However, for the duration of the drafting of the law, Mr. Sok Phal has not been able to confirm how much time will be used, but he only confirmed that the draft law will be made accurately and clearly. There is also a study of neighboring countries and past experiences.
It should be informed that the immigration law that Cambodia is currently using came into force in 1994 with 7 chapters and 41 articles. This law aims to control all foreigners who come to stay in the territory of Cambodia.
Please be reminded that the Royal Government of Cambodia has just closed the campaign to confiscate irregular Cambodian administrative documents held by foreigners and permission to apply for declaration of alien immigration and application for permanent residence for 2 years and 6 months on the 30th. June 2019 ago.
The results of the two-year, six-month work found that there were 49,603 immigrants in 11 nationalities, equivalent to 182,673 families, 82,488 of whom were females. Of these, 125,893 were aged 18 and over, 54,882 were women. Foreigners who are considered as immigrants are foreigners who come to Cambodia legally to stay for a long time or to practice or do other activities related to industry, trade, services or agriculture.
