Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated this during a meeting of the Council of Ministers at the Peace Palace on Friday morning, October 25, 2019. Samdech Techo strongly stated that "there are two points that the CPP does not change: First. As long as the CPP continues to control the Royal Government, the party will continue not to tax the people's farmland and agricultural land. "Minimum wage tax."
The Prime Minister continued that now it is time for the Royal Government to adjust the taxable salary ceiling. Since the 5th legislature of the National Assembly, the implementation of policies to improve the living standards of civil servants, teachers, doctors, national police and soldiers, as well as workers, has been regularly paid attention by the Royal Government to increase the minimum wage and salaries. Minimum wage.
At the same time, the Royal Government always considers to ensure that the minimum wage and the minimum wage that is increased must be exempt from the obligation to pay tax on salaries in the spirit of easing the burden for civil servants as well as workers. More.
At the same time, the Royal Government also provides tax incentives on additional benefits and is not included in the salary tax base for any allowances that workers can receive, such as travel expenses, food allowance, baby allowance, contract termination. Or severance pay, seniority severance pay, and so on.
Therefore, it is necessary for the Royal Government to amend two new articles, 47, in order to increase the minimum wage that is taxable from the obligation to pay tax on salaries, by including it in the draft law on finance for management. 2020.
In addition, attention to civil servants and workers who receive the minimum wage to be exempt from the obligation to pay tax on salaries will also be made continuously, along with the increase of the minimum wage and the minimum wage in time. Later.
The CPP-led government will not permanently tax the salaries of civil servants and workers on the minimum wage and minimum wage, along with a no-tax policy on arable land for farmers. As a family, the CPP has been implementing from the beginning until now and will continue to do so as long as the CPP continues to lead the Royal Government.
