(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, stated that the Ministry of Information will set up a Telegram Group to gather representatives of active journalists, representatives of government institutions and other organizations to participate in discussions and provide ideas and opinions. The Ministry is considering adopting amendments to the Press Law in Cambodia to be more effective.
The Minister of Information said this on October 24, 2019, when he chaired a consultative forum on the amendment of the Law on the Cambodian Media Regime 1995, which was held at Tonle Bassac 1 Restaurant. The participation of Mr. Ou Sarin, President of the Cambodian Association for the Protection of Journalists, Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, and representatives of journalists from various institutions.
The Minister further stated that this forum is the first time for the amendment of the Law on Cambodian Journalists, as we know that the Law on Journalists in Cambodia has been passed since 1995, which is now Still considered a more open law than the press law in ASEAN countries and in Asia as a whole is recognized as a free law.
Mr. Ou Sarin also mentioned that the forum was organized to collect key input from all participants to submit to the Ministry of Information for consideration in revising some articles in line with the current situation. This is to contribute to the promotion of press freedom in Cambodia in expression and the right to information in Cambodia better.
Mr. Ou Sarin added that the forum will also provide an opportunity for stakeholders to raise issues with the speakers for comments to the Ministry of Information to amend the applicable press law. Today, too, to be in line with the development of the media in Cambodia.
Experts see the benefits of exhibiting wholesale products in trade centers to expand business relationships
(Phnom Penh): Product display at various exhibition events is done for the purpose of promoting its products as well as finding partners to distribute to a wider market.
However, experts say that through product launches and exhibition events in the business center, it is highly effective to get direct investment partners between product owners from factories and partners.
Mr. Thuon Sinan, Executive Director of B2B Park Business and Exhibition Center, located in Sangkat Khmuonh, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh, said that B2B Park Business and Exhibition Center will create many new events to promote various business sectors. Domestically as well as internationally to be more prosperous.
"We believe that company owners or factory owners have no intention of transporting their products back, that is, they all intend to distribute their products to a wider market through collaboration between traders," he said. And suppliers.
Mr. Thuon Sinan said that B2B Park Trade and Exhibition Center has a team of experts in consulting, guidance and marketing, which is a wholesale investment partner, to bring all the products to be exhibited at the monthly event. ⁇.
He added that the team of B2B Park Trade and Exhibition Center is not a direct buyer or seller of wholesale products, but a copy agent between the original owner or manufacturer and distributor partner. High responsibility for product quality level as well as the reputation of the investment company under the recognition of the relevant professional government institutions.
The Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, Mr. Oknha Lim Heng, expressed his support for the establishment of agents to connect and find markets for national and international investors, which is the best thing.
Mr. Oknha Lim Heng added that companies such as this type of agency can also work with the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to help promote the purchase of local products to export to foreign markets, which is a good thing.
