Koy Kuong returns as Foreign Ministry spokesman, replacing Ket Sophan
(Phnom Penh): Koy Kuong, former Cambodian Ambassador to Australia and New Zealand, has returned to his post as spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, replacing Ket Sophan.
The appointment of Koy Kuong as the new spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs was made in accordance with the Prakas of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs dated October 21, 2019, according to the Prakas of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
In addition to his role as spokesman, Koy Kuong is also responsible for assisting the Minister of Foreign Affairs in the work of the Information Department and the Policy and Strategic Planning Department.
As for Ket Sophan, a former spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, who holds the position of Undersecretary of State, he has been assigned by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to assist the Minister in UNESCO and to assist Secretary of State Ouch Borith in European affairs.
It should be reminded that Mr. Koy Kuong used to be the spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs for many years, only after he was appointed by the Royal Government as the Ambassador of Cambodia to Australia and New Zealand, but now he has been given a new position. .
Meeting and presentation of brand new pipe products of Chip Mong Industries
(Phnom Penh): Chip Mong Industries organized a gathering and presentation of brand new V-pipe to distributors and depots that always support Chip Mong products in Phnom Penh on Friday afternoon, October 18, 2019 at the Brewery. Cambodia.
With the public's support and recognition for Chip Mong pipes, which are high quality and leading in Cambodia, the company has produced a new type of pipe, the MacV pipe, which is most suitable for farmers to farm. Plantations and for general use to meet the evolving and high demand of the current market.
