As a thank you to all the participants and supporters of Chip Mong products, especially V-Chip Mong Industries, there is also a raffle with a special discount for customers who have participated and ordered Chip Mong products in Applications.
It should also be noted that Chip Mong Industries is one of the many subsidiaries of Chip Mong which has a reputation for supplying high quality construction materials with prompt service.
In addition to pipe products, Chip Mong Industries also manufactures concrete tiles and is a leading supplier of ready-mixed concrete in Cambodia.
The confirmation of the new US Ambassador was made this morning, October 24, 2019, on the occasion that the Head of the Cambodian Embassy allowed him to pay a courtesy call and discuss work at the Ministry's office in Phnom Penh. Koy Kuong, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, held a press conference on the meeting.
The head of the Cambodian diplomatic corps confirmed that Patrick Murphy was a senior State Department official and former Deputy Assistant Secretary of State, so the appointment of a senior State Department official as the new ambassador to Cambodia This also shows the goodwill of the United States, which wants to improve relations and cooperation between the two countries.
The new US Ambassador to Cambodia has expressed his commitment to improving US-Cambodian relations during his mission in Cambodia.
The Ambassador's statement was made during a courtesy call and discussion with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on October 23, 2019 at the Peace Palace. The ambassador's position was also posted on the US Embassy's Facebook page in Cambodia.
The US Embassy confirmed on its Facebook page that during the meeting, Samdech Techo and Muffi discussed the United States' long-standing support for the Cambodian people and for Cambodia's prosperity, democracy and sovereignty.
Patrick Murphy was approved by the United States Senate to be its Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary Ambassador to Cambodia on August 2, 2019, and President Trump referred the nomination to the Senate in accordance with Article Two parts of the US Constitution are responsible for "advising and approving" appointments by the President, including the Ambassador.
He is a former Deputy Assistant Secretary of State for Southeast Asia and a professional member of the Senior Foreign Affairs Committee. He was Deputy Chief of Mission and Chargé d'Affaires of Thailand from 2013 to 2016, in Lesotho from 2006 to 2008 and served as Special Representative and Policy Coordinator for Myanmar from 2012. Until 2013.
It should be reminded that Mr. Patrick Murphy on October 19, 2019 expressed his happiness with great honor to meet His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia in the Royal Palace to appear on behalf of As the new US Ambassador to the King. He also expressed his desire to meet with members of the Royal Government of Cambodia to strengthen ties.
Phay Siphan also said that everything that exists today also has the contribution of the United States and Cambodia is the sister of the United States.
