(Kampong Thom): 10 new houses, which were a precious gift from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, have just been built and handed over to the 10 families to live officially.
These 10 new houses need to be handed over by Ms. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto, Honorary Vice President of Kampong Thom Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, on behalf of His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, on October 23, 2019, while the Cambodian people all over the country are happy. Celebrate the 23rd anniversary of the Paris Peace Accords.
There are 4 families living in Tbong Krapeu village, Kor Koh commune and 6 families in O Thom village in Sen Aphivath area, Ti Po commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province.
The new house is made of galvanized iron, 6 meters long and 4 meters wide, each worth more than 1,000 US dollars, a precious gift from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
On behalf of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, Ms. Khieu Sina stated that in all circumstances, especially when people face difficulties and shortages, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always take care and help to consider the well-being and help to solve There are always shortages of people, especially families, widows, the elderly and orphans.
She continued that, like the 10 new houses handed over today, it is a clear proof that at all times, the two princes are always living with the well-being of our citizens. Therefore, you must live in hope and continue to strive as long as Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, remain.
She said that the most important thing to do is to take care of health, to live hygienically and to strive to grow crops and raise animals, grow mixed crops on the land as much as possible to improve daily life. Better.
On that occasion, as a bond for this new day, through Ms. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto, sponsored the families who received 10 new houses, each family received 200,000 Riels, rice, sugar, milk, water. Lemon juice, soy sauce, fish sauce, salt, minced fish, medicine and a kit.
She and her colleagues also donated more than 800,000 Riels to families with twins to alleviate the difficulties in supplying milk for their babies.
Please be reminded that from 2008 to mid-October 2019, through Mrs. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto, Samdech Kittipritthbandit helped to build houses for poor and old families and widows in Santuk district. Kampong Thom has 351 units.
