In response, the ambassador promised to bring Peace Corps volunteers, hoping this year or next year to join the boating.
In addition to strengthening and expanding the current bilateral cooperation, the Prime Minister and the US Ambassador also discussed international cooperation, especially at the United Nations level.
In another framework, ASEAN and the United States, as Cambodia will chair ASEAN in 2022. Because the United States values ASEAN, the United States wants to see closer US-ASEAN cooperation.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn stressed that "what is important is that it seems to open a new page, strengthen and expand bilateral relations, as well as bilateral cooperation in all fields."
Also, because next year is the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries, so the Ambassador as well as Cambodia will cooperate in some activities to celebrate the anniversary of this relationship.
