October 23, 2019 is the 28th anniversary of the Paris Peace Agreement (October 23, 1991-October 23, 2019). This is an agreement that has been raised differently by government officials and some politicians, to the point that some politicians have argued that the international community still has the right to get sick and to get involved in political issues in Cambodia.
According to the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, so far, Cambodia has its own constitution and Cambodia is the owner of its own destiny and has sovereignty as well as full independence. In this regard, he urged the politicians not to take the Paris Peace Agreement to distort Cambodia's story to become a foreign story.
Mr. Phay Siphan added, "Article 2 also clearly states how the Constitution must be clear about the meaning of the peace agreement from the parties to the armed conflict, not a treaty with foreigners, we have agreed With armed groups arguing politically. So this is Cambodian and Cambodian politics, while foreigners have a duty to stand on only two points: rehabilitation and development.
He added that now Cambodia has already entered the development of the country. This development is self-imposed and everything that is the essence of the peace agreement, the parties to Cambodia's armed conflict has become the essence of the Constitution.
He added that the peace agreement also made it clear that when Cambodia has a constitution, whatever means or governing force in elections, Cambodia's state control falls on Cambodia.
"Cambodia is an independent state, a state that has been able to sit at the United Nations since we had the constitution," he said. "So what they are turning Cambodia into an international affair of other countries is impossible."
Phay Siphan considers that those who wish to revise the Paris Peace Agreement are tantamount to seeking to overthrow the Cambodian Constitution and to overthrow the Cambodian regime.
"So what we are trying to do is we are implementing our constitution and those who have the idea of bringing in foreigners are not responding to what the UN Security Council did to help Cambodia at that time."
He recalled that at that time, the UN Security Council issued a resolution ordering all countries to withdraw from Cambodia's political involvement, to stop providing weapons to Cambodia to continue the conflict. The obligations of the UN Security Council make it clear that foreigners other than Cambodia must withdraw from Cambodia, respect Cambodia's sovereignty and independence.
He said that Cambodia's constitution has been prepared and the regime has been prepared. That is the sovereignty of Cambodia, and the United Nations High Commissioner for Nationality (SNC) dissolved when Cambodia had a constitution.
"Now, development is in the hands of Cambodia, and Cambodia itself is responsible for its own destiny," he said.
