(Phnom Penh): Japan claims that it will continue to expand relations and cooperation with Cambodia by helping to find markets for Cambodian products, expanding the capacity of the port of Sihanoukville and continuing to provide assistance in other areas to promote growth in Cambodia.
Mr. Kao Kem Hourn, Deputy Prime Minister, stated that during the meeting, the Japanese Ambassador confirmed that Japan will continue to cooperate with Cambodia, including supporting the promotion of bilateral cooperation between the two countries. Even better, such as politics, economy, culture and other fields.
Regarding this relationship, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the relationship between the two countries has reached a high level as a strategic partnership by the top leaders of the two countries through the provision of direct flights between the two countries, which can facilitate It also conducts diplomacy, investors and tourism between the two countries.
Samdech Techo continued that the trade volume between Cambodia and Japan has increased steadily and Samdech would like to see the trade volume between the two countries continue to grow further, including investment from Japanese investors in Cambodia in the future.
The Prime Minister also wants to see economic cooperation between the two countries grow as well as other sectors.
The Ambassador pledged that during his tenure in Cambodia, he would work to strengthen the bilateral cooperation to be more prosperous, fruitful and more successful between the two countries.
He added that the Royal Government of Japan will continue to assist Cambodia in promoting the export of Cambodian products to international markets. Japan continues to provide demining assistance to Cambodia and unexploded ordnance.
Mr. Masahiro Mikami said that Japan is interested in providing assistance in the electricity sector in Cambodia, including continuing to make a master plan for the development of the port of Sihanoukville.
Regarding this port, Samdech Techo said that he wanted Japan to prepare a master plan for the development of Sihanoukville port quickly and successfully. The Prime Minister said that the construction of a deep-water port in Sihanoukville will help strengthen the port's ability to receive large ships without transferring some goods at the ports of Vietnam, Singapore and Malaysia.
At the meeting, senior WB and IMF officials praised Cambodia for achieving high economic growth and rapid poverty reduction. This achievement has been highly praised and appreciated by all WB member countries and has greatly improved and enhanced Cambodia's image in the WB.
This testimony was made possible by the approval of the Executive Board, which represents all members of the WB, on the "Cambodia-WB Cooperation Framework Document 2019-2013" in May in a unanimous vote. . Such unanimous support is a very special case and very rare for other countries.
In 2019, the WB has approved a total of 210 million US dollars in cooperation financing for Cambodia, and plans to approve at least another 215 million US dollars in financing for Cambodia in 2020.
At the same time, Mr. Vongsey Visoth asked the WB to provide financing to support large projects that have a major impact on the development of the country and to reduce project operating costs while continuing to improve project quality and efficiency. To meet the needs of Cambodia's development in the new phase.
Through the above meeting, the Cambodian delegation and the WB also focused on discussing the strengthening and expansion of cooperation and partnership to be stronger, especially the strengthening of Cambodia's ownership. The two sides also discussed the possibilities and opportunities for expanding the operations of the International Finance Corporation (IFC), the WB's private sector financing body, to provide more credit to Cambodia's private sector.
In a working meeting with senior IMF officials, the two sides focused on providing technical assistance to support budget reform and tax modernization, as well as strengthening government statistics management.
On the occasion of the annual participation of the WB and the IMF, Mr. Vongsy Visoth also met with Mr. Pes Osson Fried, Secretary of State for Swedish International Cooperation. During the meeting, the two sides discussed priorities for cooperation and partnership between Cambodia and Sweden for the next five years.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth thanked Sweden for its continued support for Cambodia's development and for being a good partner. He also briefed the Swedish side on the process and implementation of democracy, the rule of law and respect for human rights in Cambodia.
It should be noted that the regular meeting of the WB and IMF in 2019 was held under the theme "WB's vision towards achieving the goals of the 2030 development agenda and sustainable development goals." The meeting assessed that the world is facing a high risk of uncertainty and the global economy is shaken by policies, economic protectionism, tariff barriers and trade wars.
However, the meeting agreed that the WB must be more committed and strong than ever in fulfilling its mission to support member states in promoting economic growth and improving the lives of human beings in the world. Get out of poverty and move towards prosperity. Germany expresses willingness to strengthen cooperation and relations with Cambodia and wants to open the first Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Germany, one of the great powers in the European Union, has shown its strong will to strengthen cooperation and better relations with Cambodia. In addition, the German Chamber of Commerce plans to open its first office in Cambodia to expand trade between the two countries.
Confirmation of the position of strengthening cooperation and relations between Cambodia and Germany was made during a working meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Christian Berger, the new German Ambassador to Cambodia on the 23rd. This October 2019 at the Peace Palace.
Kao Kem Hourn, Deputy Prime Minister, said after the meeting that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the new German Ambassador expressed great satisfaction over the current improvement in cooperation and relations between the two countries. .
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his hope that during his mission as Ambassador to Cambodia, Mr. Christian Burger will strive to further strengthen and expand the bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and Germany.
In response, the Ambassador pledged to do his best to contribute to the further expansion of German-Cambodian cooperation and relations. During the meeting, the German Ambassador also thanked the Cambodian government for supporting Germany's candidacy at the United Nations in the past.
Promoting trade and investment between Cambodia and Germany is also one of the topics discussed at the meeting.
According to Kao Kem Hourn, the German ambassador saw that Cambodia and Germany still have a lot of potential to boost cooperation on trade and investment. The Ambassador stated that the German Chamber of Commerce now wants to open its first Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, as many large German companies are interested in Cambodia's economic growth and are willing to invest in Cambodia.
The Prime Minister agrees with the German Ambassador's view on trade and investment between the two countries. Samdech Techo mentioned that the economic and trade sector between the two countries is growing a lot and Cambodia also imports a lot from Germany, such as cars. At the same time, Cambodia also exports a lot of goods to Germany, such as shoes and clothes.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, reminded that in the past, Cambodia bought one of the two generators from Germany to generate electricity to meet the demand. There are also breweries that use German technology to brew beer in Cambodia.
Through these trade activities, Samdech Techo emphasized that the business and trade sector between Cambodia and Germany has a deeper relationship. Therefore, the intention to open a German Chamber of Commerce office in Cambodia is a good thing, can contribute significantly to boost trade, such as the economy between the two countries.
Samdech Techo also informed the German Ambassador about the preparations for hosting the upcoming Asia-Europe Summit in 2020, while Germany will chair the European Union. Therefore, the two countries will work together to make the Asia-Europe Meeting fruitful and successful.
