(Phnom Penh): In order to raise the value of humanitarian work better and for the benefit of our Cambodian people who are in need of relief from various difficulties such as disasters, the Cambodian Red Cross and the ICRC have appealed. Together to all relevant institutions seek to use
And proper protection of the Red Cross and Red Crescent emblems.
Institutions that can use the Red Cross or Red Crescent logo are to use it in accordance with international human rights law, especially to protect anyone who acts arbitrarily without proper permission and is not authorized to use the Red Cross or Red Crescent logo. Other misleading images, especially misuse, that will affect the humanitarian work and the interests of our citizens.
This was jointly confirmed by Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross and Representative of the ICRC (ICRC), Mr. Roman Paramov, on the occasion of the opening of the Dissemination Course on Personality and International Humanitarian Law to you. National newspaper from about 40 institutions, which took place on October 22, 2019 at the Himawari Hotel.
On that occasion, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak also stated the important point in using the image properly to avoid any bad effects that affect the reputation of the Cambodian Red Cross, especially not to any person take the image. Of the Red Cross, Red Crescent and Red Crystal used for personal gain and affect the interests of the nation and the people.
Any person who misuses, deceives, arbitrarily misleads, regardless of the purpose of the use, will also be punished according to the law in force.
At the same time, the First Deputy Secretary-General and the ICRC Representative also outlined the seven fundamental principles that have always been consistently applied to contribute to poverty reduction, protection of human dignity and protection of humanitarian values. Victims include: Impartiality, Neutrality, Independence, Volunteer Service, Unity and Globalization.
Please be informed that the Cambodian Red Cross, with Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Royal Mother of Cambodia as the Honorary President and under the wise leadership of Samdech Bun Rany Hun Sen as the President, has led and consistently led in Humanitarian causes rescue the most vulnerable and vulnerable people across the country with high transparency and efficiency every year.
