(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pech Sophoan, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and Co-Chair of the National Task Force for Prey Kabbas District, Takeo Province, said that the root cause of poverty is due to the low level of education crisis. Productivity is also low.
This statement was made at a forum on education, training, technical and vocational training and scholarship information for students who have just graduated from high school 2019 at the office of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Prey Kabbas district, on October 22, 2019.
He said that technical and vocational education and training has played an important role in the socio-economic development of the country, as well as the creation and creation of better jobs and the promotion of better living standards for each citizen.
He said that at present, most people, as well as students and parents, still do not fully understand the importance and value of technical and vocational education, while general education is just a basic or a start.
The next role is to provide technical and vocational education and training, which is to equip and develop skills and abilities continuously throughout life to meet the current and future job and career needs in the job market in response to changes in skills needs and job changes. With the socio-economic development and the higher aspirations of each citizen.
