Kratie Province to Celebrate Mekong River Dolphin Day 2019 from October 25-27
(Kratie): Kratie Provincial Administration, in collaboration with the Fisheries Administration, the Provincial Department of Tourism, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and WWF, is planning to organize "Mekong Dolphin Day 2019" under the theme "Increase dolphins, increase tourism, increase livelihood" from October 25-27 in Kratie City in order to strengthen the conservation of Mekong River dolphins to develop sustainable tourism.
He said that during the three days of the Mekong Dolphin Day, there will be many entertainment activities such as concerts, exhibitions of local products, running races, cycling, tree planting, camping, cleaning the city, visiting dolphins and resorts. Painting competitions and car and grapefruit eating contests.
Mr. Ratana added that through the dolphin conservation project of WWF Cambodia, Kratie and Stung Treng Provincial Administration, the number of Mekong River dolphins has increased by about 15%, from 80 in 2015 to 92 in 2017.
