(Phnom Penh): Today marks the 28th anniversary of the Paris Peace Agreement (October 23, 1991-October 23, 2019). The Paris Peace Accords, although terminated after the re-establishment of the Kingdom after the 1993 elections, are considered by Cambodian politicians and the people to be a valuable day for a return to peace and an end to division. In Cambodia.
However, until now, there are still different interpretations between the government and some politicians.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder of the Paris Peace Agreement, on October 23, 2018, during a meeting with Cambodians in Switzerland, spent about three hours explaining the details of the negotiation process. Paris Peace Agreement and some events after the day of the Paris Peace Agreement.
The Prime Minister emphasized that despite the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991, the civil war in Cambodia continued, caused by Democratic Kampuchea (Pol Pot). Under Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy, the civil war was completely ended in 1998, with Cambodia throughout the country experiencing complete peace and prosperity to this day.
Samdech Techo wished all compatriots happiness and good luck on the 28th anniversary of the Paris Agreement.
Agriculture Minister Tells USAID Director of Agriculture and Food Security Program on Cambodia's Agricultural Development Strategy for the Next 5 Years
On that occasion, the Minister of Agriculture expressed his deep gratitude to the US Government through USAID for its financial support for the implementation of the above program and thanked all the relevant working groups for their cooperation in implementing the program. We are proud that this achievement has been benefiting both the household economy, rural farmers, income growth, product growth, value added and market stability.
In particular, for the strategy for the development of Cambodia's agricultural sector for the next 5 years, the Minister recommended eight key recommendations:
First, training human resources is a priority of the Ministry as well as the Royal Government in terms of technology, experience and practical implementation, mainly facilitating or orienting them to participate in the private sector or create their own jobs by bringing new and modern skills. Modern, adaptable to the context of climate change, environment and innovation.
Second, strengthening and expanding the implementation of sanitary and phytosanitary (SPS) on production and in the processing sector is an important source for the export of Cambodian agricultural products to international markets, both now and in the future, and this is the policy. Ministry priority.
Third, the construction of key support infrastructure is a necessary and subsequent activity in the development of the agricultural sector, especially the establishment of a cold chain production system in the production of vegetables, meat and fishery products, which some ASEAN member countries are actively implementing. And he asked USAID to consider this in depth.
Fourthly, the Minister of Angkor Rice asked USAID to consider strengthening the private sector to participate in seed production, drying plants, warehousing and improving the quality of production and packaging.
Fifth, strengthen the implementation of contract agricultural production to ensure fairness between producers and the private sector (buyers), supply quantity, quality, price and market.
Sixth, strengthen the implementation of forest laws, sustainable management of natural resources and forests by working in partnership with forest communities and institutions to avoid accusations.
The Minister expressed the hope and belief that USAID will receive the above recommendations to review and decide to support to participate in the development of Cambodia's agricultural sector.
