(Beijing): Investment in yellow bananas in Cambodia is very attractive, with many companies are now growing and exporting to international markets, especially China.
Confirmation of Investment Plan for Yellow Banana Plant in Cambodia was made during a meeting between Mr. Ngin Chhay, Royal Government of Cambodia Delegate, Director General of the General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, and Mr. Li Zhijun, Director General. Of the Department of Agriculture and Rural Affairs of Beijing, People's Republic of China on October 22, 2019.
Regarding CAG's investment plan, Mr. Ngin Chhay stated that this work is very appropriate and very important for Cambodia because the Cambodian agricultural sector has high potential.
In addition, this investment plan is in line with the policy of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Cambodia to promote modern agriculture, processing, packaging and export of Cambodian agricultural products with quality, safety and international standards.
According to the General Department of Agriculture, the meeting between the General Department of Agriculture of Cambodia and the Director General of the Department of Agriculture and Rural Affairs of Beijing has yielded fruitful results, including:
First, the two sides agreed to hold talks with Chinese officials who are on a mission in Cambodia to increase cooperation and exchange experiences.
Second, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Cambodia supports, encourages and will provide all possible cooperation with CAG to make the investment project a success for the benefit of the people and the two countries.
Third, the two sides agreed to exchange experiences and jointly examine agricultural techniques and seed production using modern techniques.
Fourth, to increase cooperation on crop protection, sanitation and phytosanitary to promote the production and export of quality and safe Cambodian agricultural products for domestic and international markets, especially China.
It should be noted that in the first nine months of 2019, Cambodia exported more than 110,000 tons of bananas to Vietnam, China and Japan.
