Cambodian National Defense Chief Samdech Tea Banh Raises Three Challenges at the 9th Shanghai Forum in Beijing
Addressing the Third Plenary Meeting on "Benefits of All Small, Medium and Common Countries" Concerned and find solutions together on those issues.
Through the 9th Sieng San Forum, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh raised three challenges to the meeting, including:
In reality, we see that sometimes great countries and superpowers can pursue their own national interests without much regard for international moral principles. In contrast, small and medium-sized countries cannot do that. When small and medium-sized countries try to do this, they are often hampered by international moral principles.
In fact, in the case of Cambodia itself, despite the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to do everything for the benefit of its people and nation, Cambodia is still under pressure from some countries to criticize human rights, freedom and democracy.
Finally, Samdech Pichey Sena stressed that in order to solve the challenges of small and medium countries directly to Cambodia, the Royal Government has announced the policy of "internal reform, increase international ties based on the principles of sovereignty and independence." "Based on this policy, Cambodia has been actively contributing to the building of the ASEAN community and international organizations such as the United Nations."
