Authorities urge the public to stop distributing previously bad images that could affect Angkor's tourist destinations
(Siem Reap): The APSARA Authority urges the public, especially the Cambodian people themselves, to stop distributing bad images in the past that could affect tourist destinations at the Angkor Cultural Tourism Resort. Authorities, relevant ministries and institutions have been resolving it gradually.
APSARA Authority closely cooperates with national and international institutions in the goal of conservation and sustainable development of Angkor Resort by organizing the development, management, restoration and preservation of this World Heritage Site from the dangerous heritage to become a tourist destination. One of the largest in the world and ranked number one as a recurring tourist destination in the past year.
Through the conservation of heritage and cultural tourism, Angkor has contributed significantly to the national economic development and has provided great benefits, both direct and indirect, for the economic development of the family, especially the promotion of Khmer culture to the world.
But in the past, there has been the dissemination and distribution of obscure images of the Angkor resort area on social media, which are contrary to what the APSARA Authority is currently doing.
In addition, the dissemination and distribution of images contrary to the current situation can cause tourists to be confused and think badly in deciding to choose to visit Cambodia and Angkor.
In this regard, Mr. Long Kosal, Spokesman of APSARA Authority, stated that APSARA Authority, in addition to repairing and preserving the temple, pays daily attention to promoting green environment in the Angkor area through landscaping. Weeding, planting luxury trees, preventing vendors on the grassy fields of Angkor Wat, parking arrangements, bike lanes, road construction and maintenance in Angkor Park, etc.
These activities are aimed at serving the tourism service and promoting the Angkor resort area to be more beautiful and attract more tourists to visit.
Mr. Long Kosal also stated that the use of images that do not reflect the current reality is not a good thing. Therefore, the public is asked to use images and content that reflect the actual progress of the Angkor resort area, especially the activities that the APSARA Authority is currently doing, such as parking, planting grass, planting flowers, planting trees, etc. To attract more tourists to visit the Angkor resort area is increasing.
Together, eliminate and disseminate non-current images about the Angkor resort area to inspire and disseminate good images and beauty of the Angkor resort area to contribute to the development of tourism.
