This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presents Diplomas to Over 4,000 Build Bright University Students
The graduation ceremony for students to testify to the success of their studies will be held solemnly under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on Tuesday. S2563 is on October 22, 2019 at Koh Pich Center.
4,038 students (1,344 females) who successfully graduated in the 2015-2016 school year to the 2018-2019 academic year, including associate degree, bachelor's degree, master's degree and doctoral degree. The students who received this degree were 169 students of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and 62 women.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the leader who gave the highest value to education. The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia always takes the opportunity to fulfill the busy duties for the nation to award degrees and give advice to graduates.
Mr. Diep Seiha, Rector of Build Bright University, summoned the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to preside over the graduation ceremony as a high-level honor with deepest meaning to the students as well as the University.
Build Bright University is a university that has built a reputation on this path of education for about two decades. For the past two decades, the University has been actively involved in cultivating human resources to be capital and a foundation in building Cambodian society.
Mr. Diep Seiha stated that the main mission that Build Bright University has fulfilled in the past 20 years is to expand the scope of higher education services, training and development of human resources to have skills, quality, efficiency and specific expertise in the essential direction. On capacity building, use critical thinking to participate in the preservation of national culture and socio-economic development of Cambodia with the international community.
According to the Rector, Build Bright University currently has a management team of 1,072 staff and professors. As of the 2018-2019 academic year, a total of 11,437 students are studying at all levels in Phnom Penh and provincial branches, including Siem Reap, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Stung Treng, Ratanakiri, Sihanoukville, and Takeo.
Mr. Diep Seiha asserted that the priority goal that Build Bright University is pursuing in the third phase of the University Development Strategic Plan (2016-2030) is that the success of students at all levels who have graduated from the University must have knowledge and ability. Thinking skills and creativity, thinking about leadership and being able to solve current and future challenges with good attitude.
To achieve this, curricula at all levels are regularly reviewed by the Curriculum Development Committee and the University Science Council to ensure consistency with the National Qualifications Framework, National Standards for Higher Education Accreditation and Quality. The results of the students respond to the current needs of the job market and many other businesses.
At the same time, the University has been strengthening cooperation on research and training activities with many national and international institutions in cooperation on research, communication, information, seminars, conferences, work visits, studies and cultural and sports activities, etc.
The Rector of Build Bright University affirmed that the fruitful achievements of Build Bright University are due to the efforts of the Board of Directors, Management, Faculty and Professors, with the active support of philanthropists, parents, students, organizations and institutions. And local authorities.
More importantly, this positive result is really due to the high level of attention and support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who have the Ministry Education, Youth and Sports and the Accreditation Committee of Cambodia as a staff.
