Traffic Police Officers in Preah Sihanouk Province Receive Training on Techniques to Improve Traffic Law on Driving Under the Influence of Alcohol
(Preah Sihanouk): On October 21, 2019, at the meeting hall of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hall, there was a refresher course on techniques to increase the efficiency of traffic law enforcement on driving under the influence of alcohol, traffic congestion rules and duties. Rescue victims for 2 days, from October 21 to 22, 2019.
The training was organized by the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police in collaboration with CaMSafe, with the support of Sihanoukville Provincial Hall through the support of APIWSA and partner members. Relevant around the province, a total of 60 people who participated in this course.
The same session will be held from October 23 to 24, 2019 at Sihanoukville Provincial Hall for 60 more traffic police officers and stakeholders to contribute to improving traffic safety and encourage road users. Everyone obeys traffic laws when traveling on the roads throughout Cambodia.
At the opening ceremony, Mr. Mang Sineth also thanked for the good cooperation between the partners in road safety, especially the National Police, who organized the training in accordance with the actual needs and needs of the province. Construction and repair of road structures in and around the city.
According to Thi Visal, Deputy Director of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the National Police, according to the report in 2018, there were 3,267 traffic accidents out of 3,531, a decrease of 7% compared to 2017.
