Mr. Khuong Sreng: The elderly are the bank and the storehouse of work experience
The capital governor said that the elderly were taken care of by the head of the Royal Government until there was a lot of support along with medical examination. The old people have explained the many merits to the motherland and contributed to the development and progress, which is a great achievement for the younger generation.
At the same time, the Governor of Phnom Penh asked the 105 Sangkat authorities throughout the Capital to take care of them, especially the members of the Association of the Elderly, which the Capital Administration has already established in each Sangkat.
"According to the 2018 statistics, there are 146,599 elderly people in Phnom Penh from the age of 60," said Ms. Mom Chandani, director of the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
She said that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has made it a priority for the Phnom Penh Municipal Social Affairs Officer, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation to include the program and the management of the Association of the Elderly in the meeting program of the Phnom Penh Capital Council so that the Sangkat in Phnom Penh can continue to implement, compile, strengthen and expand to help its members. The association currently has a total of 19,843 members, including 11,545 women.
Mr. Hun Manet Inaugurates New Branch of Vattanac Bank in Kampong Cham
(Kampong Cham): Lieutenant General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Land Forces, presides over here this morning the inauguration ceremony of the 15th branch of Vattanac Bank at Kampong Cham branch.
The new branch is located in the center of Kampong Cham town, with a 14-storey building and a large courtyard along Monivong Blvd., Kampong Cham city, Kampong Cham province. This new branch will provide all kinds of banking services to you, Mr. Oknha, Ladies and Gentlemen, who are customers or traders living in Kampong Cham province, especially Vattanac Bank, can provide all kinds of tax payment services more easily and quickly.
Mrs. Soy Sunnary, Branch Manager and Ms. Hor Thida, Branch Vice President are all residents of Kampong Cham Province who are in charge of the branch's daily banking operations.
Please be informed that Vattanac Bank is a bank with pure local shareholders established in 2002. The Bank is headquartered on the 2nd floor of Vattanac Capital in Phnom Penh. Vattanac Bank offers all kinds of commercial banking services with branches in Phnom Penh and in the provinces of Siem Reap, Battambang, Kampong Speu, Pursat, Takeo and Kampong Cham, the 15th new branch opened today.
Vattanac Bank has gained the trust and confidence of customers with continuous progress and has gained a good reputation for providing excellent customer service and good corporate governance through the recognition of national and international institutions during the period. Its operations for many years. Cambodian officials ask Chinese media to help promote Cambodian tourism
(KUYLIN): Dr. Sok Sokretya, Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of Tourism, requested the Chinese media, including social media such as WeChat, to help spread the word about Cambodia's tourism sector in order to help attract Chinese tourists to Cambodia.
During the discussion, Mr. Sokretya informed about the joint leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which brought about social progress and high economic growth.
Mr. Sok Sokretya also highlighted the potential and investment opportunities of Cambodia, which has a strong advantage in the region due to political stability, macroeconomic stability, etc. In addition, Cambodia has kept its annual inflation growth at a record low.
It should be noted that Mr. Sok Sokretya, Representative of the Minister of Tourism, has been leading officials of the Ministry of Tourism and a number of private companies to participate in the China-ASEAN International Tourism Expo 2019, which will be held in Kulin, China from the 18th to October 20, 2019.
Through this event, Mr. Sok Sokretya sought to promote Cambodia's tourism sector and also sought additional investment from the private sector to invest in tourism in Cambodia. Preah Sihanouk provincial forces arrest a drug lord and confiscate 27 packages of drugs in Prey Nob district
(Preah Sihanouk): Prey Nup District Police Force under the command of Mr. Chuon Narin, Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner launched an operation to crack down on a suspect along with 27 packages of drugs in Cheung Ko village, Prey Nup District, Preah Sihanouk Province in the afternoon. This October 21, 2019.
Prey Nup District Police Chief confirmed that the suspect, a drug trafficking mastermind, had been arrested by district police under the direction of Major Chuon Narin. Exhibits include: 27 packs of gram powder (8 small packs, 19 large packs), a scale and a number of mobile phones.
Currently, the suspect and some exhibits have been temporarily detained by the district police force at the Prey Nup District Police Inspectorate. Legal procedures.
Svay Rieng Police Detain 7 Suspects in Bavet City
(Svay Rieng): Authorities in Svay Rieng province launched a crackdown and drug control operation, detaining seven suspects, including three suspects, who were actively involved in local burglary on October 20, 2019 yesterday. Located in Tapip Village, Sangkat Bavet, Bavet City, Svay Rieng Province.
Exhibits include 49 drugs, 2 mobile phones for some drug use.
All seven suspects, along with exhibits, are currently being held at the Bavet Administrative Police Station for questioning and to build a case for legal action.
