Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Inspects River Bank Landslide in Kampong Siem District Affecting People's Homes and Bridges
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the afternoon of October 21, 2019, led a professional officer to inspect the landslide situation in the river area of Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province, which affected people's houses. And a bridge as well.
After inspecting the river bank in Ta Meang village, Koh Rokar commune, the provincial governor continued to lead the relevant department officials to inspect the condition of Kien Chrey bridge which is facing the impact of landslide and to visit the families of the people who are Faced with the impact of more than 10 families to be demolished on both sides of the Kien Chrey canal in Kien Chrey commune, Kampong Siem district.
On that occasion, the provincial governor told people to be more careful when crossing the bridge, and heavy vehicles, please drive around to avoid accidents.
The provincial governor said that if the people who face and have to dismantle their homes can ask the authorities to intervene at any time. Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Graduation Ceremony for Over 4,000 Students from Build Bright University (BBU)
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 22, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the graduation ceremony of more than 4,000 students from Build Bright University (BBU). Successfully, after overcoming many years of difficulties on the way of this study. The graduation ceremony took place at the Koh Pich Center.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was happy to be invited to distribute diplomas again to Build Bright University students.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers today's graduates as another new achievement for Cambodian society.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he still remembers the hardships of the youth of the past who lost their educational opportunities due to the flames of war.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia's education sector resumed in 1979 with the most difficult situation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that both the public and private sectors today need well-educated human resources.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech had just rejected the request of the Ministry of Health to request a health examination of candidates before the entrance exam.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers the request of the Ministry of Health to check the health of candidates before the civil service examination is to create a way to earn money from candidates.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that on Friday, October 25, the Council of Ministers will pass a budget law.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that as long as the CPP is in control of the Royal Government, it will not levy taxes on farmers' farmland and the minimum wage tax.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the national budget for education and the Ministry of Health will be increased every year to strengthen the education and health sector.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech is very proud of the progress in the field of education in Cambodia as well as universities.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the new academic year, Samdech received up to 3,707 scholarships from various universities.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed the expectation that today's graduates will strive to develop their capacity to respond to the development of society.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia needs to buy 450 vehicles to serve the Asia-Europe Meeting in 2020.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that both France, Germany and the international community have shown commitment to doing business with Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that tomorrow he will meet with the Japanese and German ambassadors in the morning and the new US ambassador in the afternoon.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen tells the opposition to recognize their abilities. Friendly countries work with the Royal Government, not with groups other than the Royal Government.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Paris Agreement of October 23, 1991 ended after the presence of UNTAC in Cambodia and the Constituent Assembly became the National Assembly.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reaffirmed that the Royal Water Festival is still held normally, even though the river in front of the Royal Palace is low.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call for Ok Ambok on November 9, National Independence Day and the Khmer Army's birthday. Samdech Techo Hun Sen called this eating ambok eating the national ambiguity, religion and the King.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the Governor of Phnom Penh to gather young people to clean up garbage during the Royal Water Festival.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cintri alone could not effectively collect garbage in Phnom Penh. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that there must be at least three companies operating to collect garbage in Phnom Penh.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the revocation of Cintri's garbage collection rights and puts it up for auction again, but there must be at least three companies.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen suggested to study the construction of public parking lots in parks to facilitate parking.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that if people eat and do not throw open fields, it will not make garbage.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that people must know how to protect their capital Phnom Penh by keeping garbage properly.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the law enforcement forces have already received orders for traitors to enter Cambodia and be handcuffed.
