(China): Seeing that the market for Cambodian agricultural products in China is huge, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Veng Sakhon has tried to capture the market of the world's second largest economy by assigning Officials meet with Chinese officials to accelerate and expand cooperation on Cambodia's agricultural exports to China.
Minister Veng Sakhon said that during the meeting, Cambodian officials achieved some important results, such as:
First, the Chinese side agreed to encourage and expedite the examination of documents provided by the Cambodian side before reaching the approval of the second Cambodian rice mill registration in the near future.
Second, the two sides will cooperate in coordinating and implementing the procedures on hygiene and phytosanitary requirements on Cambodian spice and pepper at the same time.
Third, in relation to mangoes, the Chinese side has examined the risk analysis documents, the contaminants and will send experts to finalize the evaluation of mango farms in Cambodia in November, with plans to sign a protocol on sanitary and phytosanitary requirements. Sanitation for fresh mango exports to China in early 2020.
Fourth, the Chinese side has been reviewing the documents related to the request to export longan from Cambodia to China and plans to send experts to review the required procedures and techniques.
Fifth, the Chinese side agreed in principle to provide four more Cambodian yellow banana farms to export fresh bananas directly to China. What should be proud of is that to date, there are nine Cambodian yellow banana plantations that have received the principle of direct export to China, with a total area of about 10,000 hectares.
