The following is the announcement of Phnom Penh Capital Administration: The Ministry of Justice announces the official election results for the election of members of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Justice on October 21, 2019 issued a press release on the official election results for the election of members of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy.
According to the announcement received by Fresh News on the evening of October 21, 2019, the candidates elected as members of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy in the election on October 19 and 20, 2019. For the election of members of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy are as follows:
First, Mr. Chay Chandaravan is a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy, elected by the Judges of the High Court.
Second: Mr. Seng Bun Kheang is a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy, appointed by the Prosecutor of the Supreme Prosecutor's Office and the Prosecutor of the Ministry of Justice.
Third: Mr. Iv Borin is a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy, elected by full judges of the courts throughout the country.
And 4: Mr. Srea Rattanak is a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy, appointed by the full prosecutor of the Prosecutor's Office throughout the country.
