Tbong Khmum Governor Instructs the Chamber of Commerce to Unite to Attract Large Investors to Invest in the Province
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan made this remark on October 21, 2019 at the meeting hall (a) of Tbong Khmum Provincial Hall on the occasion of meeting with Tbong Khmum Provincial Chamber of Commerce with Mr. Oknha Sok Heang Chairman.
On that occasion, Mr. Cheam Chansophoan pointed out that the GDP of the people has increased significantly compared to the GDP of the whole country, with the population throughout the province increasing to nearly 900,000 and about 500 companies and enterprises.
He added that especially the trade volume situation in the province, which provides a lot of convenience for traffic, because Tbong Khmum province borders neighboring countries, there are up to seven major ports, which makes rapid economic growth in line with the situation of this province. It is also full of high potential in agriculture and agro-industry.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan emphasized that this rapid growth in Tbong Khmum province as well as throughout the country is clear because the country is peaceful under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, only local investors and large foreign companies dare to invest. Keep doing business in Cambodia that we have all seen in the past as well as today.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan added that although the Tbong Khmum Chamber of Commerce has just been established, it is not young under the leadership of Mr. Oknha Sok Heang, who has been the President of the Kampong Cham Chamber of Commerce for many terms. Congratulations to the tycoon who resigned from Kampong Cham to run and be the President of Tbong Khmum Chamber of Commerce now.
