(Phnom Penh): Currently, MFIs are constantly evolving, which is due to the success of customers, which means that without the success of customers, MFIs will not succeed. No. This was confirmed by Mr. Kea Boran, Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Microfinance Association (CMA).
Mr. Kea Boran said that in order to promote this sector even better, the Cambodian Microfinance Association has set two goals, including:
1: Providing credit to people who have not yet received this financial service from official institutions.
2: How to make customers grow to help the microfinance sector to be better, because microfinance institutions can be successful only if customers are equally successful.
Mr. Kea Boran made this remark on the occasion of his participation in the program "Rural Economic Development through the Microfinance Sector" organized by Mr. Heng Bo Makara, Deputy Director General of the National Bank. Of Cambodia on October 21, 2019.
He said that microfinance institutions began to grow strongly during 2006, but in 2009-2010, Cambodia experienced the global economic crisis, slowed down for a while, but grew back at the end of 2010.
He said that today is the third phase and the sector is growing rapidly and so far more than 2.1 million households have received loans from the Cambodian microfinance sector (microfinance institutions. Finance under CMA) licensed by the National Bank of Cambodia to provide loans to rural areas.
He added that this growth can be said to be a success factor for all of us and recognized as a success of customers because customers get credit to use to increase business and profit for their families.
Mr. Heng Bo Makara also said that the contribution of microfinance institutions is very important in improving the lives of the people of Cambodia and has contributed significantly to the financial drive in Cambodia to achieve development. Economy.
He added that with this growth, there are also some challenges, including: the provision of services does not meet the needs of customers, the provision of services unprofessional, customer fraud, and for some establishments do not disclose service fees. And all conditions to the customer.
He said that in order to solve these problems, the National Bank of Cambodia has introduced a number of measures through regulations in order to provide information, protect the rights and interests of customers, as well as encourage the public on the banking system.
