Minister Vong Soth: Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Must Be Good Guides and role models to represent Cambodia in order to preserve national honor, values and culture
Mr. Vong Soth's remarks were made on October 21, 2019, allowing the delegation of the Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship Association to pay a courtesy call at the Ministry of Social Affairs before leaving for the Asian Youth Ship Program. The 46th Southeast Asia and Japan is coming soon.
On that occasion, Ms. Sun Mallika, President of the Cambodian Youth Group of the 46th Southeast Asia Cambodia and Japan Youth Ship Program, informed that the 46th Southeast Asia and Japan Youth Ship Program 2019 was organized for the main purpose. The four are to strengthen friendship, solidarity and deep understanding between Japan and ASEAN.
Ms. Sun Mallika said that this program is also to expand the knowledge and vision of young people and the world, cultivate the spirit and practical skills of international cooperation, encourage and encourage young people who have the ability to use their leadership potential in Various sectors to help develop society, especially in youth development. This program will run for 52 days, from October 24 to December 13, 2019.
The 29 Cambodian youth delegates nominated by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports will join a total of 335 ASEAN and Japanese youth delegates to start and participate in the program in Japan for 10 days, then sail on the NIPPON MARU. To participate in programs in four other ASEAN countries, including Vietnam, Singapore, Myanmar and Malaysia.
She added that during the program, the youth delegates will participate in a wide range of activities, including discussions on various topics related to the area, art and culture performances, accommodation with parents, study visits and courtesy calls with the leadership. Depending on the country where the ship docked.
In addition, Minister Vong Soth congratulated the children for the precious opportunity to participate in the upcoming 46th Southeast Asia and Japan Youth Ship Program. At the same time, he praised and appreciated the achievements and achievements of the association, especially the contribution to enhance the national prestige on the international stage, as well as the training of youth resources as future successors.
He hopes that the children will continue to strengthen and expand this success even better, especially to continue to strengthen and expand friendly relations and mutual understanding between ASEAN youth and with Japan.
