Phnom Penh and Baria-Vong Tao, Vietnam promote tourism integration
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, has promoted the connection of tourism between Phnom Penh and Baria-Vong Tao Province, Vietnam to attract more tourists from both countries to visit each other.
The Governor of Phnom Penh wants to connect the bus transportation sector from Phnom Penh to Baria-Vong Tao Province of Vietnam or from Baria-Vong Kao Province to Phnom Penh for your convenience. Tourists from both countries visited the main tourist destinations in Phnom Penh and Baria-Vong Tao.
Mr. Khuong Sreng made the remarks at a reception for a Vietnamese delegation led by Mr. Nguyen Hong Linh, Member of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam and Chairman of the Bari-Vong Tao Provincial People's Council of Vietnam on the morning of October 21. 2019 to discuss cooperation projects in various fields for the benefit of people on both sides.
The Governor of Phnom Penh affirmed that the project to connect tourism between the provincial capitals of the two countries will be a new product package to attract tourists, while Phnom Penh and Baria-Vong Tao of Vietnam are rich in natural and historical tourist sites. Same. He said that now, under more than 7 percent of the economy for more than two decades, Cambodians live in a civilized way to travel, both at home and abroad.
"While Bari-Wong Tao of Vietnam and Phnom Penh are rich in tourist destinations, we must change the tourism sector, especially the direct bus service from Phnom Penh to Bari-Vong Tao," he said. From Baria-Vong Tao to Phnom Penh. "In addition, the exchange of investment in tourism, which makes it easier for the people of the two countries to travel to each other."
Nguyen Hong Linh, Member of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam and Chairman of the Bari-Vong Tao Provincial People's Council of Vietnam, supported the plan to expand tourism cooperation to attract more tourists. .
