Pursuant to Article 568 of the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, a concession refers to a contract which shall be entered into by one party expressing its intention to give the other party the property free of charge and the other party agrees to accept it.
According to the above definition, a gift is created with the consent of the giver, called the donor, and the recipient, called the recipient.
Donations can be made orally or in writing, and the subject of the gift contract may be in the form of money, but for immovable property, the gift will only be legally valid if it is authentic.
According to the law, donations are divided into three types: gifts with a fixed schedule, gifts with a burden and gifts with a cause of death:
A. Time-limited gift: is a gift made for the purpose of giving a talisman for a certain period of time and will lose its power when the patriarch or devotee dies.
B. Bonded Giving: A gift in which the beneficiary is obligated to perform a fixed gift to receive the property that is the subject of the gift is called a binding gift. For the father of the dependent gift can dissolve the contract of gift attached in case the donor does not carry the burden.
C. Donation for the cause of death: This gift will take effect after the grandfather dies.
Reasons for cancellation of gift:
A. Cancellation of an unwritten gift: The parties to the contract can cancel the gift agreement if the contract is not made in writing. But for parts that have already been applied, it cannot be undone.
B. Cancellation of a gift due to a breach of trust: A grandparent can cancel a gift within 5 years if the grandchild finds out that the host has committed a serious breach of trust.
C. Cancellation of a gift due to the poverty of the child: The child can cancel the gift that has been applied for 5 years from the time of implementation if the child falls into a state of poverty and can not maintain the livelihood of the child. The body itself.
In general, we can conclude that a gift contract is a voluntary act of handing over one's property or property to the other party in connection with the liability or death of the other party.
However, the gift can still be modified when the gift contract has not been made in writing and the part has not yet occurred, but for the part that has been implemented and the father can also claim back in case of violation. The serious confidence and poverty of the grandparents that the claim can be made within 5 years.
