The General Assembly of the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund is held annually to provide an opportunity for the leaders of the Ministries of Finance and the Central Bank of member countries to be aware of the achievements, challenges and priority goals of the World Bank and International Monetary Fund.
The Governor and the delegation also attended the 52nd Asia-Pacific Group Meeting, which discussed the regional economic situation, challenges and policies, and the work plan of the Asia-Pacific Group of Representatives at the IMF to protect the interests and voice of the country. Member in IMF decisions.
The National Bank of Cambodia delegation also met with the chair and leaders of the Asia-Pacific Department and the International Monetary Fund's Department of Capital and Monetary Markets to discuss the economic situation in Cambodia and the need for technical assistance from the IMF.
It should be noted that in the past, the IMF has always provided technical assistance to Cambodia, especially the National Bank of Cambodia to strengthen the capacity of human resources and institutions.
The meeting aims to provide an opportunity for ASEAN member states to present challenges in the current economic environment and needs to the IMF.
The Governor briefed the meeting on the growth and major challenges of the Cambodian economy and thanked the IMF for its past contribution to the achievements of Cambodia through the performance of its duties, especially in monitoring, evaluating and making recommendations. Good to support the implementation of economic and financial policies of the Royal Government and the National Bank of Cambodia.
On that occasion, the Governor-General signed a Memorandum of Understanding on the Swap Mechanism for 2019-2021 within the ASEAN framework. This Memorandum of Understanding has been signed every two years since 2005 with the aim of establishing an agreement to help provide mutual liquidity among ASEAN member countries for strengthening the ASEAN financial security network.
