Some resort owners in Kampot province claim to tell the tourism minister that they will be ready before the sea festival
(Kampot): The owners of some important resorts in Kampot province have confirmed to Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism that they will try to organize other related work in the resort to be ready to receive tourists before the Sea Festival. By the end of next year.
The direct visit to the resort took place on October 19, 2019, in which Minister Thong Khon and officials arrived at the tourist resort "Dong Prek Park" in Bot Kbal Damrey village, Mak Prang commune, Teuk Chhou district and Continue to "Doung Ter" resort, "Koh Tada" natural tourism resort and "Teuk Chhou" natural tourism resort, all located in Snom Prampi village, Mak Prang commune, Teuk Chhou district.
During the direct inspection, Mr. Thong Khon saw some problems such as garbage, water storage and sanitation problems, in which he advised the owners of the resort, especially the Department of Tourism to participate in the improvement.
The Minister assessed that the organization and reception at those resorts are much better, but please pay attention to the problem of garbage scattered in some of the resort grounds. At this point, the Minister also praised the organization of the reception and cleaning at the resort of Dong Ter and Dong Prek Park.
He further advised the owners and supervisors at the resorts to pay more attention to hygiene, food, environment, security, order and to strengthen the quality of special services, do not increase the service fee too much when the sea festival arrives.
In addition, he checked the problem of watering and some other sanitation problems, but also not too serious, as the access road to those resorts is easily accessible, especially in those places is true It has a beautiful view of the waterfall, which is a resort for all tourists.
It is also a feature for the four main tourist resorts above, as it is located next to each other on the same road, which allows tourists to travel to visit and not far from each other.
Please be informed that the 8th Sea Festival (Round 2) in Kampot will be held from December 20-22, which is why Minister Thong Khon strongly urges the Provincial Department of Tourism. Kampot, as well as the owners of each resort, must be ready before this big tourist event arrives.
