CDX cooperates with the Securities and Exchange Commission and the state of Berlin to share knowledge on derivatives trading
(Pailin): The Cambodian Derivatives Exchange (CDX) Co., Ltd., in collaboration with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and the Pailin Provincial Administration, organized a seminar to share knowledge on derivatives trading to the public in Pailin Province.
This workshop is the sixth goal of the provincial seminar in 2019 organized by Cambodian Derivatives Exchange Company, Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and Pailin Provincial Administration, held on October 19, 2019.
The workshop in Pailin is the sixth goal in 2019 and will be organized with the participation of Mr. Chea Balika, Deputy Director of the Securities and Exchange Commission of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, Mr. Un Bunly, Director of Administration of Pailin Provincial Administration and Mr. Lawrence Kook. Governor of Cambodian Derivatives Exchange. The workshop was organized under the theme "What is Derivatives Trading: Investment Preparation and Relevant Awareness?"
These provincial workshops aim to share knowledge, skills, experience, regulations and investment opportunities to the public throughout Cambodia.
Mr. Un Bunly introduced the participants to the development work on derivatives market, which is also an important part of the financial market development policy.
He added that this understanding is very useful for trainees to expand their knowledge as well as reduce the risk level of investing in this financial instrument. He encouraged all participants to pay attention to learn more about new techniques and experiences related to trading in the derivatives market.
Mr. Chea Balika gave the opening remarks of the 2019 Provincial Workshop in Pailin and confirmed the direction of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia in expanding the development of derivatives market in Cambodia. He also encouraged investors to increase their knowledge and be ready to invest in derivatives while efforts to protect investors are ongoing.
"A number of relevant regulations have been put in place to ensure order, efficiency and transparency in the market," he said. "As an authority, we must not forget about investor protection. One of the most important mechanisms of investor protection is cash security."
He added that up to now, Cambodian Derivatives Exchange and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia have cooperated with the provincial administration in organizing workshops in 11 provinces, including Sihanoukville, Kampong Cham and Siem Reap. Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Takeo, Kampot, Kep, Kampong Chhnang, Pursat and Pailin provinces.
