(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, Ministry of Economy and Finance, said that the achievement of innovative and sustainable tax revenue growth depends on the implementation of administrative and fiscal reforms. Modernize the tax system, especially the new measures of the General Department of Taxation.
He said that combined with these new measures, in the first nine months of 2019, the management of revenue collection of all types of taxes and duties achieved more than 95.42% of the annual plan.
Mr. Kong Vibol made this statement during a meeting to review the results of tax collection for September and for the first nine months of 2019, as well as the direction for further implementation with the participation of Mr. Chou Vichit, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. Objects on October 17, 2019.
Mr. Kong Vibol stated that the new measures of the General Department of Taxation include:
Adherence to the proactive spirit, continue to strive to enforce the law effectively and gently, based on the legal aspects of providing services to taxpayers and revenue collection management, in particular to ensure consistency, accuracy and Accuracy, justice.
Strengthening the strict implementation of measures to investigate tax offenses to prevent all forms of tax evasion.
He pointed out that the tax revenue in September 2019 was about 232.06 million US dollars, a new record for the General Department of Taxation, because September used to be the month to collect low tax revenue in the year. Previously.
Mr. Chou Vichit also praised and provided valuable comments on the achievements of the General Department of Taxation in September and the first nine months of 2019, especially in a context where there is no new tax, no tax rate increase, only strengthening Apply the laws and regulations in force.
