(Pursat): Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on Saturday On October 19, 2019, World Food Day was celebrated under the theme "Together we promote food safety and nutrition to reduce hunger to zero for our future".
Mr. Mao Thunin informed the ceremony about the status of development process in all sectors, especially agriculture in Pursat province, which has the potential to invest to increase productivity, ensure safety, nutrition and reduce hunger in line with the theme of the day. This.
Francesca Erdelmann reports to the event that this is the 39th anniversary of World Food Day and that this day is a United Nations global event that the world is holding to raise awareness and Recognize the important role of the agricultural sector in addressing food security, food security issues that all stakeholders must be willing to actively participate in leading to the end of global hunger.
Alexandre HUYNH stated that eradicating hunger is a top priority of the FAO and also called on all stakeholders, including producers, consumers, government, the private sector and research institutions to increase sustainable activities in a collaborative manner. Being a partner is the most important key to making the above topics a success.
He said the FAO will continue to support all activities to contribute to food safety and nutrition for human beings in all member countries, including Cambodia.
Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his gratitude for the presence of national and international guests and citizens who participated in this day and highly appreciated the efforts of all relevant partners who have worked together to make this day meaningful and fruitful. Should be proud.
Understanding the above issues, the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, has given top priority to food security and nutrition and considers investment in this sector as a "catalyst" to help accelerate Achieve the goal of sustainable development and well-being of the people, help develop human capital and the national economy.
He added that in order to achieve the goal of eradicating hunger by 2030, sustainable development is needed to ensure food security, improve nutrition, and promote agricultural development in accordance with the National Action Plan 2016-2025. Initiatives to reduce hunger to zero in Cambodia as expected.
The Minister recalled Samdech Techo's remarks that "solutions related to food security and nutrition are not only in response to the priority policies of the Royal Government that have been set in the past, but also have contributed significantly to Reduce poverty, solve hardships, improve living standards and improve well-being. "And the Royal Government is committed not to let any people die of starvation.
