Samdech Picheay Sena: World military sports have played an important role in finding and ensuring regional and global peace and stability
(China): Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Minister of Defense, confirmed that the World Military Games has really played an important role in finding and ensuring peace and stability in the region and the world.
This confirmation was made by Samdech Picheay Sena on the occasion of Samdech led a delegation of the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia to pay an official and friendly visit to the People's Republic of China from October 17 to 23, 2019 at the invitation of Chinese Minister of Defense
Samdech Picheay Sena stated that under the theme, sports bring peace, sport brings friendship and is an important element in cultivating the spirit of love for peace in the field of education in the army and an open platform for all armies in the world. Opportunity to communicate, understand each other, contribute to strengthening and expanding friendship and cooperation under the umbrella of peacekeeping missions of great value in human history.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh expressed his strong hope and belief that by participating in the 7th World Military Games, this will be a great opportunity for delegates from all countries to learn. Discover more about the experience as well as new knowledge in organizing major world-class sporting events such as current events.
During the meeting, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, on behalf of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and leaders in the field of defense, congratulated the success of the 7th World Military Games in Wuhan, People's Republic of China. With great significance for the history of mankind and all the armies of the universe.
It should be noted that upon arriving in Wuhan, Hubei Province, People's Republic of China on the occasion of attending the opening ceremony of the 7th World Military Games in Wuhan on the afternoon of October 18, 2019, Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh with leaders Defense agencies from other countries paid a courtesy call on Xi Jinping, General Secretary of the Communist Party of China, President of the People's Republic of China and Chairman of the Central Military Commission.
"Today we gathered for the 7th World Military Event in Wuhan, attended by more than 10,000 troops from more than 100 countries," said President Xi Jinping.
