Kampot Provincial Court Detains 3 Men Who Rape French Woman in Kampot City
Please be informed that two more perpetrators involved in the rape of a French woman in Kampot City, Kampot Province were arrested by Kampot Provincial Police on the afternoon of October 16, 2019 after fleeing Hiding on Bokor Mountain.
Kampot Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Mao Chanthurith, who led the operation directly to Bokor Mountain, told Fresh News that after the arrest of a member of the gang on the evening of October 15 in cooperation with the Prey Nup District Police Force. He confessed and gave additional clues to the other two factions who escaped, so the force used professional measures to arrest them.
The three suspects were identified as:
* First: Seng Srun, 37 years old, resident of Boeung Veng Village, Veal Rinh Commune, Prey Nob District, Preah Sihanouk Province, Occupation: Taxi driver, was arrested yesterday Bor Seth, Kampong Speu Province: Occupation: Water Worker on Bokor Mountain * Third: Name: Nget Naphea, 23 years old, living in Trapeang Leuk Village, Kraing Sbov Commune, Chhuk District, Kampot Province. Occupation: Water Worker on Bokor Mountain.
Please be informed that at 4:00 AM on October 11, 2019, a 43-year-old French woman was forced into a car by three people and raped (in the car) on the concrete road and then entered. Into a quiet forest around the beach at the mouth of the Kampot canal, Kampot city. The assailants then dropped the victim on the back and escaped.
