(Phnom Penh): The Embassy of Japan in Cambodia has decided to select 6 groups of Cambodian youths to perform "My Hometown in Japan", a total of 24 people to compete and show their ability to sing and dance under the theme "My Hometown" with young people ASEAN in Japan in early 2020.
The decision to select Cambodian youth to perform in this film was made on October 17, 2019 yesterday, on the occasion that the Embassy of Japan organized the final competition to select Cambodian candidates to participate in the Jeneseys Youth Exchange 2019.
He said that in this competition, the committee finally decided to select 6 outstanding teams, a total of 24 candidates to participate in the competition and show their ability to dance, sing and perform in Japan with young candidates from various countries. In ASEAN in late January, early 2020.
According to Mr. Sutri, Deputy Director of the Youth Department of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, all the performances with singing, dancing and performances by all the candidates are all good, especially the performances that show the meaning. History and development of cultural and tourist sites in the localities of Cambodia.
Mr. Sutri said that for the best winners, the latest winners are the group with the most creative ideas, and the performance is attractive and well-coordinated.
