Calmette Hospital Holds Workshop on "Nutrition for Premature Babies"
(Phnom Penh): The theme "Nutrition for Premature Babies" was chosen in line with the current focus on infant health care, as well as strengthening the quality and ability of doctors to save infants. The first mission we have to do as well.
Professor Chheang Ra, Director General of Calmette Hospital, said this at the opening ceremony of the workshop on "Nutrition for Premature Babies" on October 18, 2019 at Calmette Hospital, which hosted the workshop. Third, the Cambodian Pediatric Association, in collaboration with a professor from KK Hospital, Singapore.
The topic of nutrition for premature infants and babies with abnormal birth weight is an important topic in contributing to reducing infant mortality has become a priority throughout Cambodia that the Royal Government has set and Working together is a necessity to help solve this problem better.
Professor Calmette Hospital Director General hopes that this workshop and the participation of doctors from major hospitals in Phnom Penh and from provinces across the country will contribute significantly to the development of knowledge in saving the baby. Timely in the first minute, called the golden minute.
At the same time, Prof. Dr. Im Sithikar, President of the Cambodian Pediatric Association and President of the Pediatrics Department of Calmette Hospital, considered that this is the third workshop of the Association, the first under the theme "Baby Rescue and Lift. Second, in early 2019 on "the use of ventilators on newborns."
The doctor stated that this technique requires specific experience in placement and requires close monitoring by the nurse during the baby's hospitalization.
Senior official of the National Anti-Drug Authority warns experts to encourage drug addicts to seek treatment and rehabilitation
(Siem Reap): Lt. Gen. Chey Bopha, Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, warns and urges medical professionals to work together to encourage drug users and addicts to receive treatment. And rehabilitation.
Lt. Gen. Chey Bopha said this on October 18, 2019 at the closing ceremony of the training course on management and governance on the treatment and rehabilitation of drug addicts in Cambodia, the 2019 LOA.
Dr. Sin Eap, Officer of the Ministry of Health, summed up the training course on Management and Governance on the treatment and rehabilitation of drug addicts, provided participants with increased knowledge leading to the strengthening of management and governance on the job. Treatment and rehabilitation of drug addicts in Cambodia.
Speaking on behalf of the trainees, Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, Deputy Commissioner and Permanent Deputy Chairman of the Secretariat of the Kandal Provincial Drug Control Committee, said that this training was very important. He suggested that such training be given later to improve the efficiency of drug rehabilitation in Cambodia.
At the end of the three-day training program, certificates were distributed to all participants.
