Ministry of Justice cooperates with Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court on "Roles and Duties of Implementing Institutions" and "Enforcement Procedures"
(Preah Sihanouk): The Ministry of Justice, in collaboration with the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court, organized a dissemination meeting on "Roles and Duties of Implementing Institutions" and "Enforcement Procedures".
According to the Code of Civil Procedure:
First, the role of the court in enforcing enforcement: the confiscation of immovable property, the confiscation of ships, the confiscation of debt rights and matters related to the issuance of protection orders.
Second, the role and duties of the bailiff in the enforcement of the rights and jurisdiction of the law are related to the procedure for confiscation of movable property, transfer of immovable property, immovable property and protection practices, such as: Provisional confiscation of movable property to Immovable property and the implementation of a protection order in any type of commission.
According to Mr. Sok Kalyan, President of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court, he thanked the delegation and the working group of the Ministry of Justice for their support and cooperation in spirit and technique with the court in organizing the above meeting.
