(Phnom Penh): The nationwide campaign against illegal drugs for October 18, 2019 showed that law enforcement forces cracked down on 25 cases of illegal drugs by detaining 52 suspects.
According to the report of the Third Commission of the Anti-Illegal Drug Campaign, the types of crimes include: 14 cases of trafficking, 31 arrests and 11 cases of use, 21 arrests.
According to the report, the results of the nationwide drug crackdown from January 1 to October 18, 2019 totaled 7,801 cases, detaining 16,487 people (1,123 females). (344 foreigners, 59 females with 12 nationalities). Ministry of Tourism Leads a Youth Group to Study Garbage Storage and Toilet Standards at Aeon Market 2
(Phnom Penh): On October 18, 2019, the Ministry of Tourism led a group of government officials, youths and students to visit Aeon Mall Sen Sok (Aeon 2) to find out the tips for storing garbage, standard public toilets and Some of the model work that this mall has been working on as well as to promote and inspire people to increase their participation in this necessary work even more.
This activity was conducted under the leadership of Mr. Hout Rithy, Director of the Department of Clean City Support and Promotion of the Ministry of Tourism, with the participation of civil servants of the Ministry of Tourism, youth groups from the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, representatives of Sen Sok District, Women's Organization For society, representing Aeon Mall 2 and some other students, a total of about 30 people.
Mr. Hout Rithy said that the purpose of the study visit at Aeon Mall Sen Sok is to learn about the management, management, storage of garbage, participation in environmental protection, public toilets, which this mall has been Work hard and also contribute to attracting customers to visit and shop in this mall.
Aeon Mall Sen Sok's representative said that now about 18 million people as well as customers have entered the second Aeon Mall.
They have a better understanding and spirit to take care of sanitation and garbage disposal, as they store garbage according to the market's guidelines, which are divided into solid waste and recyclable waste compartments. Their understanding also makes it easier for the market's cleaning staff to take the garbage to be stored or recycled.
He added that in order to join the Ministry of Tourism and the National Committee for the Evaluation of Clean Cities, as well as to inspire the public to participate in reducing waste problems, Aeon Market 1 and Aeon Market 2 are all teaching activities to shop staff in Both markets to properly dispose of garbage according to the division of the directory and have activities to collect garbage in public places around and outside the market on the 11th of every month every year.
Mr. Hout Rithy claimed that through his personal study visit, he saw that the garbage was properly stored and a good example for other places, especially the proper implementation of hygiene standards.
In addition, he inspected the toilets in the market and found that this supermarket complied with the public toilets, both national and ASEAN standards, as well as rooms for mothers and babies.
Mr. Hout Rithy stated that through the movement of the Clean City Competition, the supermarket also participated a lot in arranging public toilets in accordance with the standard, but at present, some entertainment places still do not have room for mothers and babies. The mother can still exchange items for the baby.
For this reason, he also called for the arrangement of rooms for mothers and babies to make it easier for mothers to exchange items for babies, while now observed in public places or places full of children. More than ever, which requires some planning for children and babies, especially the toilet.
Tbong Khmum CamControl Officers Continue to Strengthen Food Safety at Phsar Dar, Met District by Checking Iodine on Iodized Salt
(Tbong Khmum): On October 18, 2019, CamControl officers continued to inspect the food safety quality at Dar Market in Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province to inspect the quality of iodized salt and other food and beverage products.
During the inspection, CamControl officers used test kits to perform preliminary tests on salt labeled on iodine packaging, as well as physical inspections of food products on display, focusing on Content on the packaging label, such as product source, name and address, manufacturer, country code, manufacturer, product lot number, date of manufacture and expiration date.
Through the inspection conducted, the professional officers did not find any defective or defective goods due to the small size of the exhibitors, which was easy to manage and organize. Preliminary tests on iodized salt showed compliance with the declaration on the packaging.
Deputy General Commissioner of National Police asks all transport company owners to compete to obey traffic laws
(Phnom Penh): Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police, General Him Yan, has asked all freight and passenger company owners to compete in respecting traffic laws to set an example for transport companies in Cambodia to reduce fatalities. By accident.
General Him Yan stated that the disciplines that the owners of freight and passenger companies must compete and apply in accordance with the conditions include driver management and vehicle technology, legal education and traffic technical standards to drivers, Obey traffic laws and standards and reduce traffic accidents in its transportation services, in order to reduce the number of deaths and injuries.
(Kampot): On October 18, 2019, Dr. Ouk Saravuth, Deputy Auditor General of the National Audit Authority, opened a seminar to disseminate the law on audit and public audit standards to officials in Kampot province.
The ceremony was held at Kampot Diamond Hotel in Kampong Bay North Village, Sangkat Kampong Bay, Kampot City, Dr. Prohm Vichet Sophorn, Deputy Secretary General of the National Audit Authority and Mr. Chiao Tay, Governor of Kampot Province Districts, communes, sangkats and departments, units, public institutions in the province, a total of 125 people, the workshop lasted for one morning.
Mr. Chiao Tai considered that the current workshop is very important to provide more new knowledge to officials operating in public administration institutions in the province to make the review of operations and programs of public institutions transparent. On collecting revenue and implementing expenditures of the national budget, monitoring and reviewing the accuracy and appropriateness of financial statements, as well as strengthening the internal control system of public institutions.
On that occasion, Mr. Prohm Vichet Sophorn also made a presentation on the Audit Law and Public Audit Standards of the Kingdom of Cambodia, identifying four main points, including: 1: Background of Institutions, National Audit Authority, 2: Why there is a law on audit Of the Kingdom of Cambodia, 3rd: the content of the Audit Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia and 4: the standard of public audit of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Mr. Sar Sokha: The Royal Government considers higher education as an important sub-sector in the development of human capital in Cambodia
(Siem Reap): Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia considers higher education as an important sub-sector in the development of human capital to bring Cambodia to a middle-income country. High and developed countries in the future, with the long-term vision of the Royal Government and a clear strategy, with reforms to improve the quality of education with high quality and efficiency.
Mr. Sar Sokha made this remark on the morning of October 18, 2019, when he and Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, presided over the graduation ceremony for undergraduate and graduate students. Senior students and awarded certificates to 1,892 outstanding students at the University of South East Asia in Siem Reap.
Mr. Sar Sokha said that the successful graduation of students at the university now is to build quality human resources to meet the needs of the labor market and the country.
Mr. So Sokha stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has achieved the most glorious change. At the same time, it has become a country that strictly adheres to the principles of liberal democracy, pluralism, a country that upholds the rule of law, and is a sovereign state with complete independence and territorial integrity.
According to Mr. Sean Sovanna, Rector of the University of South East Asia and Director General of Future Bright International School, the private higher education institution was established in 2006 to provide competent and competent higher level human resources training. Good attitude responds to national and international labor markets so that they can work and live in an era of globalization and Buddhist society.
He said that in order to ensure the quality of education in response to the strategic plan of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the ASEAN Economic Integration, the university has clearly defined the vision and mission and developed the strategic plan for 2015. -2019 and the strategic plan for 2020-2025.
With high commitment, this university has a good reputation in the Kingdom of Cambodia and is recognized and supported by students and relevant national and international institutions. The university has trained nine generations of associate degree students, 13 generations of bachelors and 11 generations of master's degree students. At the same time, 1,892 students will be the winners today.
