(Phnom Penh): PRASAC, the largest financial institution in Cambodia, recently became a new member of Bakong System, a mobile payment application that allows customers to make interbank transactions and bill payments. Easy in Cambodia.
Initiated and managed by the National Bank of Cambodia, this Bakong project aims to promote a more efficient payment system and improve the financial environment in Cambodia.
Mr. Say Sony, President of PRASAC, stated, “PRASAC is honored and happy to be an integral part of the National Bank of Cambodia Bakong Project. This is a mobile payment application using Blockchain technology that will bring all payment service providers and financial institutions into one system in order to make it easier for users as well as facilitate daily cash management. "
He added, "Bakong is a payment service that allows customers to make interbank transactions and pay bills easily, quickly, securely and free of charge. Therefore, customers can enjoy using this service to transfer money, make deposits and receive money easily.
He also mentioned that Bakong is the first mobile app that combines e-wallet service, mobile payment, online banking and other financial services with the first easy-to-use functions. They will have the largest number of partner banks in Cambodia.
Say Sony also emphasized that this great payment program plays an important role in promoting environmental growth and poverty reduction, as well as being a vehicle for strong growth in the digital age.
He also stated that the Bakong project is one of the projects that PRASAC has cooperated with the National Bank of Cambodia to make payments more efficient, such as fast payment service and Cambodian Swiss.
