(Kampong Chhnang): Cambodian Derivatives Exchange Co., Ltd., in collaboration with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration, organized a workshop to share knowledge, skills, regulations and rich experience related to derivatives investment in Kampong Chhnang.
This workshop is the fourth goal of the provincial workshop in 2019 with the participation of Mr. Sok Dara, Deputy Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and Mr. Srun Samrithy, Deputy Governor of the Board of Governors of Kampong Chhnang Province. Representative of Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province.
The workshop was organized under the theme "What is Derivatives Trading: Investment Preparation and Relevant Awareness?" Provincial Workshop 2019 focuses on promoting and expanding the understanding of derivatives investment in Cambodia, the evolution of the derivatives market, increasing investor confidence and helping investors be ready to invest in derivatives. Which is the most popular financial product in the world.
Mr. Sok Dara, Deputy Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, highlighted the current state of the derivatives market in Cambodia, as well as the mission of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia in strengthening investor protection regulations and trading practices.
He also encouraged investors to increase their knowledge and development, as well as to select companies licensed by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to manage risk when investing. He also expressed his pleasure to cooperate with Cambodian Derivatives Exchange, a leading central counterpart and always active in promoting investment skills to the Cambodian public and raising Cambodia's profile on the international stage. .
Mr. Lawrence Kook is also committed to developing the derivatives market in Cambodia to be better by bringing the latest technology, smooth and transparent trading software, a wide range of trading products, effective investor protection principles, quality of Services, training, knowledge and skills, as well as presenting good investment opportunities and increasing the role in the market.
Mr. Srun Samrithy closed the seminar in Kampong Chhnang and thanked the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and Cambodian Derivatives Exchange for bringing investment-related workshops to the people of the province.
He reminded the trainees to invest only with the right companies and the right licenses to prevent risks.
It should be noted that at present, Cambodian Derivatives Exchange and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia have jointly organized workshops with provincial administrations in nine provinces, including: Sihanoukville, Kampong Cham, Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Takeo, Kampot and Kep. And Kampong Chhnang province.
