(Phnom Penh): Secretary of State for the Ministry of Health, Professor Ing Phirun, said that we have already prepared more than 500 inspectors to fine producers, traders and smokers in prohibited places. Public workplaces and other prohibited places at the end of 2019 after the Ministry has already visited and educated throughout the country.
This statement was made by Professor Ing Phirun at the National Workshop on Tobacco Control under the theme "Do not let tobacco poison your breath" which took place on October 17, 2019 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Professor Ing Phirun continued, "In order to be healthy, do not let tobacco poison your breath, we must all people dare to talk to smokers to stay away from us and tell. "Danger to the health of smoking and cigarette smoke from others."
He called on restaurant owners, hotel owners and business owners to "join in banning smokers to ensure that there is no tobacco pollution in your customers, and that no smoking signs be put up at the entrance." "Entrance and exit, which makes it easy for the public to see clearly and do not have to display plates or containers knocking cigarettes, otherwise the inspectors will be fined 50,000 riel per case and smokers 20,000 riel."
"Tobacco is a public health problem that hinders sustainable development," said Dr. Chhea Chadaphea, director of the National Center for Health Promotion at the Ministry of Health. "Consumption of tobacco products causes premature death, leading to non-communicable diseases, including cancer, chronic respiratory disease and cardiovascular disease."
"The World Health Organization (WHO) estimates that tobacco kills nearly 8 million people a year and that 1.2 million smokers smoke about 1.4 million dollars a year," she said. Trillion dollars. "Cambodia has about 2 million users of tobacco products, of which 1.7 million are smokers, which causes a loss of about $ 201,534,701 per year."
The Ministry of Health, under the direct supervision of Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, has taken care to protect public health by urging laws and regulations related to tobacco control to educate the public about the effects. Of tobacco products, promote counseling, quit smoking and encourage the participation of stakeholders and the public in the implementation of the law on tobacco control.
The Royal Government also issued Sub-Decree No. 43, dated March 16, 2016, on measures to ban smoking or fumigation of tobacco products in the workplace or public places, urging the Ministry of Health and relevant institutions to further implement the population protection mechanism. Everyone from tobacco smoke.
Please be informed that the areas where smoking or smoking of tobacco products are prohibited in the workplace or public places are: health facilities, educational institutions, nurseries, public parks, public parks, religions, museums, cultural resorts, history, gyms, gas stations and sensitive places. Fire.
