According to research documents, Mr. Ngin Sarun claimed that the people who lived on Phnom Kulen existed before the Angkorian period, that is, before the reign of King Jayavarman II, the founding king of the capital Mahindrapot on this mountain.
He said that on Phnom Kulen today, there are also a lot of people living there, there are more than 4,000 families divided into 9 villages in the same commune, Khnong Phnom commune, in which Preah Ang Thom village has people Live more than any other village.
Mr. Ngin Sarun said that now people as well as communities living on Phnom Kulen earn a living by selling and providing services to tourists, growing vegetables, raising animals for sale to tourists, planting balm, finding medicine and farming a little. And so on.
Please be informed that Phnom Kulen is a special mountain range that covers an area of about 40 km from northwest to southeast, covering two districts: Svay Leu and Varin districts of Siem Reap province. It is about 60 km from Siem Reap city and about 25 km from Banteay Srei temple.
This sacred mountain was the former capital of Jayavarman II, where he celebrated the "Devaraja" ceremony to anoint him as a deity. It was at this archeological site that Jayavarman II declared the independence of the Khmer Empire from the domination of the Srivijaya Empire of the Javanese during 802 AD, that is, when the pages of the Angkorian Empire were opened. Hong Kong protest leader beaten to death by mob
