Minister Vong Soth said, "In the past, I have seen that the NPC It is a matter of pride, especially for the NPC, to pay attention to providing the social security system to the rights of the people. Strengthen and develop social security services for civil servants to achieve effective results in accordance with the plan.
The Minister of Social Affairs stated that the National Social Security Fund for Civil Servants is a public administration institution that has the obligation to manage and ensure the opening of the social security system, which has six mandates: retirement, loss of professionalism, maternity, occupational accident and death. And those in charge in accordance with the principles of good governance, transparency, efficiency and high responsibility.
Mr. Vong Soth's speech was made on the occasion that he and she were invited to attend the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the results of the first nine months of 2019 and the implementation direction of the National Social Security Fund for civil servants organized. Held on October 17, 2019 in Kep province. The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Ken Sotha, Governor of Kep Province, as well as officials from ministries, departments and civil society organizations.
Minister Vong Soth added that in the past, he had observed that the NPC Focused on providing excellent social security services to the public, including strengthening and developing social security services for civil servants through the banking system and cooperating closely with the Social Security Administration. Distribute ID cards to retirees and people with disabilities who are former civil servants in all 25 capitals and provinces.
Mr. Kim Sovandy, Director of the National Social Security Fund for Civil Servants, reported that in the first nine months of 2019, We have made great efforts to fulfill our duties and responsibilities in serving the social security system effectively and in good cooperation with ministries, institutions, banks and development partners and have achieved excellent results.
Mr. Kim Sovandy added that in order to achieve better results. Strive to find solutions by all means to solve all the old-new challenges by always setting a clear plan and action that is implemented in accordance with the strategic plan of the Ministry, as well as the national development plan and the Rectangular Strategy.
After listening to the report, Minister Vong Soth made some recommendations to the leaders at all levels and the staff of the NPC. All to be implemented in order to promote high efficiency work. These recommendations include:
1. Strengthen the implementation of the procedure for placing civil servants to retire or lose their professional qualifications and the timely payment of social security benefits to the right people twice a month (once every two weeks) with a sense of responsibility. Yes.
2. Strengthen the mechanism for the transfer of rights to retirees and the disabled who are sick and the elderly who are unable to pay their monthly pensions through banks in the capital and provinces effectively.
3: Accelerate the procedure for preparing social security for retirees and disabled persons who have died and monitor the payment of the remaining monthly pension in the account of the retired and disabled persons to their families. Corpse as soon as possible.
4: Strengthen the management of data on retirees and people with disabilities and their dependents in the capital and provinces clearly in cooperation with the Department of FYI.
5: To review the work accident insurance, maternity insurance and death insurance for civil servants who have not yet applied.
6: Study and make specific plans to increase pensions with the right mechanism, that is, have a long-term vision to bring high and low pensions closer together.
