Four Ministries Jointly Organize National Consultative Workshop on 25 Years of Cambodia's Progress Towards Nairobi Summit
(Phnom Penh): Four Ministries, including the Ministry of Planning, the Ministry of Women's Affairs, the Ministry of Health, and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, jointly organized the National Consultative Workshop on ICPD 25 of Cambodia's Processes for the Nairobi Summit in Kenya and beyond. Conference.
The consultative workshop was organized to mobilize and promote the Royal Government's commitment to accelerate the 1994 Pledge in Cairo, Egypt on the ICPD Action Plan.
The workshop was organized by Mr. Bouch Bunnak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Planning, Ms. Nhean Sochetra, Director General of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, Mr. Chea Chantum, Representative of the Ministry of Economy, Ms. Soeun Socheata, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, and many distinguished guests. Pictures too.
Mr. Bouch Bunnak reminded the seminar that 25 years ago, the Royal Government of Cambodia participated in approving the activities of the International Conference on Population and Development (ICPD) in Cairo, Egypt with about 179 countries.
He added that since the adoption of the ICPD Action Plan, Cambodia has made significant progress in the past 25 years. The Royal Government of Cambodia has recognized the reproductive health program as a basis for the development of the country and established the National Reproductive Health Program to promote and provide this service to the people.
At the same time, Mr. Chea Chanthum presented the progress of the mid-term of the 6th Asia-Pacific Conference on Population, Challenges and Conclusions and the next steps.
In 1994, at the International Conference on Population and Development, 179 governments recognized the rights and health of all people. A national delegation led by Minister of Women's Affairs Ing Kantha Phavi will attend a summit in Nairobi this November to reaffirm the government's commitment to address unresolved challenges.
Cambodian Parliamentarian Khuon Sodary also thanked the IPU President for agreeing to Cambodia's request to remove Sam Rainsy from the list of those to be addressed at the 141st General Assembly because he was a convicted felon. The court is pursuing the arrest.
It should be noted that the 141st General Assembly of the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) was held in Belgrade, Republic of Serbia from the evening of October 13 and officially opened on October 14, 2019 with representatives from all countries. Give a speech. The conference will end on October 17, 2019.
The General Assembly was attended by more than 1,700 IPU delegates from 140 countries, including 70 Speakers, 40 Vice-Chairmen, 700 MPs, 30% women and 17% young people, as well as representatives of key institutions. There are the United Nations, international organizations and civil society partners from many countries around the world.
