Speaking on the occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen mentioned that this is his fifth visit to Bulgaria, after the fourth visit in the early 1980s. The Prime Minister also claimed that the relationship between Cambodia and Bulgaria has been around for about 60 years so far.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked and remembered the Bulgarian government for providing assistance to Cambodia after the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, and Samdech also thanked the government and the people of Bulgaria for their continued assistance to Cambodia. In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also offered his condolences to the three Bulgarian soldiers who lost their lives in the operation in the early 1990s.
In particular, for this bilateral meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister emphasized that the two sides spoke sincerely and frankly on the existing bilateral relations, and Samdech believes that this visit will produce new fruitful results and a roadmap. The path of relations between the two countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that during the meeting, the two sides discussed, focusing on bilateral relations, promoting economic, trade, investment and other areas, including education. In addition, the meeting also established various mechanisms to promote relations between the two countries, and at this point, Samdech Techo stated that the Minister will do some more work to decide on what is planned and discussed already.
As for education, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that from 1980 to 1989, about 200 Cambodian students went to study in Bulgaria, at which point he requested the Prime Minister of Bulgaria to provide more scholarships to train Cambodian students.
In this cordial meeting, the Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia also invited the Prime Minister of Bulgaria to attend the Asia-Europe Meeting, which Cambodia will host in 2020. In response, the Bulgarian Prime Minister promised to find a suitable time to visit Cambodia.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the delegation started their official visit to Sofia, Bulgaria on October 16, 2019. The Prime Minister was warmly greeted by Bulgarian Prime Minister Boyko Borissov at the Government House in Sofia.
