Duke Kouch Mengly Continues to Expand Khmer Nursery Education Due to Favorable Factors of National Peace and Political Stability
(Phnom Penh): Oknha Dr. Kouch Mengly, Founder, Chairman and CEO of AII Language Center and American Intercontinental School, officially inaugurated another private school building on Chroy Changvar Branch on the 16th. This October 2019.
Oknha Dr. Kouch Mengly said that due to the political stability, the higher economic growth of Cambodia and to meet the needs of the market, as well as many requests from parents, guardians and students from all walks of life about the quality of discipline and service, he made efforts. Expand to create more private schools to participate in national development with the Royal Government.
He said that all these factors have made his private education sector, which was established in 2005, more and more famous both domestically and abroad, initially with only four students so far. Currently, the number of students has increased to more than 1,100.
According to Oknha Dr. Kouch Mengly, the AII Language Center and the American Intercontinental School, Chroy Changvar Branch is the sixth branch of the educational institution after Phsar Thmey, Chom Chao, Chak Angre, Toul Kork, and Mao Tse Tung. In addition to the above six branches, his private educational institution will continue to expand its potential in all districts throughout Phnom Penh and many provinces throughout the country.
The new course at AII Language Center will take place on October 21, 2019. On the occasion of the official inauguration of the Chroy Changvar branch building, Mr. Oknha Dr. Kouch Mengly awarded 50% scholarship to each student who enrolled from 4 at the same time.
