In response, the Commander of the Cambodian Armed Forces thanked the Korean government, army and people for their continued support and assistance to Cambodia, in general and to the Cambodian military in the past.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet stated that after the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Korea began in 1997 under the initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, relations between the two countries have developed in all fields, including defense. Nation is also a priority sector.
