Oknha Kouch Mengly: Learning a foreign language does not value Khmer as a point, lacking equal to not value one's own nation
(Phnom Penh): Oknha Kouch Mengly, an expert in the field of education in Cambodia, expressed great concern to the parents and guardians of some students who sent their young children to learn a foreign language at the same time or before starting to learn Khmer. In its national language.
While expressing concern, this expert also strongly criticized the ideas of some Cambodian children who think only of trying to learn a lot of foreign languages, Khmer, while themselves write the Khmer script incorrectly at all.
The Concerns of the Founder, Chairman and CEO of the AII Language Center and the American Intercontinental School were presented to the media, teachers, students, parents and guardians on the occasion of his inauguration. Official use of its private school building, Chroy Changvar branch on October 16, 2019.
He also advised that everyone in Cambodia should not learn their language first. Doing so will only make the country more ignorant. If literature is lost, then the nation may also be lost, as the saying goes, literature represents the soul of the nation.
"They can not stay in their own country, take their language as a basis," he said. Destroy the race, destroy the language, destroy the future, destroy the Khmer children, destroy the Khmer country, which makes our Khmer have no foundation, no culture, no language, no civilization, no future.
