Minister of Education urges young people to study and research Khmer history and language in line with the modernization and research in international countries
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, urged students to study and research on Khmer history, Khmer language in accordance with the modernization and research in international countries. He added that the education sector has been reformed for the past six years, and quality education depends on teaching and learning.
He made the remarks at an international conference on "Languages, Cultures and Education in Southeast Asia and Diversity" on October 16, 2019 at the Cambodia-Korea Cooperation Center (CKCC). He said that today's conference also focuses on the past, present and future for young people to do research.
"I want our young people to do research on the history as well as the language of Cambodia," he said. I think this task is huge for young Cambodians to raise awareness of the national identity culture. "We also need to do international research."
Mr. Hang Chuon Naron also said that in this research, we want our Cambodian children to know and know how to solve what happens. Importantly, foreign languages are also important for young people at the beginning of higher education. The minister added that young people not only do research, they must understand the past, but also plan for the future to do good research.
The minister also added that young people, if they want to know the literary history of the Khmer national identity, must know French, English, because most of the books written by previous researchers on history are written in French and English.
On that occasion, Mr. Chet Jelly, Rector of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, said that the Center for Humanities and Sociology Research will contribute to students and youth in research.
He said that the center was established by the Royal University of Phnom Penh, the University of Fine Arts and the National Institute of Education, and the Royal University of Phnom Penh also has a Faculty of Humanities that provides students with quality education to respond to research.
