Bulgaria offers 10 scholarships for Cambodian students
This proposal and decision was made during a working meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Bouy Koborisov on October 16, 2019.
Bulgaria was one of the few countries in Eastern Europe that supported the Cambodian government in the 1980s after the overthrow of the genocidal regime, although many countries at the time imposed sanctions on Cambodia. Bulgaria also provided many scholarships to Cambodian students at the time.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, between 1980 and 1989, Bulgaria provided scholarships to about 200 Cambodian students. To date, those students have been working in other government institutions as well.
