(Sofia, Bulgaria): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his delegation began an official visit to Sofia, Bulgaria on October 16, 2019. The Prime Minister was warmly greeted by Bulgarian Prime Minister Boyko Borissov at the Government House in Sofia.
The Prime Minister expressed his deep gratitude to the Government and people of Bulgaria for their outstanding assistance and support to Cambodia during the difficult period after the war and the genocidal regime of Pol Pot. Special thanks to the deployment of Bulgarian Blue Hat forces in Operation UNTAC in Cambodia in the early 1990s.
He added that the reopening of the Cambodian Embassy in Sofia in 2019 underscores the Royal Government of Cambodia's commitment to provide additional energy to traditional friendly relations and cooperation between the two countries. Both are based on the principles of mutual benefit, mutual respect, mutual trust and equality.
Samdech Techo continued that the reopening of the embassy also recognizes the importance of expanding economic cooperation.
During the meeting, the two heads of government expressed satisfaction with the signing of a memorandum of understanding on tourism cooperation between the two countries last year, which aims to boost people-to-people contacts. Population and tourist exchanges between the two countries.
