(Brunei): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and a delegation attended the 19th ASEAN + 3 Ministerial Meeting on Agriculture and Forestry (China, Korea and Japan) in Brunei on October 16, 2019.
The Chairman of the 19th Ministerial Meeting on Agriculture and Forestry Plus Three reported on the report and recommendations of the 19th Ministerial Meeting on Agriculture and Forestry Plus Three on six strategic points, including: 1. Strengthening food security. Biological energy development 3: Sustainable forest management 4: Adaptation and mitigation to climate change 5: Disease control and plant and livestock health 6: Inter-sectoral issues
On the same day, Mr. Veng Sakhon and his delegation attended the 5th ASEAN-India Ministerial Meeting on Agriculture and Forestry in Brunei.
The Chairman of the ASEAN-India Agriculture and Forestry Working Group reported and made recommendations to the 5th ASEAN-India Ministerial Meeting on Agriculture and Forestry on the progress of ASEAN-India Agriculture and Forestry Cooperation activities.
Activity 1: Strengthen cooperation in the fields of food, agriculture and forestry in key areas that can be mutually beneficial to enhance the productivity of agricultural products and respond to food security issues, as well as improve the flow of agricultural products to the world market. .
Activity 2: Promote networking and cooperation between competent governments with agricultural and food experts, laboratories, institutions related to food and agriculture, farmers and agricultural communities and ASEAN and Indian business community
Activity 3: Promoting investment, capacity building, sharing of information and experience and best practices, research and development of agricultural technology, management and innovation in food, agriculture, fisheries and forestry
Activity 4: Develop human resources in the food, agriculture, fisheries and forestry sub-sectors by providing opportunities for the next generation of ASEAN to learn about the management and conservation of natural resources, the use of better techniques, management and implementation on farms through training and dissemination.
Activity 5: Support and strengthen cooperation in the implementation of the ASEAN Integrated Food Security Framework (AIFS) and the ASEAN Regional Food Security Action Plan 2015-2020.
Activity 6: Promote the adaptation of natural systems and enhance the accessible capacity of the human community to deal with environmental hazards. Chinese Government Grant-Based Mineral Resources Laboratory Officially Inaugurated
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Mines and Energy, in cooperation with the Office of Geological Exploration and Mining of Guangxi Province, People's Republic of China, organized the handover ceremony and inauguration ceremony of the National Geological Laboratory of Cambodia, the National Geological Laboratory of History. In Cambodia in the mining sector under a grant from the People's Republic of China.
The National Geological Laboratory of Cambodia is located in Phsar Trach Village, Longvek Commune, Kampong Tralach District, Kampong Chhnang Province. The National Geological Laboratory of Cambodia can also assist relevant units in studying the potential of mineral resources throughout Cambodia.
The National Geological Laboratory of Cambodia is the result of a Memorandum of Understanding on Geological and Mineral Cooperation between the Ministry of Mines and Energy of Cambodia and the Ministry of Land and Resources of the People's Republic of China, signed on December 19, 2011. Go.
Separately, the Cambodian side is responsible for providing a site of at least 14,000 square meters for the construction of a laboratory located in Phsar Trach village, Longvek commune, Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province and facilitate administrative work, law and communication with local authorities.
The opening of the National Geological Laboratory of Cambodia is a new opportunity for Cambodia in the field of mining, which allows civil servants of the Ministry of Mines and Energy to strengthen and expand their professional knowledge as technicians in geological laboratories and can also help To the relevant units to study the potential of mineral resources throughout Cambodia as well.
In addition, companies operating in the mining sector will also be able to reduce the time and cost of taking samples to test abroad, as well as make Cambodia a new source of income. Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province told Techo Sen Svay Rieng Polytechnic Institute to determine the curriculum that provides job opportunities for students after graduation
