The Hungarian President's state visit to Cambodia is at the invitation of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia. This is according to Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister.
He claimed that in a meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen that afternoon, the President of Hungary thanked the King of Cambodia for his state visit to Cambodia and that the President would pay a state visit to Cambodia at the end. This coming October.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and Hungary. Samdech said that the King of Cambodia is looking forward to receiving the President's visit to Cambodia in the near future.
In addition to attending the official meeting of the state visit, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also invited the President of Hungary to visit Cambodia's Angkor Wat.
Samdech thanked the President of Hungary and look forward to welcoming the President to Cambodia in the near future.
This statement was made on the occasion of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid a courtesy call on the President of Hungary in Hungary on the afternoon of October 15, 2019.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, confirmed the results of the meeting that during this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen raised issues related to the EBA. Samdech requested the President of Hungary to continue to assist Cambodia in relation to the EBA issue, however, he stressed that the decision depends on the EU, but make the EU make a fair decision for Cambodia.
He also quoted the Hungarian president as saying: "He also stressed the importance of the European Union and the European Commission, which will soon have a new commission. Newly started, we will continue this work and we will continue to support Cambodia. "Hungary continues to demand that Cambodia continue to support the EBA."
In February 2019, the European Union announced the start of proceedings that could lead to a temporary suspension of the preferential treatment. The EBA system may be abolished if the beneficiary is found to be violating important human and labor rights.
The Royal Government of Cambodia considers this European decision to be the most unjust. However, the Royal Government of Cambodia is ready and has put in place other mechanisms in response to the removal of the EBA.
