Speaking on behalf of the Thai Drug Control Council, Jari Pokpa confirmed that the Thai Drug Control Board (ONCB) is ready to coordinate and work with the National Anti-Drug Authority as a counterpart in supporting the work. Drug testing in Cambodia.
Speaking on behalf of Minister Mam Bunheng, Mr. Chhum Vannarith emphasized that the work of treating drug addicts is complicated because drug addicts, who are mentally ill, are carefree and do not seek medical treatment differently from general patients. Get sick and run for help to recover.
Mr. Chhum Vannarith added, "All skills in the fight against drugs must work together, help each other, complement each other, solve and treat drug addicts for the safety of the community and the safety of the people." "People are like a band that needs to perform together in a beautiful way."
He instructed all participants to work hard to learn and share experiences with each other in theory and practice, continue to explore and solve drug problems successfully.
It should be noted that the training course on management and governance on the treatment and rehabilitation of drug addicts in Cambodia took place for three days from October 16 to 18, 2019 in Siem Reap.
