Dispute over rice drainage leads to violence in Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province
(Kampong Cham): The dispute over the drainage of rice fields led to the use of violence against each other until one side arrested an older man, tied his hands and feet, beat him and dived into the field. The incident happened at more than 10 am on October 14, 2019 at a farm in Pdao Chum commune, Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province.
Suddenly, a man named Pen Nime became angry with Lim Lam, causing water to flood his farm. To the point of using violence against each other, but because the name Pen Nime has two wives, Lim Lam could not win. By the name of Pen Nime, named Lim Lam, tied his hands and feet and dived into the field. Later, people came to see and detained both parties and reported to local police officers.
In connection with this case, Brigadier General Heng Vuthy, Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Planning of Kampong Cham Province, confirmed that there were indeed cases of mutual violence in the fields. He added that in this case, he is processing the case according to the procedure by sending it to the Kampong Cham Provincial Court.
However, the relatives of the victims still insist that the authorities and the Kampong Cham Provincial Court take action against the perpetrators due to the use of serious violence, which must be punished according to law.
(Belgrade, Serbia): The Second Vice President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, Ms. Khuon Sodary, stressed the importance of respecting international law based on the rule of law and promoting the strengthening of the multilateral system in building international order for all states. Regardless of the size, wealth and strength of each state.
She made the remarks during a speech to delegates from IPU member states, including the Speaker of the National Assembly, the Vice-Speakers of Women and Youth, as well as representatives of key institutions, including NGOs. Nations, international organizations and key civil society partners at the 141st General Assembly of the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) in the Republic of Serbia on the afternoon of October 15, 2019.
"Each country has its own traditions, interests, security and aspirations," she said. In particular, for Cambodia, despite being a small state, Cambodia adheres to international values and principles, and is committed and actively working to promote an open, efficient and rule-based multilateral system. Law.
The 141st General Assembly of the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) is currently attended by more than 1,700 IPU parliamentary delegates from 140 countries, including 70 Speakers, 40 Vice-Chairmen and 700 women MPs. 30% and 17% young people, as well as representatives of key institutions, including the United Nations, international organizations and civil society partners from around the world.
"Strengthening international law starts at home," she told the General Assembly. In fact, at the national level, Cambodia has a strong and clear political commitment to strengthen the rule of law, which is the foundation of good governance and strong democracy.
In fact, she said, in the last national election in July 2018, 20 different political parties competed for seats in the National Assembly. Thus, Cambodia is very proud of the steady growth of the democratic process in Cambodia. She firmly believes that peace, development, democracy and the rule of law are inextricably linked, and that there is no lasting peace and security without international law.
She shared that the peace that Cambodia is enjoying today is due to Cambodia's value for peace, full stability, as well as good regional and international cooperation, which are a prerequisite for the development and continuation of Cambodia. Achieving steady economic growth of 7% over the last two decades.
She also expressed concern over the peace and stability that Cambodia has so far achieved, which seems to remain fragile and vulnerable due to the challenges rooted in the rise of extremist politics and its people. Population politics, as well as the infiltration of superpowers, including some Western countries, into Cambodia's internal affairs.
"Even though our country is under pressure from the threat of sanctions through the use of the pretext of democracy and human rights, the Royal Government of Cambodia remains united with the Cambodian people in all circumstances," she said. All.
She emphasized the important role that lawmakers play in linking people-to-people with policymakers, especially with regard to foreign policy-making and strategic responses to external change.
With this in mind, she briefed the General Assembly on Cambodia's participation in regional cooperation, as well as the promotion of norms and principles of international law-based law, with the Cambodian Parliament actively participating in the forum. Many, both regional and international.
She added that in 2020, Cambodia will be honored to host the 11th Asia-Europe Parliamentary Partnership Meeting with the aim of strengthening multilateralism and partnership for sustainable development and common growth. . Cambodia has adopted a flexible and certain foreign policy under the motto "Internal reform and increase external friendships based on the spirit of independence" to achieve sustainable and environmental development.
The Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) is a large legislative body established in 1889 with 179 members of parliament from sovereign states. The Cambodian Parliament joined the IPU in April 1997 at the 97th Inter-Parliamentary Assembly in Seoul, Republic of Korea.
At a press conference in Beijing, Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Geng Shuang said: "We strongly express our strong dissatisfaction and strong opposition to the US House of Representatives over the passage of the resolution. "Hong Kong's draft law on human rights and democracy ... and relations between Beijing and Washington could be damaged if it is passed."
The Hong Kong Draft of Human Rights and Democracy is a measure passed by the US House of Representatives, which requires the US Secretary of State to confirm annually that Hong Kong remains committed to its autonomy. Terms: Special as a major economic center.
Beaten to death, robbed a motorcycle in Sangkat Sak Sampov, Khan Dangkor, now the police are searching for the perpetrator
(Phnom Penh): A man was found dead in the middle of the road in Kvit village, Sak Sampov commune, Dangkor district, Phnom Penh, on suspicion of murder and robbery of a motorbike. This incident caused a surprise at 6:30 am October 16, 2019.
According to the police, the victim, 29-year-old Mek Phin, was a glassblower and a motodup driver, living in a rented house around Jinchuri Plaza Market, Po Sen Chey District, and was born in Sam Khly Village, Prek Khla Commune, Koh Andat District, Takeo Province.
Police said that after receiving reports from residents that there was an immediate death, the police force of the Sampov police station, in cooperation with the specialized force of the Dangkor district inspector, went to the scene and found a plastic gun near the body. Helmets and motorcycle goggles and bruises on the neck and ribs.
According to the relatives of the man, the victim rode a 2015 Dream Series motorcycle from home and disappeared at 8 pm on October 15, 2019, but could not be reached until the morning of October 16. Authorities said the victim had been beaten to death and robbed of a motorcycle.
After checking and asking information from the relatives of the man, the police concluded that it was a case of murder and robbery of a motorcycle because the victim had left the house on a motorcycle before his death, while the competent authorities of Dangkor district and relevant authorities are conducting a search to arrest the person. Violators will be punished according to the law.
