Speech by Samdech Techo at Water Summit in Budapest: Malaysia Amend Law on Response to Rising Suicides
KUALA LUMPUR: The Malaysian government is studying the possibility of amending the law on suicide attempts as the number of cases rises significantly across the country. This is according to a quote from CNA on Tuesday evening, October 15, 2019.
The goal is to amend the law so that suicide attempts are no longer illegal. Malaysia hopes that in the near future it will have a law that no longer considers suicide attempts illegal, but instead an effective solution that can help those involved in such cases. .
According to the Malaysian government, since the current law was enacted long before independence, this effort could take some time and require detailed study and consultation with a number of stakeholders.
At the same time, Malaysia is also studying and comparing with other countries with similar laws, such as the United Kingdom, Australia, Pakistan and India, to consider their methods and solutions.
