(Phnom Penh): Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Association of Travel Agents of Cambodia, said that there is still fraud, import and sale of counterfeit souvenirs in Cambodia, but a small amount before the measures from the relevant ministries.
Ms. Chhay Sivalin stated, "In the past, the import of counterfeit souvenirs has been very strong, which has made a name for the country and tarnished the country's reputation. "Selling souvenirs in Cambodia after the issuance of these laws has seen some calm, but not completely, because they used to do this business, so still want to do that business."
She stated that selling fake souvenirs to tourists can really make tourists lose confidence to stop visiting Cambodia, because when tourists go anywhere, as long as he is happy and feels good with that country.
She also called on the relevant institutions as well as the Ministry of Handicrafts to support some communities, encourage them to produce more and more quality, and help find handicraft experts to help them grow.
With this call, she stated that currently not only there are fake souvenirs, but also the supply of souvenirs is not enough for tourists.
