For the Cambodian delegation, there was an invitation to participate and lead the monks 'group from Samdech Preah Udom Vongsa Muong Ra, Secretary of the Monks' Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia. In addition, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information and his wife and accompanying officials were also invited to Chiang Rai to attend the opening ceremony of the pilgrimage on October 15.
The venue will be held at Wat Preah Theat Phangor in Chiang Sen District, Chiang Rai Province, Kingdom of Thailand. Wat Preah Theat Phangor is located on the western side of the Mekong River, opposite the border of the Lao People's Democratic Republic. According to the history of Yonnok, "Khun Pha Ping" or "Prince Ping", the mayor of Yon Nok of the 23rd Dynasty, was the builder of this shrine.
On the other hand, in the opening ceremony of the five pilgrimages of the Mekong region, there will also be a blessing ceremony from the monks of the five countries, as well as a presentation of a special plan of the Royal University of Chiang Rai along with the plan. The other rafts are the rafts of the 5 Territorial Pilgrimage Project.
