Hemorrhagic fever or hemophilia is one of the most dangerous diseases. When it strikes, it causes great pain and if left untreated, it can lead to disability or illness. From death to death. The world does not yet have a cure for this deadly disease, and in Cambodia, the cure for this deadly disease is limited and expensive.
Currently in Cambodia, the disease can be diagnosed in only three places: the National Children's Hospital in Phnom Penh, the Angkor Hospital for Children in Siem Reap and the National Institute of Public Health Research, and if they are aware of the disease, they can find a solution Some effects to avoid serious accidents such as disability, death and can reduce pain.
