(Siem Reap): Over the centuries, the water in the Angkor Wat temple complex has played an important role in sustaining the foundations of Angkor Wat from ancient times to the present and beyond, especially in the future. In this mythical city also represents the ocean that surrounds Mount Sumeru and our universe.
Another feature of the Angkor Wat temple complex is its role in supporting the foundation of the Angkor Wat temple for long-term stability. He said that the piles of stones that were arranged to make Angkor Wat weigh up to millions of tons, which is usually not sustainable, but Angkor Wat is not like that, meaning that due to the power of the water in This is what made this great temple lasting until now and into the future.
Mr. Long Kosal said that the Khmer ancestors of the Angkorian period were really great, he (ancestors) built the temple of Angkor Wat on the dense sand, sand as a foundation under the temple of Angkor, and the water from The surrounding basins feed on the sand under the temple to keep it moist.
He said that when the sand has a strong density that can withstand the weight of our wonderful Angkor temple to survive for a long time. These are the wonders of the great temple of Suryavarman II and Kasindhu around the temple as well.
According to the spokesperson of the APSARA Authority, the amount of water in the basin of Angkor Wat temple is about 1 million cubic meters and has an average depth of 2 meters, length from east to west is 1,500 meters long and width from north to south is 1,300 meters long. Which is a great force in supporting the whole temple.
Later, experts found traces of an ancient waterway that connects the Angkor Wat temple complex to the Angkor Thom temple complex on the eastern side of Phnom Bakheng to collect water from the Angkor Thom temple complex and incorporate it into the Angkor Wat temple complex. The canal is called "Sampov Loun Canal". Later, the Apsara Authority diverted water from the Samdech Techo Hun Sen canal to the Sampov Loun canal because it was closer than the Samdech Techo Hun Sen canal.
Due to these efforts, the APSARA Authority has achieved water stability in the Angkor Wat temple complex to jointly continue the great legacy of the ancestors to be stable for a long time to come. Dr. Nguon Nhel Leads National Assembly Delegation to Honor the Late King
