(Phnom Penh): While the number of tourists visiting Cambodia has increased significantly from year to year, Cambodia has also lost billions of dollars in revenue from the import of souvenirs from abroad. To meet the needs of tourists.
In the "Special Guest of the Week" program, the President of the Cambodian Association of Travel Agents, Ms. Chhay Sivlin, said that we regret the amount of losses from the import of souvenirs from abroad, because the amount of losses is really large, while in a year Cambodia Received more than 6 million tourists.
According to Ms. Chhay Sivlin, imports to Cambodia include dried fruits, which Cambodia continues to import from neighboring countries, and souvenirs such as handbags, bracelets for sisters, home shoes, clothes, scarves, etc.
At the same time, she also pointed out that despite the abundance of Cambodian silk scarves, but still need to import because our production can not produce cheap and expensive. .
Ms. Chhay Sivlin continued, "Some visitors to Cambodia do not want expensive things, just want things to send to friends, so he wants a cheap price here, we can not do this, which is a problem."
The president of the association also said, "Why can't we produce?" Because they produce in large quantities, different from us, because our enterprise is small and not yet supported.
It should be noted that in the first eight months of 2019, Cambodia received more than 4 million tourists, an increase of 10.4 percent compared to the same period in 2018.
