In this conference, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his deep satisfaction with the continued maintenance of good relations between Cambodia and the Czech Republic. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his happiness to the Czech government for choosing Cambodia as a priority country for development cooperation from 2018 to 2023.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia also did not forget to thank the Czech government for providing scholarships to Cambodian students since 1981. As of 2019, a total of 362 Cambodian students have been educated in the Czech Republic, and some are working in government ministries and institutions.
It should be noted that Cambodia established diplomatic relations with the former Socialist Republic of Czechoslovakia on May 18, 1956. In 1975, diplomatic relations between the two countries were severed during the Khmer Rouge regime. In 1979, Cambodia became closely associated with the Socialist Republic of Czechoslovakia. On September 7, 1996, diplomatic relations between Cambodia and the Czech Republic were re-established after Czechoslovakia was divided into two countries.
