Tycoon Kith Meng asks Czech investors to open small aircraft factory in Cambodia
(Czech Republic): Cambodia's top billionaire tycoon Kith Meng, president of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, has asked Czech investors to open a small aircraft factory in Cambodia. Kith Meng also proposed training for small pilots in Cambodia. Mr. Kith Meng sees that the production of aircraft and pilot training will be a part of promoting the flight in Cambodia from one province to another to promote tourism.
The request of Duke Kith Meng was made during a meeting on trade between Cambodia and the Czech Republic this morning, October 14, 2019, in Prague, Czech Republic. The meeting was chaired by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce of Cambodia, and Mr. Karel Havilik, Deputy Prime Minister of the Czech Ministry of Industry and Trade.
During the meeting, Duke Kith Meng mentioned that the Czech Republic is a country with high technology, equipment, machinery, but currently there is not much market in Cambodia. Therefore, investing in Cambodia is an opportunity for Czech investors, and the Czechs can also capture investment in information technology, information security, information technology, data collection, and so on.
As the trade volume between Cambodia and the Czech Republic is still small, about $ 243 million in 2018, Duke Kith Meng has asked the Czech Republic to increase trade volume. Neak Oknha Kith Meng stated that the Czech Republic and Cambodia have many sectors that can be invested, such as agriculture, industry, tourism, food processing, construction, electric vehicles and health.
To boost trade between the two countries, Duke Kith Meng also asked the Czech government to open direct flights to Cambodia.
In today's meeting, the Cambodian and Czech Chambers of Commerce also signed a memorandum of understanding on trade cooperation between the two chambers of commerce.
