During his official visit today, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was warmly welcomed by Czech Prime Minister Andrej Babis. After the official reception, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Czech Prime Minister held a closed-door meeting and a bilateral summit, including a working lunch in a very friendly and cordial atmosphere.
On behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his deep gratitude for the invaluable assistance provided by the Government and people of the Czech Republic to Cambodia in the most difficult times after the liberation of the country. 1979
The two heads of government reviewed with satisfaction the development of Cambodia-Czech relations and the progress made in recent years for the common benefit of the people of the two countries and pledged to strengthen Strengthen friendships and cooperation in politics, economy, trade, tourism, health and agriculture.
During the summit, the two leaders exchanged views and agreed on enhancing cooperation on regional and international issues of mutual concern. In addition, the two leaders recognized the importance of promoting multilateral and international cooperation for world peace and integration for the benefit of global development.
The two leaders also agreed to boost ties at all levels, including exchanges of high-level visits and political consultations between the two Ministries of Foreign Affairs aimed at seeking mutually beneficial cooperation.
The Prime Minister thanked the Czech government for turning debt into development aid for Cambodia, especially the continued support of the Czech government and people in continuing to provide assistance in the areas of education, health and rural development under the cooperation program. Development.
The two sides agreed on a joint plan to celebrate the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries in 2021. The Prime Minister of the Czech Republic Andrej Babis expressed his deep appreciation for Cambodia's commitment to peace and stability under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who has led the country towards sustainable socio-economic development.
The Czech Prime Minister expressed his firm belief that Cambodia will achieve its goal of becoming a high middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2050.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen invited Czech Prime Minister Andrej Babis to pay an official visit to Cambodia at an appropriate time. The Prime Minister gladly accepted the invitation and expressed his gratitude to the Prime Minister for this invitation.
After the meeting, the Heads of Government of the two countries witnessed the signing ceremony of two important documents, namely: the Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation between the Ministry of Health of Cambodia and the Czech Health Project Implementation Agency (VAMED) and the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU). Mutual understanding between the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Czech Chamber of Commerce.
The signing of the two memoranda is an indication of the two leaders' desire to expand ties and continue development cooperation for the benefit of both peoples.
It should be noted that Cambodia established diplomatic relations with the former Socialist Republic of Czechoslovakia on May 18, 1956. In 1975, diplomatic relations between the two countries were severed during the Khmer Rouge regime. On September 7, 1996, diplomatic relations between Cambodia and the Czech Republic were re-established after Czechoslovakia was divided. NATO must choose between Turkey and terrorists, says Turkish president
