According to Samdech Techo's program, when he arrived in the Czech Republic, Samdech Techo had to visit the old city of the Czech Republic, but Samdech Techo canceled this program and invited him to meet with the Cambodian people who came to receive him.
During the talk, Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the nieces and nephews of students who had the opportunity to study in a developed country like the Czech Republic. This is the pride of Cambodia with human resources being trained everywhere, both inside and outside the country. Although not directly with you, but as the Prime Minister, the Prime Minister always misses and loves all Cambodians, not only in the Czech Republic.
In fact, Cambodia and the Czech Republic have had good relations since the 1960s, and former King Norodom Sihanouk was also a student in the Czech Republic. Diplomatic relations between our two countries were good, especially from 1979-1990, when the Cambodian government sent a large number of students to study here through scholarships that Cambodia received.
Please also note that the former Embassy of the Czech Republic was located at the European Embassy today. The Czech Republic also has good relations with ASEAN, and at the same time, the Czech Republic has decided to provide $ 1.5 million in annual development assistance to Cambodia from 2020.
Before concluding, Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed his position on cooperation with the Czech Republic, which will be discussed in detail tomorrow. Samdech Pramukh led the Cambodian people and nieces and nephews of students who are studying in their country to pay attention to study and respect the laws of their country well.
At the same time, Samdech Techo provided financial support to the children who are studying here with love in a very happy and friendly atmosphere. This morning, the 70th Brigade celebrated the 25th anniversary of the division
Over the past 25 years, the officers, deputies and soldiers of the 70th Brigade under the command of Lt. Gen. Mao Sophan, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the 70th Brigade and Commander Sub-commanders at all levels strive to carry out core tasks effectively.
Lt. Gen. Mao Sophan said that for 25 years from its inception, the 70th Brigade has overcome all obstacles to achieve the highest orders of the Prime Minister as well as the Ministry of National Defense. And the Army Command, with many achievements, including:
Defeated the target of Phnom Penh International Airport to protect national and international leaders, ASEAN Summit 2012 and related meetings a total of 586 times
* In addition to the operational work, the brigade has made efforts to strengthen the capacity of the army by sending them to training schools in the country and abroad, as well as conducting live ammunition training exercises in all skills on a regular basis to increase the capacity of the army. In accordance with the plan set by the Steering Committee for Training and Training of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces
* Focused on psychological education for soldiers through the organization of unit competition movements
* Excellent individuals compete in sports and disseminate all content, instructions, especially education, strengthen the spirit of the army on a regular basis according to the situation to ensure effective management and leadership.
* Promote gender work by providing opportunities for female soldiers to have positions in command at all levels and actively participate in social movements and day-to-day tasks such as rescue and security operations.
* Paying attention to solving the policy when there are soldiers who have died, died or disabled, settling the funeral expenses, visiting sick soldiers, supporting veterans and military families in the spirit of contributing to the implementation of national policy for veterans, a total of 215 times. A total of 1,203,580,000 (one thousand two hundred billion five hundred and eighty thousand riels) and 350 tons of rice
* Efforts have been made to take care of and ensure the livelihood of the army, such as farming and animal husbandry. Daily coffee for soldiers throughout the division as well
* In order to improve the well-being and contribute to reducing poverty of the people, the division has 1 hospital and 2 health centers, the first health center is located in Kraing Ampil commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province and the second health center is located in Trapeang Reang commune, Chum Kiri district, Kampong Speu province. Kampot to treat people and have clean water machines distributed to people free of charge
* A clearing ceremony was held for the opening and closing ceremony of 6 shooting lanes, a skyscraper, a helipad, a parking lot, a kitchen and a 145 km road 144 from Phnom Cheal to the entrance of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Techo Sen base. Phnom Thom Meas Pov, the venue for the 2018 Golden Dragon Exercise between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army
* Developed 17,000 hectares of land in Chum Kiri district, Kampot province into a live-fire training ground for mixed battalion battalions and built a total of 53 buildings and named it Chea Chumki Training School Serve for the Hanuman Gold Exercise 2018 of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Golden Dragon Exercise 2019 between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army.
At the same time, with the permission of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the division is also clearing roads and fields for the construction of a 21-meter-tall Buddha statue and other buildings for religious purposes.
Considering that Sihanoukville is the second economic pole of the Kingdom of Cambodia, especially with the permission of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the 70th Brigade cooperated with JPR to build a relief school in Sihanoukville under the name "Cambodia-Japan Friendship Rescue Training School" and equipped with fire trucks, ambulances and other rescue equipment.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Mao Sophan also expressed his gratitude to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh and the Commander-in-Chief, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Army for providing good advice and directions to promote the construction and development of training. The division has made progress in all areas in the past.
The Lt. Gen. also thanked the National Police Commissioner, Deputy Commander and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, Deputy Commander and Commander of the Bodyguard Command, Chairman of the Capital-Provincial Unity Command and the authorities. There are authorities throughout the country who have cooperated well with the brigade for the past 25 years in the task of national defense, security and maintaining social order in Phnom Penh.
At the same time, he thanked friendly countries such as the People's Republic of China, Japan, the Republic of Korea, the Socialist Republic of Vietnam for providing technical assistance and military training of the brigade in the past.
