Director of National Children's Hospital calls on parents to find out what foods should and should not be given to children, especially sweet drinks
(Phnom Penh): The director of the National Children's Hospital, Dr. Nhep Angka Bos, said that parents should prepare food for children when they go to school regularly, such as providing cakes with nutritious foods such as milk, cakes without having to give money to children to Do not let children buy any food that is harmful to health, especially too many sugary drinks, make children full, do not eat other foods, risk malnutrition to children.
This statement was made after attending the closing ceremony of the first pediatric conference organized by the National Children's Hospital under the theme "Sharing experiences of practice in infant and child care" held at the hotel. Phnom Penh this weekend.
Dr. Nheb Angka Bos said that all parents need to know how to care for and feed their children properly so that children can be healthy, grow well, be intelligent and learn well. In particular, help children avoid malnutrition and health challenges or dangers.
The National Children's Hospital is a leading hospital in providing nutrition to children, meaning that the hospital provides three free meals to children who come to the hospital. Standards help children get adequate nutrition.
At the same time, Professor Kruy Leang Sim, Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of Health, also said that giving children a sweet diet will put children at risk of diabetes, which parents have to face daily expenses because Diabetes requires lifelong treatment, and children are at risk for their health and education.
At the same time, some pregnant women are also at risk for diabetes due to the habit of eating too many sugary foods such as durian and some foreign foods. Therefore, she advised people to eat a balanced diet is to eat vegetables, meat and fruits to have enough nutrition to support our health, especially children to be healthy and strong.
