To better understand how the use of violence committed by spouses or juvenile offenders is punishable? Therefore, for this week's Legal Awareness Program, under the collaboration between FRESH NEWS and the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, we will present to the following students:
To understand the level of punishment for the above offenses, we need to understand the terms spouse and incest. Spouse refers to the spouse or both spouses who acquired the status of the spouse after the legal registration of the marriage, while the term adultery refers to the status of a man and a woman living together but not registering the marriage.
Punishment of violence committed by spouses or juvenile offenders is more serious than intentional violence is for the purpose of educating and eliminating domestic violence that has affected the family economy, society and public order, especially To the memory as well as the future of the child.
Pursuant to Article 229 of the Penal Code, additional types and periods of punishment may be declared as follows:
In summary, violence committed by a spouse or juvenile in the 2009 Penal Code is clearly defined in terms of punishing and punishing the perpetrators who have violated public order, family and children, and for the purpose of education prevention. Do not let this crime happen again.
