Senior Minister Kun Kim personally inspected and intervened in the case of people's houses facing collapse into the river in Chhlong district, Kratie province
(Kratie): After hearing the news that a house in Kandal village, Koh Kandor and Kandal village, Chhlong commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province collapsed and faced collapse into the river due to the collapse of the river bank on the afternoon of October 12, 2019, Mr. Senior Minister Kun Kim, in charge of special missions and First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, led a team to inspect the situation and intervene.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim ordered the provincial and district armed forces to work together to dismantle people's homes and evacuate people to avoid endangering their lives.
At the same time, Senior Minister Kun Kim also announced to the people living near the area to be ready to dismantle because he observed that behind their house there is a series of cracks in the ground. The senior minister also asked the working group to find out why it caused landslides and landslides.
Please be informed that this morning, October 11, 2019, 12 houses in Kandal village, Koh Kandor and Kandal village, Chhlong commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province, collapsed into the river due to the collapse of the river bank, including one house. It completely collapsed into the river as authorities and police arrived to help dismantle it.
Mr. Thim Seang Leng, Deputy Governor of Chhlong District, said that 12 houses could collapse into the river if not demolished in time, one house completely collapsed into the river and many others collapsed. 50% fall into the river if not dismantled in time.
The deputy governor added that he was leading forces to dismantle the houses of the people to a safe place to break into the river in time and no one was injured in the landslide.
