Senior Minister Kun Kim Inspects River Bank Collapse in Front of Kratie Provincial Hall
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, this morning, October 13, 2019, led an inter-ministerial working group consisting of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Ministry of Mines. And energy as well as local authorities inspected the river bank collapse in front of Kratie Provincial Hall to find measures to solve it.
Mr. Kun Kim said that the riverbank in front of Kratie Provincial Hall was completely broken by 30 meters and faced an additional 145 meters long. Mr. Kun Kim stated that the landslide caused by the growth of islets in the middle of the river led to the diversion of water to hit the bank and the groundwater level from Boeung Romleach and the flooded area there, causing the river bank to become unbalanced and lead to slippage. The bank collapsed immediately.
After inspecting this morning, officials from the Ministry of Water Resources requested the Ministry of Mines and Energy to supply sand to block the riverbank to prevent it from spreading to another 145 meters. When the water recedes, take further action.
Please note that the river bank collapse in front of Kratie Provincial Hall occurred on October 10, 2019 at 1:00 pm. The landslide caused landslides, as well as sidewalks along the river.
