Samdech Techo Hun Sen Calls on 6 Points for Cambodian Christians to Participate in the Development of Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on October 12, 2019 Called on 6 important points for the Cambodian Christian people to participate in the implementation to develop Cambodia to grow even more.
The six-point appeal was made on the occasion that Samdech Techo Hun Sen was honored to preside over a banquet with more than 3,000 Cambodian Christians at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center on the evening of the 12th. This October 2019.
During the ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on the people to implement six important points, including:
* First: We must work together to maintain peace, security and order in the society, because if there is no peace, do not talk about religious progress, there is peace, we can do everything.
* Second: To participate in the implementation of a safe village-commune policy, such as participating in the elimination of thieves, robbers, gamblers.
* Third: In the community or in the church must participate in the campaign to reduce and eliminate the problem of illegal drugs.
* Fourth: Pay attention to traffic problems, which are important issues in our country. Therefore, when traveling on the road, all traffic rules must be obeyed. Today, tomorrow, do not have a traffic accident.
* Fifth: Continue to pay attention to the harmonization of religion itself and always have good relations with other religions as well.
* Sixth: Continue to train more human resources to facilitate social contribution and development in other areas with the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked all Christians to join the Royal Government in continuing to maintain peace in order to develop Cambodia further. The Prime Minister wished all Christians happiness and prosperity, and may Jesus Christ bless Christians and nieces and nephews throughout the country.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pleasure to be invited to join the conversation and have a meal with the Christians now. This is the fourth time that Samdech Techo has met with leaders and Christians to harmonize Christianity in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo also thanked all the people who are Christians in Cambodia who have always contributed to the Royal Government of Cambodia in the development of the country and peacekeeping, especially in the past to vote. Cambodian People's Party.
At the same time, the Prime Minister of Cambodia stated that there are three major religions in Cambodia: Buddhism, the state religion, Islam and Christianity. And all religions can live together without religious conflicts, and the government always provides opportunities and support for all religions without any religious persecution.
Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia is very proud of all the religions that have lived without conflict and no attack. For Cambodia, whichever religion you believe in is your right. The Prime Minister stated that all religions in Cambodia were revived after the fall of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
