Finally, the US and China are ready to reach a "incomplete but positive trade agreement for everyone"
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US President Donald Trump on Friday announced an incomplete trade deal with China following the opening of a new round of talks in Washington. This is according to a quote from CNA on Saturday morning, October 12, 2019.
The following are the main points of the agreement that have not yet been signed:
1: Industry
2: Financial services and currency
3: Technology transfer
Donald Trump said talks between senior Chinese and US officials in Washington have made good progress on technology transfer, a key issue in the trade dispute between the two countries, but did not elaborate.
4: Intellectual property
