Minister of Commerce: Cambodia's growth is inseparable from Japan as trade and investment increase
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, said that Cambodia's current progress is inseparable from Japan's trade and investment relations and cooperation.
During the ceremony, Mr. Pan Sosak stated that the Royal Government and the people of Japan have made significant contributions to the pursuit of peace, national unity and the restoration and development of the Cambodian economy through the financing of cooperation, the construction of infrastructure, technical assistance and Human resource development as well as Japanese private sector investment in Cambodia.
The minister stressed that economic cooperation between the two countries has steadily increased the volume of trade and investment.
According to the Minister of Commerce, the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and Japan in 2018 amounted to more than 1.588 million US dollars. Exports from Cambodia to Japan amounted to about 1.079 million US dollars and imports from Japan to Cambodia amounted to about 509 million US dollars.
As for investment, from 1994 to the first quarter of 2019, there were 137 projects with a total investment capital of about 2.5 billion US dollars. The investment focuses on the production of electrical and electronic components, car parts and technical equipment, agro-industry, food processing, hotels, tourism, hospitals and supermarkets.
Minister Pan Sosak also pointed out that in order to solve problems for investors in Cambodia, on September 5, 2019, the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia signed a Memorandum of Understanding with the Japan External Trade Organization (JETRO) to establish a cooperation framework. Operation to promote trade between Cambodia and Japan.
In front of Japanese officials and investors, the Minister hoped that the business and investment activities of Japanese companies in Cambodia will continue to grow to provide added value and provide a better working and living environment for Cambodian workers in line with the Royal Vision. Government to provide decent employment opportunities, maintain economic growth and diversify Cambodia's industrial base.
Mr. Pan Sosak also encouraged Japanese companies to invest more in all sectors, especially food processing using local raw materials, ecotourism, industry, connecting local and regional production chains and human resource training centers for the industrial sector. Original.
At the event, Mr. Tsuyoshi Nozoe, a representative from the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry of Japan, praised Cambodia's progress. Especially the use of technology by Cambodians like this, and Aeon Market also sells goods online to meet the needs of Cambodian customers.
Please be informed that the 2019 Japanese Food Products Exhibition is held from October 2 to November 3, 2019.
