Six Westland International School A and B students visit Singapore to learn and exchange experiences
(Phnom Penh): To encourage A and B students of Westland International School, the school sponsors and organizes a 4-day study tour to Singapore at the partner university of Westland International School from 08 to 8 October 11, 2019 to quote and exchange study experiences at Westland Partners University.
Program Objectives: To motivate students, cultivate young leadership, cultivate a self-reliant mindset, experiment and explore the education system in Singapore, and explore the world outside of developed countries.
For 3 A-level students, the school sponsors 100% of the expenses and with 2 million Riels per student and free 4-quarter English classes for free. For 6 B-level students, the school subsidizes 50% of the cost or 1 million Riel per person and free part-time English study for 4 quarters.
C D and E students will receive a 50% discount on part-time English language study throughout the year. In addition, in order to encourage, motivate and reward the 12th grade teachers, the school donated 1 million Riels to the teachers in the subjects where the students got A grade. From 3 people up.
