Phnom Penh Capital Hall Agrees to Accelerate the Construction of Pedestrian Flyover in front of Doeum Kor Market and Santhor Mok Primary School
(Phnom Penh): To facilitate the travel of people and students, Phnom Penh Capital Administration has agreed to expedite the construction of two more pedestrian flyovers at Doeum Kor Market and Santhor Mok Primary School soon to cross the road. Safe, no risk of any accident.
Phnom Penh Governor Khuong Sreng urged the company to build the first pedestrian flyover in front of Doeum Kor Market in the near future, while the project to build a pedestrian flyover in front of Santhor Mok Primary School needs to be studied further because it wants to expand the construction project. This is on the four-way intersection at the Santhor Mok traffic light.
Speaking at a meeting between Phnom Penh authorities and private companies, on October 10, 2019, Mr. Khuong Sreng said that the acceleration of the construction of the pedestrian flyover in front of Doeum Kor market due to the support of the people want Build as soon as the experts have already studied the impact.
The governor continued, "As for the project to build a pedestrian flyover in front of Santhor Mok Primary School, it needs to be studied in more detail because the authorities want to build this flyover on all four intersections to make it easier for students to cross the road." This is safe, no matter where they come from. ”
Representatives of Spek Media, which has been awarded the right to build the two pedestrian flyovers, said that the pedestrian flyover in front of Doeum Kor Market was built across Mao Tse Toung Boulevard, affecting about eight houses, but they Still able to get in and out of the car due to the distance up to 5 meters from the project. In particular, the project to build a pedestrian flyover in front of Santhor Mok Primary School, the company will continue to study more.
Please note that so far, Phnom Penh has 3 pedestrian flyovers, 2 in the Chompouvorn area of Po Sen Chey district and 1 in the Neang Kong Hing traffic light area, and the Phnom Penh Capital Administration plans to expand this construction project a lot. More places to respond to a developed nation and cities, civilized and convenient for people to cross the road safely.
