(Phnom Penh): Lawyer Ky Tech, Chairman of the Royal Government Lawyers Group and Chairman of the Samdech Techo Sen Volunteer Law Group and his family, who are the children, son-in-law, grandson, grandson and granddaughter, organized a ceremony to celebrate the 3rd anniversary of Kosal's death. Father Ky Leng Pheav and mother Ngor Chou on October 10-11, 2019 at 771, Street 369, Sangkat Prek Pra, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
The three-year anniversary of the dedication of Kosal to the father and mother of the family, lawyer Ky Tech, was attended by close relatives, distinguished guests and many lawyers. Cambodia has more than 100 communities attracting tourists, Tourism Minister urges more community-based tourism activities
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, has announced that the relevant ministries and institutions should strive to transform non-tourism communities into communities that can attract tourists to visit through the integration of tourism activities, exploration and production. New tourism in the community, even under the control of any ministry.
Such promotion was made during the 4th meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group on Management and Development of Community-Based Tourism and Ecotourism on October 10, 2019 at the Ministry of Tourism.
After the meeting, Mr. Chuk Chumnor, Director of the Department of Tourism Product Development, said that the meeting encouraged the communities to integrate tourism activities into their localities, whether the community is under the control of the Ministry of Tourism or any ministry. .
Mr. Chumnor said that according to the latest update, there are more than 2,300 communities under the Ministry of Tourism, Ministry of Environment, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, of which 125 are community-based tourism activities.
Among them, the Ministry of Tourism has 79 communities in 20 provinces operating as tourism communities, the Ministry of Environment has 168 protected area communities (20 communities include tourism activities). Separately, various ministries and institutions are also updating this work.
He added that the meeting also encouraged the community to train technical standards as well as knowledge related to hospitality and safety for tourists, environmental protection, garbage disposal, quality improvement, service and sanitation.
According to Chuk Chumnor, the issue of promoting the construction of roads to connect to the community, infrastructure, water supply, electricity, and telecommunications were also strongly discussed at the meeting.
Please be informed that the development of tourism community has contributed significantly to attracting tourists, delaying tourists' stay and direct income to local people. In fact, according to the World Tourism Organization (UNWTO), cultural tourism accounts for about 50% of the global tourism market and has an annual growth rate of about 6%.
In particular, for Cambodia's tourism, which is cultural and natural tourism, cultural and historical tourism has a market share of about 50% of the total market, and coastal tourism has a market share of about 20%, ecotourism about 20% and tourism, sports and other entertainment.
