Ms. Khuon Sodary attends the 141st IPU General Assembly in Belgrade
(Phnom Penh): The Honorary Dr. Khuon Sodary, Second Vice President of the National Assembly, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, and Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, led a high-level delegation from the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Cambodia on the evening of October 10, 2019 to attend the 141st General Assembly of the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) in Belgrade, Republic of Serbia.
The 141st General Assembly of the Inter-Parliamentary Union was held under the theme "Strengthening International Law: The Role and Mechanism of Parliament and Contribution to Regional Cooperation", which will take place from 13 to 17 October. 2019 in Belgrade, Republic of Serbia.
The annual general assembly is scheduled to be attended by more than 1,700 IPU parliamentary delegations from 140 countries, including 70 parliamentarians, 40 deputies, 700 deputies, and 30% women. 17% of young people, as well as representatives of key institutions, including the United Nations, international organizations and civil society partners from around the world.
The main purpose of the conference is to promote respect for international law to strengthen security, stability and development, during which parliamentarians will discuss the latest developments to promote gender equality, empower youth and protect their rights. People will achieve universal health coverage.
In addition to attending the General Assembly, a high-level delegation from the Cambodian Parliament will also attend 11 related meetings, including:
The Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) is a large legislative body established in 1889 with 179 members of parliament from sovereign states. The Cambodian Parliament joined the IPU in April 1997 at the 97th Inter-Parliamentary Assembly in Seoul, Republic of Korea.
On the morning of October 10, 2019, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin made this request during a meeting with Mr. Naj Mulkavin, the new Ambassador of the People's Republic of Bangladesh to the Kingdom of Cambodia at the National Assembly.
The National Assembly President further stated that the National Assembly of Cambodia is ready to fully cooperate for the success of Mr. Najmul Kavinin's diplomatic mission in Cambodia and Samdech would like to see both countries Cambodia and Bangladesh continue to strengthen and expand their relations. Cooperation in trade, investment and tourism.
On that occasion, Mr. Najmul Kavin congratulated Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin for leading the National Assembly again in this new term. Through his many years of experience in leading the country, especially the leadership of the legislature, he firmly believes that Samdech will bring many new successes to the country and the National Assembly of Cambodia.
The Ambassador also requested Samdech to facilitate the exchange of visits between the Cambodian-Bangladesh Parliamentary Friendship Group, especially the Cambodia-Bangladesh Parliamentary Friendship Group visit to Bangladesh at an appropriate time. At the same time, he brought the invitation of the President of the National Assembly of Bangladesh, who also invited the President of the National Assembly to pay an official and friendly visit to Bangladesh.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin accepted the above request and emphasized that Samdech will strive to strengthen the cooperation between the National Assembly of the two countries to be stronger and more comprehensive. Through the Ambassador, Samdech invited the President of the National Assembly of Bangladesh to visit Cambodia and attend the 11th Asia-Europe Parliamentary Partnership Meeting (ASEP) to be hosted by the Cambodian Parliament at the end of 2020. Also.
