The Cambodian Agriculture Reform Project was approved by the World Bank in January 2019 with a total budget of $ 101.67 million, of which the Royal Government contributed $ 10 million over a six-year period (2019-2025) in the province. The 12 targets are Kampong Chhnang, Battambang, Preah Vihear, Siem Reap, Stung Treng, Ratanakiri, Mondulkiri, Kratie, Tbong Khmum, Kampong Cham, Kandal, Kampong Speu and Phnom Penh.
She added that the World Bank will continue to support and support both financially and technically to develop Cambodia's agricultural sector.
Minister Veng Sakhon thanked the World Bank for financing various projects to contribute to the development of Cambodia's agricultural sector from 1997 to the present. As a testament, the project on "Diversification of Cambodia's Agriculture" is a new project that responds to the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy Phase 4, as described in detail, as well as its meaningful and far-reaching initiatives and vision.
He also said that the agricultural sector still plays an important role in sustaining socio-economic growth in rural areas, reducing poverty and ensuring food security.
