Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Reminder was made while allowing 29 young Cambodians who passed the competition to participate in the Southeast Asian and Japanese Youth Ship Program to meet and receive some advice before leaving to participate in the program in the country. Japan.
On this occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen made many remarks on the leadership of building and developing the country to achieve peace and prosperity as at present.
In addition to highlighting the leadership and building of the society, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted the situation in the region and the world, as well as the ASEAN community to provide knowledge to young Cambodians.
The Prime Minister pointed out that there are four priority factors that led Cambodia to decide to join ASEAN. The four priority factors are: 1: ASEAN has a principle of non-interference in internal affairs, 2: ASEAN has a community spirit, that is, ASEAN decides everything in the spirit of consensus, not by election or by sanctions, 3 For the benefit of socio-economic development, ASEAN has many partners and fourth, ASEAN is Cambodia's diplomatic gateway.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister also instructed the 29 youth delegates to prepare to be worthy of Cambodian children, because this delegation represents about 16 million Cambodians across the country and also need to build more friendships to The future can be a good cooperation partner.
It should be noted that the Southeast Asia and Japan Youth Ship Program was established in 1974 by a joint statement of the Government of Japan and the five founding members of ASEAN, including Indonesia, Malaysia, Singapore, the Philippines and Thailand.
Within the framework of ASEAN, the Royal Government of Cambodia has always sent a delegation of Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ships to officially participate in the Southeast Asian and Japanese Youth Ships program every year without interruption. In addition to participating in this program, Cambodia also hosted the two general conventions of the International Association of Southeast Asian Youth Ships in 2007 and 2016 in Siem Reap.
Cambodia has also hosted two Southeast Asian and Japanese Youth Ship programs in 2014 and 2017 in Sihanoukville and Phnom Penh, and delegates were allowed to pay a courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Peace Palace as well.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has always allowed the delegation of youth ships of the Southeast Asian and Japanese Youth Ship Program to meet before leaving.
Allowing the Cambodian youth to meet this courtesy is the greatest encouragement to the youth in the mission of the youth ship delegation, which is a goodwill ambassador and propagandist to promote the rich culture, civilization and real situation of Cambodia. In particular, the demonstration of the real truth through peace, stability and national development in all areas in Cambodia.
North Korea sends message to US: "Patience is limited, restoration of confidence may need to be reconsidered"
SEOUL: North Korea on Thursday said its tolerance is limited and may reconsider restoring relations and trust with the United States. This is according to the release by CNA on the evening of Thursday, October 10, 2019.
In a statement released by state television KCNA, the North Korean Foreign Ministry also condemned the recent US missile test and criticized the UN Security Council's call for North Korea to abandon its nuclear program. Nuclear weapons, too.
"Our tolerance is limited and there is no law governing our tolerance ... but the UN Security Council's unjust decision on self-defense could push," the statement said. "Let us reconsider restoring relations and trust with the United States."
