Senior official of the Council for the Development of Cambodia confirms Cambodia's investment potential and key advantages in attracting investment (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Royal Government always welcomes investors of all nationalities, including local investors. The Cambodian Investment Law does not discriminate against investors in Cambodia and provides all the same treatment.
These are the factors that make Cambodia attractive for investment projects from many countries, with Chinese investment being the most prominent in the last five years, especially from 2016 until August 2019, where these investments do not focus only on the garment, footwear and bag industry.
Chea Vuthy, Deputy Secretary-General of the Cambodian Investment Committee and the Cambodian Special Economic Zone Committee, Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC), speaks at a press conference on "Investment Potential in Cambodia" by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia on the morning of October 10. This October 2019 highlighted Cambodia's investment potential and key advantages as follows:
First, the favorable conditions for peace, political and macroeconomic stability, as well as effective legal, institutional and institutional frameworks, transparency, accountability and predictability.
Second, economic openness for all investors without discrimination between Cambodian and foreign investors. Cambodia allows foreigners to invest 100% in all sectors without the need for shares of local investors, which is Cambodia's most open compared to other countries in the region.
Third, a diverse and young workforce, in which the population over the age of 35 accounts for 72% of the total population, combined with competitive wages.
Fourth, Cambodia has the potential for the development of "cultural and natural" tourism, including cultural treasures, natural resources, historical heritage, as well as the beautiful scenery of beaches, rivers, lakes and national forests, which are attractive for both domestic and foreign tourism markets. And international.
Fifth, Cambodia is in a strategic position in the ASEAN region, which has been becoming a "factory of Asia".
Mr. Chea Vuthy said, "Through the efforts of the Royal Government to put in place measures to improve the business and investment environment, Cambodia will continue to be a potential investment destination and can attract more new investment activities, especially activities. "High value-added investment."
Please be informed that from 2016 to August 2019, the Council for the Development of Cambodia has approved 831 investment projects with a total investment capital of more than 22.5 billion US dollars.
