(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court has ordered the detention of seven Chinese nationals in connection with the severe detention and torture of 10 Chinese nationals in Sihanoukville. This was confirmed by Brigadier General Heng Bunty, Provincial Gendarmerie Commander, to Fresh News on the afternoon of October 10, 2019.
Please note that at more than 11 am on October 6, 2019, a group of Chinese people illegally detained a person (same Chinese) in Sangkat 1, Sihanoukville, but was forced. The military arrested and arrested seven people.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Gendarmerie Commander Brigadier General Heng Bunty told Fresh News that in this case, his forces were under the coordination of the prosecution and under the command of General Sao Sokha, National Gendarmerie Commander and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun. The Chairman of the Provincial Unity Command launched an operation to crack down on the crime of detention and torture of the same 10 Chinese nationals in Sangkat 1, Sihanoukville.
The commander added that the 10 male victims were detained by the assailants and their accomplices and severely tortured, causing serious injuries, and were rushed to the hospital. All seven suspects were handcuffed.
It should be noted that on the same day, in Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, an ethnic man was dragged out of a car by three assailants and shot dead, but two suspects (a woman) were beaten by police. Arrested immediately.
