This statement was made by a senior official of the Council for the Development of Cambodia on the occasion of the press conference of the Royal Government of Cambodia held a press conference on "Investment Potential in Cambodia" this morning, October 10, 2019 at the office of the Council. Minister.
Chea Vuthy said that on the basis of strong peace and political stability over the last two decades, Cambodia has achieved an average annual economic growth of around 7.7% and has left the status of a rich country. Low income to low middle income country in 2015.
"In the field of investment, Cambodia has also achieved excellent results, from 2016 to August 2019, the Council for the Development of Cambodia has approved 831 investment projects with a total investment of more than 22 $ 5 billion.
Mr. Chea Vuthy added that from year to year, investment activities have increased steadily, both in terms of number of projects and investment capital. In fact, the Council for the Development of Cambodia approved 171 investment projects with an investment capital of about 3.6 billion US dollars in 2016, 183 projects with an investment capital of 6.3 billion US dollars in 2017, and 255 projects. With an investment of 6.4 billion US dollars in 2018.
During the same period, investment activities in SEZs also increased steadily, with 42 investment projects in SEZs in 2016 with an investment capital of approximately 283 million US dollars. In 2017, there were 47 projects with an investment capital of 484 million US dollars, and in 2018, there were 79 projects with an investment capital of 442 million US dollars.
In the first eight months of 2019, there were 222 investment projects with an investment capital of over 6 billion US dollars, an increase of 81 projects and an investment capital of 1.88 billion US dollars compared to the same period last year. Same time in 2018. In the special economic zone, there are 71 investment projects with an investment capital of 578 million US dollars, an increase of 26 projects and an investment capital of 19 million US dollars.
Mr. Chea Vuthy noted that "As of August 2019, there are 23 special economic zones in operation, including 482 investment projects with an investment of more than 3.6 billion US dollars. Exports originating from special economic zones will account for about 15% of the Kingdom's total export volume in 2018.
Along with the growth of overall investment activity, which has been steadily increasing from 2016 to August 2019, the most prominent investment activities in the sector are tourism, which accounted for 47%, infrastructure 24%, Industry and manufacturing 23%, and agriculture and agro-industry 6% of total investment.
He added that in the first eight months of 2019, the number of investment projects in industry and manufacturing increased significantly, while investment in tourism increased by more than 94% compared to the same period last year. 2018. In particular, investment figures in agriculture and agro-industry, infrastructure and other sectors have declined.
Farmer woman in Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province wins 100 million Riel prize from Echitan green tea
(Phnom Penh): An elderly woman named But Sophoan, 53 years old, a farmer and a dishwasher and now a resident of Chong Boeng village in Dambok commune, Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province, was lucky to win 100 million Riels. Green Echinacea.
In front of the team that handed over the grand prize to the house in the above geography, Ms. But Sophoan described that today, the standard of living of her family is very poor because there is no business other than a little farming and Working as a dishwasher at occasional festivals or weddings only earns a living.
She went on to say that winning 100 million Riel now is the most surprising thing, as last weekend, after washing the dishes for the festival and coming home feeling exhausted. The force also uses his son to buy echinacea green tea, a bottle of lemon tea, honey from a vendor near his house to drink.
When you open the bottle cap, you suddenly see a prize of 100 million riels. Suddenly, she did not seem to believe and called her son-daughter and relatives to help check to find out that she really won 100 million Riel and called the company through the existing phone number. Bottle cap.
She stated that the prize money of 100 million Riel is very important for her and after receiving the prize money of 100 million Riel, she will take some to build debt and leave some for her children to study and build a house. Suitable for living in the future.
(Siem Reap): All ASEAN Environment Ministers have expressed concern over the seriousness of transboundary smog pollution and the recent spread of smog, which is affecting some ASEAN countries, especially in ASEAN. North and South of ASEAN.
The ASEAN Environment Ministers in charge of Environment, Land, Forest Fires and Smog from ASEAN Member States acknowledged the recent achievements and developments in environmental protection in the region and regional cooperation on a number of environmental issues, in particular. Prioritize activities and initiatives on environmental sustainability, as well as promoting environmental cooperation in the region.
The ASEAN Environment Ministers also expressed their condolences to the millions of people affected by the cross-border smog. The ASEAN Environment Ministers noted and appreciated the efforts of ASEAN members and the assistance provided by countries to control wildfires and cross-border smog.
ASEAN members pledged to continue to closely monitor and set up mechanisms to increase efforts to prevent smog and minimize cross-border smog problems during the The coming dry season.
The ASEAN Environment Ministers noted the efforts of the Conference Parties on the Transboundary Haze Agreement, which has been active in providing and providing services to the ASEAN region in relation to meteorological and weather forecasting and monitoring and information. Urgently warn of cross-border smog pollution. The ASEAN Environment Ministers also proposed capacity building and equipment upgrades to monitor climate change.
The ASEAN Environment Ministers proposed initiatives as well as activities implemented by ASEAN Member States and noted with appreciation the continued efforts to strengthen national capacity for regional activities and cooperation in accessing information. Prevention and control and management of land and forest fires and smog control.
