Seeing that money in the economic sector is a policy tool to stimulate economic growth, strengthen the resilience of the economy to risks, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has set out five key recommendations for the National Bank of Cambodia, the backbone of The national economy has achieved more significant achievements.
The five main recommendations of Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government are:
Second, the National Bank of Cambodia, all institutions and stakeholders must continue to support and implement the financial sector development plan 2016-2025 and the strategy on the environment in Cambodia effectively and consistently to support national economic growth, continue to contribute to poverty reduction and Improve people's living standards in line with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy.
Third, the National Bank of Cambodia, as well as relevant institutions, must continue to support the use of new technologies that make financial services in Cambodia more modern, easy to access, low cost and high efficiency. The risks of all these new technologies need to be monitored to maintain the stability and development of the financial sector in Cambodia.
Fourth, the National Bank of Cambodia, relevant institutions and financial institutions must continue to raise financial awareness to the people, must continue to increase awareness and strengthen the credit culture for those who are using financial services, especially in rural areas to prevent Risks that may occur eventually, now and in the future.
Fifth, the National Bank of Cambodia, the Financial Intelligence Unit of Cambodia, the Ministry of Economy and Finance and all stakeholders, the Anti-Corruption Unit, the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Justice must continue to work closely to strengthen the timely and effective prevention. Clearing money and terrorist financing to protect the financial sector, banking, transparency and good governance.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Prime Minister said that the National Bank of Cambodia has maintained the value of the riel, which fluctuated within only 1% with the increase of international reserves to a high level, which these results show the effectiveness of Manage the supply of the riel and the accumulation of national wealth better to keep prices stable with a low inflation rate of about 3%.
