This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the 40th Anniversary of the Re-Establishment of the National Bank of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presides over the 40th anniversary of the establishment of the Bank on Thursday, October 10, 2019. Nationalization of Cambodia (October 10, 1979 - October 10, 2019).
The event will be held at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall with the participation of about 600 members of the National Assembly, the Senate and the Royal Government, leaders of banking and financial institutions, diplomats, representatives of national and international organizations, leaders and officials of the National Bank of Cambodia.
The National Bank of Cambodia was re-established on October 10, 1979, after the genocidal regime of Pol Pot was overthrown. After the re-establishment, the National Bank of Cambodia has been restored from scratch and has successfully gone through many stages of development, and to date, the National Bank of Cambodia has steadily strengthened with 19 capital-provincial branches throughout the country. To ensure an efficient and reliable monetary and banking system.
Meanwhile, the banking sector has developed rapidly, especially in the last two decades, and has actively contributed to supporting economic growth and reducing poverty. Modernization of financial infrastructure, especially payment systems, is also regularly focused on reducing operating costs, enhancing payment efficiency and security.
Please note that the National Bank of Cambodia is the central bank of Cambodia and the monetary authority and regulator of the banking system in Cambodia. The main mission of the National Bank of Cambodia is to determine and lead monetary policy in order to maintain price stability in order to contribute to the development of the national economy in consultation with the Royal Government within the political, economic and financial framework of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
As a monetary authority, the National Bank of Cambodia has the exclusive right to issue the riel, the national currency. The National Bank of Cambodia maintains monetary stability. As the regulatory authority of the National Bank of Cambodia, the issuer and revocation of licenses, regulations and supervision of banking and financial institutions in Cambodia.
In addition, the National Bank of Cambodia regularly analyzes the economic and monetary situation, publishes reports and bulletins, monitors the national payment system, installs statistics, balances accounts, and participates in foreign debt and credit management.
The National Bank of Cambodia was established on December 23, 1954, after gaining independence from the French colony. Between 1975 and 1979, the National Bank of Cambodia was shut down by the Democratic Kampuchea (Khmer Rouge) regime. Headquarters were demolished, the national currency was decommissioned and the banking system was completely abolished.
The National Bank of Cambodia was re-established on October 10, 1979, after the country was liberated from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot. Between 1979 and 1993, the National Bank of Cambodia was rebuilt from scratch. At the same time, the national currency was reissued.
From 1993 to the present, the banking system has been steadily strengthened and modernized. Cambodia has also become one of the fastest growing economies in the world.
At present, the National Bank of Cambodia has Mr. Chea Chanto as the Governor-General and has a total of 1,384 employees. Ministry of Economy is continuing the training campaign on technical skills training for public financial management for more than 1,000 target trainees
