Cambodian Human Rights Committee-UN Holds Workshop on Dissemination and Implementation of the Third Round of UPR Recommendations 2019
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Human Rights Committee (CCHR) and the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia on October 9, 2019 co-organized a national workshop. First, the dissemination and implementation of the Universal Periodic Review (UPR) Recommendation Round 3 2019.
The workshop will be held for one and a half days on October 9 and 10, 2019 at Himawari Hotel, Phnom Penh. National and international civil society, including a total of 200 development partners, and for the following purposes:
* First: Increase the understanding of the UPR mechanism and Cambodia's participation in the UPR process to all stakeholders * Second: Distribute and determine the 173 recommendations to the ministries in charge to implement * Third: Provide a forum for Civil society groups and relevant development partners participate and advise on the distribution and implementation of these 173 recommendations.
The workshop will last for one and a half days, with the first day disseminating the UPR recommendations to all stakeholders and discussing the distribution of recommendations to the relevant ministries and institutions for implementation. The second day focused on the implementation of an action plan to implement the 173 recommendations, with a presentation and guidance from UPR Info experts from Geneva.
The workshop was co-organized by the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, the United Nations in Cambodia and UPR Info from Geneva and lasted for one and a half days. Involve and discuss and distribute recommendations to relevant institutions to implement.
Day 2: One morning, with the participation of the inter-ministerial working group at the technical level and the working group of CCHR focused on the implementation plan of the implementation of the 173 recommendations, with the participation of the presentation of UPR Info experts from Geneva.
