The following are the meaningful remarks of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that remembering this difficult situation, Cambodia is very proud of its development over the past 40 years.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the people are really proud of Cambodia's progress because what Cambodia has now does not inherit from previous generations.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that in order to use banknotes, they had to be issued abroad, and it was not until the 1990s that small machines were available for printing banknotes.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it was very difficult after becoming the Prime Minister in 1985 and until the Second Kingdom in the first mandate, there was still a lack of cash to open for civil servants.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen spoke about the difficult situation of life in Cambodia after the liberation from the genocidal regime without paper money for people to use to exchange goods with each other.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech was almost in danger of changing the market regime in Cambodia from a planned market to a free market. Samdech Techo added that it is very difficult to lead the reform.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the reforms of the 1980s were the most shocking.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the 1980s, he launched two major reforms: political and economic reform.
* Samdech Techo stated that political reform is the goal of achieving peace talks for Cambodia. Samdech confirmed that Samdech decided to change the Minister of Defense, Koy Buntha, who refused to negotiate, saying that if the negotiations are equal to the abandonment of the achievements of the state of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it is not possible to jump from a planned economy to a market economy immediately.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that his reforms were successful thanks to the support of Samdech Chea Sim, Samdech Heng Samrin, Say Phu Thong and other top party leaders.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that his reforms came from below.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reacted to some people always mentioned that the puppet of Vietnam. But when Vietnam had an army in Cambodia, Vietnam never ordered Samdech to do anything. In contrast, some foreigners often give orders with conditions and assistance.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the presence of Vietnamese troops in Cambodia in the 1980s was not an obstacle to Samdech's reforms.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterated that there were three repressive forces that endangered Samdech's reforms, including: First: Disagreements within the internal state of Cambodia, Second: Vietnam did not withdraw its troops Cambodia will not yet be reformed. Fortunately, Vietnam did not interfere in Cambodia's internal affairs, and third, the Soviet Union and Eastern Europe were able to cut off aid from the Cambodian government at the time.
* Samdech Techo thanked the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party and the people who have supported the idea of change at all stages of Samdech to stand strong for more than 40 years.
* Samdech Techo stated that the market economy in Cambodia did not occur after the Paris Peace Accords of October 23, 1991.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the 1980s, many countries imposed economic sanctions on Cambodia, and the countries that shouted the strongest economic sanctions did the most business with Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the game of punishment can not kill any country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that achievements come from difficulties and self-effort is to pay attention to protection.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the world, there are countries that change regimes, but they only change political leaders, but there is no abolition of the system of governing the country like in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo said that there are countries in the world that have changed regimes, but there is no abolition of the use of banknotes like in Cambodia.
* The Prime Minister stated that Cambodia has an efficient banking system, environment and high integration into the region and internationally, as well as meet the needs of a wider range of financial services throughout the country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the banking sector has become a pillar in supporting the national economic growth. At the same time, the national and international community has recognized the central role of the banking sector in contributing to macroeconomic stability, financial stability, improving living standards and reducing poverty, especially through the microfinance sector.
* Samdech Techo stated that the National Bank of Cambodia has maintained the value of the riel, which fluctuated within only 1%, with the increase of international reserves to a high level, which shows the effectiveness of money supply management. Riel and better accumulation of national assets to keep prices stable, with a low inflation rate of about 3%.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the banking sector has expanded to provide financial services to people across the country, especially the poor, to improve their lives, of which 71% of the adult population is receiving services. Finance and financing through the banking system have increased to 115% of GDP to meet the needs of business expansion in all sectors.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that through credit to the banking sector, Cambodians have the opportunity to expand their business, have a better life and buy affordable housing, which is an important contribution to socio-economic development and social harmony. The whole nation.
* Samdech Techo stated that the banking sector has expanded to provide financial services to people across the country, especially the poor to improve their lives, of which 71% of the adult population is receiving financial services. And financing through the banking system has increased to 115% of GDP to meet the needs of business expansion in all sectors.
* Samdech Techo stated that Samdech has authorized the construction of a new building of the National Bank of Cambodia on the old site. Samdech Techo added that Samdech is proud that Cambodia has a printing house for printing its own riel currency in its own country, while some countries in the region do not yet have access.
* Samdech Techo stated that the currency in the economic sector is a policy tool to stimulate economic growth, strengthen the resilience of the economy to risks.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order for the National Bank of Cambodia, the backbone of the national economy to achieve more important achievements, I would like to make the following recommendations:
Second, the National Bank of Cambodia, all institutions and stakeholders must continue to support and implement the financial sector development plan 2016-2025 and the strategy on the environment in Cambodia effectively and consistently to support national economic growth, continue to contribute to reducing Poverty and improve the living standards of the people in line with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy.
Third, the National Bank of Cambodia, as well as related institutions, must continue to support the use of new technologies that make financial services in Cambodia more modern, easy to access, low cost and high efficiency. The risks of all these new technologies need to be monitored to maintain the stability and development of the financial sector in Cambodia.
Fourth, the National Bank of Cambodia, related institutions and financial institutions must continue to raise the financial awareness of the people, must continue to contribute to increase awareness and strengthen the credit culture for those who are using financial services, especially in rural areas. To prevent potential risks, current and future.
Fifth, the National Bank of Cambodia, the Financial Intelligence Unit of Cambodia, the Ministry of Economy and Finance and all stakeholders, the Anti-Corruption Unit, the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Justice must continue to work closely to strengthen timely prevention. Effective money laundering and terrorist financing for transparent banking and transparency and good governance.
