Japan supports strengthening marine waste reduction capacity in ASEAN and ASEAN Green Activities
(Siem Reap): Japan has announced its support for capacity building for marine waste reduction in the ASEAN region, support for the World Bank Green ASEAN and the ASEAN-Norway Cooperation Project on strengthening local capacity for reducing plastic pollution in the region. ASEAN and so on.
At the meeting, the ASEAN Environment Ministers met with their dialogue partners from China, Japan and South Korea to discuss future cooperation strategies such as biodiversity, climate change, environmental education, environmental science and sustainable urban technology. And controlling marine pollution by plastic waste and other issues.
At the same time, the ASEAN Environment Ministers acknowledged that urgent and interconnected environmental issues such as climate change and marine pollution remain challenges that require joint action in the region.
The ASEAN Environment Ministers agreed to meet again in the Philippines in 2020 at the ASEAN Summit on the Transboundary Pollution Control Agreement and in Indonesia in 2021 on Of the 17th ASEAN Environment Ministers Meeting and related meetings.
Overall, the 15th ASEAN Environment Ministers 'Meeting was remarkably fruitful on the occasion that Cambodia hosted the 15th ASEAN Environment Ministers' Meeting.
Japan seems to want to play a role in reducing the plastic waste that is polluting the earth, especially in the sea, and in order to achieve this environmental goal, Japan will try to persuade the G20 to adopt an international agreement.
