In the first 9 months of 2019, the APSARA Authority Community Working Group approved the repair of 879 cases of houses and small structures of Angkor residents
(Siem Reap): According to the report of the Community Secretariat of APSARA Authority, in the first 9 months of 2019, the community working group of APSARA Authority has granted permission to renovate 879 houses in the Angkor resort area.
The above permits were issued to 106 cases in Prasat Bakong district, 115 cases in Angkor Thom district, 185 cases in Puok district, 167 cases in Banteay Srei district and 306 cases in Siem Reap city.
Mr. Oeun Sam On, Director of the Community Secretariat, said that in the past nine months, people have applied for 1,746 cases of home improvement to the APSARA Authority, of which 879 cases have been approved by the working group.
This permit is based on the principle of housing management in accordance with the conditions of conservation of World Heritage sites.
