Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the 40th Anniversary of the Re-Establishment of the National Bank of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the celebration of the 40th anniversary of the establishment of the Cambodian People's Liberation Army (PLA) in the morning of Thursday, October 10, 2019. Establishment of the National Bank of Cambodia (October 10, 1979 - October 10, 2019).
Please note that the National Bank of Cambodia is the central bank of Cambodia and the monetary authority and regulator of the banking system in Cambodia. The main mission of the National Bank of Cambodia is to determine and lead monetary policy in order to maintain price stability in order to contribute to the national economic development in consultation with the Royal Government within the political, economic and financial framework of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
As a monetary authority, the National Bank of Cambodia has the exclusive right to issue the riel, the national currency. The National Bank of Cambodia maintains monetary stability. As the regulatory authority of the National Bank of Cambodia, it provides and revokes licenses, issues regulations and oversees banking and financial institutions in Cambodia.
The National Bank of Cambodia was established on December 23, 1954, after gaining independence from the French colony. Between 1975 and 1979, the National Bank of Cambodia was shut down by the Democratic Kampuchea (Khmer Rouge) regime. Headquarters were demolished, the national currency was decommissioned, and the banking system was completely abolished.
At present, the National Bank of Cambodia has Mr. Chea Chanto as the Governor-General and has a total of 1,384 employees. Notice! The National Social Security Fund for Civil Servants will pay in October for the first two weeks from October 11.
