Cambodia-EU vows to continue partnership to make the investment climate in Cambodia more attractive to the European Union
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia and the European Union are committed to continuing their partnership in addressing any requests or concerns to ensure that the investment climate in Cambodia remains attractive, especially to the European Union.
The positions of both sides were expressed through Dr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, on the occasion of allowing the European Chamber of Commerce delegation led by Mr. Arnaud DARC, President of the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia to pay a courtesy call and Discuss in detail the contents of the chapter on human resources of the "White" book of the European Chamber of Commerce 2019 and request recommendations in the morning of October 9, 2019 at the Ministry.
Mr. Ngoy Rith added that during the meeting, the European Chamber of Commerce also raised the issue of the Ministry of Labor creating a number of qualifications to increase the attractiveness of investors. In particular, Europe is full of things that facilitate the various procedures related to the field of employment and vocational training.
He said that "what the Chamber of Commerce wants to know is 1: the organization in the establishment requires a nursery, 2: training apprentices, 3: the process of setting up a modern online system to apply to foreigners who use staff. Foreigners, 4: Learn about the new laws that the Ministry applies, including the National Social Security Fund.
Mr. Ngoy Rith said that the Chamber of Commerce was pleased with the new information for the White Book. The information received by the business community because in the past, the Chamber of Commerce has played an important role in helping to attract investors from the European Union to Cambodia to another level.
The Minister said that the labor sector is very important in the management of human resources to facilitate trade. When an investor does not understand the law, he is worried and ambiguous, he can not invest softly at risk.
According to Mr. Ngoy Rith, the points written in the book "S" will be written clearly to tell the investors to understand before investing in Cambodia. He said that during the meeting, the Minister requested the Chamber of Commerce to continue its efforts in partnership with the Ministry of Labor, which in the past the Chamber of Commerce has done a lot of work to ensure the soft investment environment of the European Union.
"In the past, it was part of the European Chamber of Commerce that has played this role and worked well with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training," he said. Please continue that good cooperation, especially in the development of Cambodia's human resources related to human resource training, apprenticeship in the labor law, which is part of promoting the increase of human resources.
