This Victory Monument is a testament to the happiness of people from all walks of life, established by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. A man walks over a rice field with his right leg amputated
(Pursat): A man was seriously injured when he went to look at the rice fields in his field and stepped on a landmine, causing his right leg to explode, and his family sent him to Trat Provincial Hospital. Thailand at 8:30 am on October 8, 2019 at point 85 in Ekpheap village, Thmor Da commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
According to the report of the Veal Veng District Police Inspectorate, the victim who lost one leg due to stepping on a landmine was Chhorn Virak, a 39-year-old Cambodian man living in Ekpheap Village, Thmor Da Commune, Veal Veng District, Pursat Province. .
The victim is currently being treated at a hospital in Trat, Thailand, and is recovering well, the report said. Three draft laws were unanimously approved by the National Assembly today
(Phnom Penh): Three draft laws, which are full-day agenda for the third session of the sixth legislature on the morning of October 8, 2019, have been fully approved by the National Assembly.
These draft laws include: the draft law on e-commerce, the draft law on consumer protection and the draft law on social security.
Today's plenary session of the National Assembly was chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, with the participation of 108 members of the National Assembly.
The draft law on consumer protection, which has 11 chapters and 51 articles, will be the law for protecting the interests of consumers from the actions and misconduct of traders in business activities to protect the rights and interests of consumers. Support the market to be competitive in terms of price, quality of goods and services.
17 tons of rice seeds distributed to farmers in Tambor district
(Tbong Khmum): About 17 tons of rice seeds were distributed to 168 families in Tbong Khmum province's Tambor district by the National Committee for Disaster Management (NCDD) after their rice was submerged. Damage by floods.
This rice seed was distributed by Mr. Lam Heng Huot, Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, on behalf of Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management on Tuesday afternoon, October 8, 2019. The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Mam Amnath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture and Mr. Kun Sophea, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum, as well as other relevant officials.
The governor of Tambor district said that the floods in the rainy season this year affected two communes and affected about 172 hectares of rice fields.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, recently reminded the National Committee for Disaster Management to immediately distribute rice seeds to farmers for further cultivation.
People expressed their happiness after receiving rice seeds for further cultivation. They also thanked Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for always thinking about their well-being and difficulties. Senior Minister Kun Kim Continues to Distribute Rice Seed to Farmers in Tbong Khmum District
(Tbong Khmum): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, continues to distribute 23 tons of rice seeds to 285 families in Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province for further cultivation after their rice was damaged by Past floods.
The distribution of rice seeds took place in Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province on Tuesday, October 8, 2019 with the participation of Mr. Lam Heng Huot, Deputy Chairman of NCDD. Mr. Mam Amnot, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture and Mr. Kun Sophea, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province.
According to the district governor, this year's floods affected six communes and affected about 200 hectares of rice fields. The Senior Minister said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, recently reminded the National Committee for Disaster Management to immediately distribute rice seeds to farmers. Continued cultivation.
The Senior Minister brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who always pays attention to the well-being of the people who are suffering, the poor, the sick, the vulnerable and the victims of various disasters. Regret the victims of the floods that caused damage to crops and property in the past.
With a happy face, the people who received the rice seeds donated by Samdech Techo expressed their deep gratitude to the two Samdechs who always thought of them. President of the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia led a delegation to meet with the Minister of Agriculture to discuss business in agriculture
He said the EuroCham Agricultural Business Committee was set up in 2018 after members of the Chamber of Commerce expressed strong interest in the food processing and agriculture sectors. In this new chapter, there are 5 main topics, including: 1- Prohibited substances, 2- Fighting against illegal agricultural materials, 3- Labor regulations 4- Agricultural diversification and 5. Water testing in agriculture according to legal requirements.
He said that in each topic, the Committee on Agricultural Business has made important recommendations to the General Department behind the roof of the Ministry to take into consideration and improve any shortcomings or problems. To improve the environment for doing business in agriculture based on the principles of law, technology, transparency, quality, safety and competition, etc.
On that occasion, the members of the working group also raised some issues related to the implementation of the law on animal health and animal production, the importation and exploitation of illegal agricultural equipment, the approval of the minimum wage, the standardization of hybrid rice cultivation and the requirements of The Ministry of Environment, which requires agricultural businesses to test water quality directly at the Ministry of Environment.
Minister Veng Sakhon briefed the delegation on the above five topics, and then allowed the officials and those in charge of technical work related to this topic to continue to explain in more detail to the delegation.
However, the Minister acknowledged that there are still some challenges in doing agribusiness, which the Ministry as well as relevant institutions are considering to find appropriate, timely and effective solutions to maintain the investment climate in the agribusiness sector. To be better both now and in the future.
