Mr. Pa Socheatvong was elected by the General Assembly as the President of the National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils for the second mandate.
(Phnom Penh): On October 08, 2019, the National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils organized the second general assembly by electing Mr. Pa Socheatvong, Chairman of the Phnom Penh Capital Council, along with 12 other Vice-Chairmen. 273 out of 278 votes in favor.
As a result of the General Assembly, Mr. Pa Socheatvong, President of the Phnom Penh Capital Council of the third mandate, will become the third President of the National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils, which was established in March 2013. The first chairman is Mr. Nam Tum, former chairman of Kampong Thom Provincial Council, first mandate, and the second chairman is Mr. Mop Sarin, former chairman of Phnom Penh Capital Council, first and second mandates.
The 12 Vice Presidents of the 3rd National Association include:
A total of 410 participants in the General Assembly, including 280 delegates from the Capital and Provincial Councils, including 275 from the Cambodian People's Party, 3 from the Khmer United National Party and 2 from FUNCINPEC.
The National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils was established through the 1st General Assembly on March 27-28, 2013 in order to enhance the status, develop the capacity and protect the legitimate interests of the councils that are members of the National Association. Phnom Penh Capital Council and 24 provincial councils.
