The National Assembly fully approves the draft law on e-commerce (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Finally, the draft law on e-commerce, which has 12 chapters and 67 articles, is a new important draft law. The National Assembly has finally approved in the plenary session on October 08, 2019.
Please be informed that the draft law on e-commerce was approved by the Council of Ministers at the plenary session of the Council of Ministers on July 12, 2019. The draft law on e-commerce consists of 12 chapters and 67 articles. As follows:
Chapter 3 The process of electronic communication has 4 articles (from Article 15 to Article 18) This Chapter 3 stipulates the time and place of sending and receiving information in electronic communication. Errors of entering information in electronic communications.
Chapter 4 defines electronic electronic signatures and secure electronic signatures in five articles (Articles 19 to 23). Chapter 4 deals with secure electronic records, secure electronic signatures, assumptions related to secure electronic records and signatures, identity theft, and the competent authority governing security procedures.
Chapter 5 Intermediaries and Individuals Providing Electronic Business Services There are 5 Articles (Articles 24 to 28). This Chapter 5 deals with the responsibilities of intermediaries and individuals providing e-commerce services, information or facts, the issuance of licenses or licenses, professional ethics and regulations for intermediaries and service providers. E-commerce and tax obligations, incentives and favors.
Chapter 6 Consumer Protection has 5 articles (from Article 29 to Article 33). This Chapter 6 deals with the minimum information on e-commerce, business communications that do not require the establishment of fraudulent electronic systems and malicious codes, data protection and the implementation of consumer protection regulations. The activities and operations of the state electronically have 1 article (Article 34)
Chapter 7 deals with the recognition of electronic communications by state institutions.
Chapter 9: Payment and / or electronic money transfer has 3 articles (from Article 46 to Article 48). Chapter 9 deals with electronic payment transactions, the responsibilities of the payment service provider and the responsibilities of the customer.
Chapter 10: Competence, Complaints and Procedures for Fines There are 3 articles (from Article 49 to Article 51). Chapter 10 stipulates the competence, procedure of complaint and procedure of fine.
Chapter 12: Final Provisions There are two articles (from Article 66 to Article 67). Chapter 12 deals with the repeal of laws and regulations that are contrary to this law and the implementation of this law.
Chairman of Wat Prek Touch pagoda in Saang district, Kandal province, has been charged with insulting monks at a pagoda
(Kandal): Mr. Him Bunnara, Chairman of the Prek Touch Pagoda Commission in Prek Run Krom Village, Prek Koy Commune, Saang District, Kandal Province, received a complaint from a member of the pagoda subordinate committee accusing him of insulting monks at Prek Touch Preah Pagoda. Nam Vanrath in front of the Buddhists who came to the 12th Ben on September 25, 2019 at more than 11 noon.
According to the people, the pagoda committee and the monks themselves said that the chairman of the pagoda committee insulted the monks using all kinds of obscene words, which made the people and the members of the pagoda committee turn. Expressed outrage as he served as chairman of the pagoda commission and as a permanent member of the Economic, Social and Cultural Council with the same status as undersecretary of state.
This insult made them so upset that they even filed a complaint to the director of the Saang district cult office, the chief of Saang district and the district governor to help find justice and ask the authorities and Professional officers fired this person from the chairman of Wat Prek Touch commission.
As the leader of the shift group that brings people to take turns at this pagoda, he is not satisfied with that person, so he asks his superiors to help him find justice, because it will have a bad effect on Buddhist monks if Unresolved, next year, as the chairman of the shift and ask to take the turn, stop taking the turn Ben.
Mr. Van Eng, a resident of Prek Khmer village, Saang Phnom commune, Saang district, Kandal province, the father of the victim monk, also demanded that the authorities and professional officials help find justice in connection with insulting his son-in-law monk.
Preah Chao Athikar Wat Prek Touch, Sambath Thommo I Sambath, also issued three letters dated October 2, 2019 to the Saang District Governor, Saang District Cult Office Chief and Saang District Chief regarding the case. It was confirmed that the name Him Bonnara had indeed insulted the monk named Vanrath.
Regarding this case, Mr. Nhim Vandin, Governor of Saang District, said by telephone on the morning of October 8, 2019 that he had indeed seen and received the complaint, but he was mediating the case.
However, the people of Nhom, the monks and the pagoda committee still refused and insisted that the authorities and professional officials help find justice and expel this person from the pagoda and stop being the chairman of the pagoda committee. Also.
