Earlier this week, a Ho Chi Minh City court sentenced eight people to death, including seven men and a woman, who were members of a network of drug smugglers from the central Vietnamese city of Da Nang to the city. Ho Chi Minh City in the south of the country. Meanwhile, Vietnamese police are pursuing other possible suspects.
According to Vietnamese law, anyone who smuggles 600 grams or more of heroin or more than 2.5 kilograms of methamphetamine will be sentenced to death. In addition, the production or trafficking of heroin weighing 100 grams or other drugs weighing 300 grams or more also carries the death penalty. However, despite such strict drug laws in Vietnam, drug crimes are still common.
