Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth urges ASEAN Environment Minister to urgently address illegal cross-border waste, especially plastic waste (Video inside) (Siem Reap): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, on October 08 This 2019 has urged all ASEAN Environment Ministers to pay more attention to, consider and urgently address the flow of illegal cross-border waste, especially plastic waste.
Such encouragement by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth was made on October 08, 2019 on the occasion that he was invited to represent Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the official opening ceremony of the 15th meeting. ASEAN Environment Ministers and related meetings 2019 hosted by Cambodia in Siem Reap.
The meeting was attended by Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, a delegation of representatives of the ASEAN Ministry of Environment and officials of relevant institutions, a total of about 400 people.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth considers the flow of illegal cross-border waste, especially plastic waste, as a threat to the country's ecosystem, health, well-being, as well as the country's tourism attraction.
"We need to arrange for information sharing, strengthen cooperation among institutions and partnerships with countries that are the source of waste to stop this illegal flow from the country of origin," he said.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth also urged the ASEAN Working Group on Chemicals and Waste to prioritize this issue and provide specific measures in the near future to respond to this common problem in a spirit of cooperation and cooperation. .
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth called on all ASEAN countries to make joint efforts to raise awareness of environmental protection and biodiversity conservation by recognizing the importance of conservation efforts in Biodiversity protection.
The Deputy Prime Minister also called for more efforts to accelerate cooperation and expand cooperation among ASEAN member countries and partners in order to effectively respond to the increase in marine litter.
