The 15th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Environment in Siem Reap Province
(Siem Reap): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of October 08, 2019, officially opened the 15th Meeting of ASEAN Environment Ministers and Relevant meetings 2019 hosted by Cambodia.
The meeting was attended by the Minister of Environment, a delegation of representatives of the ASEAN Ministry of Environment and officials of relevant institutions, a total of about 400 people.
Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said that after the official opening ceremony and the planting of cactus at the Siem Reap Cactus Garden in front of Angkor Wat in the morning, the ASEAN Environment Ministers will begin the first meeting. 15 in the afternoon to review cooperation in the field of environment and natural resources within ASEAN members.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra pointed out that the ASEAN Environment Ministers' Meeting, chaired by Cambodia and Indonesia, will discuss issues related to climate change, urban sustainability, biodiversity conservation, coastal environment, environmental education, water resources management, and management. Chemicals and hazardous wastes, pollution control, transboundary smog, etc.
Within the framework of this meeting, Cambodia will host the 3rd ASEAN Environmental Friendship School Award Ceremony and the 1st ASEAN Environmental Friendship Youth Excellence Award for all ASEAN Member States through the ASEAN-Japan Integration Fund, chaired by Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment of Cambodia, chaired the meeting and Minister of Environment of ASEAN.
On October 9, 2019, the third day of the 15th Meeting of the ASEAN Conference on Transboundary Haze Pollution.
Please be informed that the ASEAN Environment Ministers' Meeting is held every two years for the purpose of discussing environmental cooperation in the region. The 14th ASEAN Environment Ministers' Meeting and related meetings, including meetings with dialogue partners, were held in September 2017 in the host country Brunei.
