On October 05, 2019, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training issued a new notification allowing foreigners in Cambodia to re-engage in self-employment, ie to be able to engage in self-employment or non-related work. Wages.
This declaration reiterates the decision of the Ministry of Labor to ban all foreigners from doing business and doing 10 kinds of work in Cambodia on August 28, 2019.
On October 7, 2019, 54 unions, associations, communities and civil society organizations expressed their disappointment with the declaration on "re-authorization of self-employment activities by foreigners". They consider that allowing foreigners to engage in self-employment is an opportunity for foreigners to "take over the jobs of workers and the Cambodian people."
Heng Sour, a spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, dismissed the joint statement, stating: "The lifting of the ban requires all foreigners to comply with other applicable laws." "Such as the Law on Trade Rules and Business Registration, which requires the registration of businesses in the form of traffic laws, as well as to respect the rules of public order in Cambodia."
He confirmed that the new decision of the Ministry of Labor was made after a request from the private sector, which is a major source of investment in Cambodia.
Kampong Cham Police Crack Down on Illegal Fishing in Kang Meas and Koh Sotin Districts
(Kampong Cham): On October 7, 2019, the joint police force of Kampong Cham province launched an operation to crack down on illegal fishing in 2 targets in Kang Meas and Koh Sotin districts, confiscated some exhibits and released the young fish into the natural lake. 300 kg.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Em Kosal, confirmed that the first location: cracked down on Prek Sanday in Damnak Pring Keut village, Mohaleap commune, Koh Sotin district, Kampong Cham province. Koh Sotin District Local Authority.
As a result, the police confiscated 15 nets, a 450-meter-long mosquito net, 215 bamboo poles, and released 36 kilograms of mixed fish into the natural lake. For the above exhibits, with the permission of Mr. Huot Wutty, Prosecutor of Kampong Cham Provincial Court, the police set up a committee to destroy and burn on the spot.
Location 2: He assigned the Economic Crimes Police Office in cooperation with the Kang Meas District Police Inspectorate, local authorities, Boeung B6 Community Force and People's Defense Force to crack down on illegal fishing at Chroy Krabao I village, Prek Liv IV village. Svay Sranos I, Chroy Krabao 2 village, Khchao village 3, Varin 1 village in Rokar Ar commune, Kang Meas district, Kampong Cham province (Boeung B6).
As a result, 65 nets were removed, 550 meters of nets were changed, 65 poles were erected, and 250 kilograms of fish were released back into the natural lake. For the above exhibits, the authorities burned them with the approval of the Prosecutor of Kampong Cham Provincial Court.
