Ministry of Posts and Ministries of Economy jointly disseminate the implementation of sub-decree on non-tax revenue management
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and the Ministry of Economy and Finance jointly organized a workshop on October 7, 2019 to disseminate the implementation of the sub-decree on non-tax revenue management to the public. This workshop was organized with the participation of Mr. Tram Itek, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications.
The sub-decree on the management of non-tax revenue was established with the aim of ensuring the efficiency, effectiveness, transparency and accountability of the management and collection of non-tax revenue.
This sub-decree aims to determine the mechanisms, rules and procedures for the collection, payment, collection, recording, monitoring and evaluation of non-tax revenue, as well as the implementation of contracts and the enforcement of non-tax debts.
The Minister also stated that this workshop will give wisdom to all relevant officials and operators to better understand the obligations to implement payments and revenue collection, as well as measures to contribute to building partnerships between sectors. Private and public.
"I hope that the workshop on disseminating the implementation of the sub-decree on non-tax revenue management will give all relevant officials and operators a clearer understanding of their obligations to implement payments and revenue collection," he said. "As well as measures to contribute to building a partnership between the private sector and the state."
Mr. Mao Ponha, Director of the Public Revenue Department of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, also gave a detailed presentation on the topic of non-tax revenue and debt management to the public.
It should be noted that according to the implementation of the sub-decree on the management of non-tax revenue, said that non-tax revenue refers to the income from the management of business and the sale of state property, the proceeds from concessions, fees from public services. Consequences of fines and penalties, favorable financial support, other benefits and special effects and other income that is defined as other non-tax revenue.
Non-tax liabilities, on the other hand, refer to the amount of non-tax revenue that has not been collected because the taxpayer failed to fulfill the obligation to pay the income within the specified period and conditions.
