(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dy Tharen, the winner of the 2011 Art Festival Song Award, released a new song describing the last struggle of the Khmer Rouge and national reconciliation in Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, entitled "Anlong Veng Sneha".
This song describes the seasonal view of Anlong Veng district and the weather, accompanied by stories of love, romance and historical content. This song also highlights the historical area of Anlong Veng district and incorporates it into the lyrics so that this song retains its image, taste and meaning. The music and lyrics were written by Mr. Sou Saroeun.
Youk Chhang, director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, said: "Although the singer's economic and marketing factors have affected Tharen's livelihood, Tharen has retained his innate abilities and talents. "Tharen has a conscience, ideals, love and struggle with this career without giving up."
Ms. Te Sokly went to the meeting with excitement because her father was away. Despite the emotional turmoil, while attending this morning's ceremony, Sokly tried her best to fulfill one of her father's great wishes before her death.
Mr. Te Chhor Pheng, 49 years old, the father of Ms. Te Sokly, before his death had a big wish is for his daughter to take a photo with Samdech Techo Hun Sen. In fact, taking photos with Samdech Techo for A-level students is not a problem. Five years ago, Samdech Techo Hun Sen always gave permission for A-level students to take photos as a souvenir.
But for this year, due to the large number of students up to 443, so if Samdech allows all students to take pictures with can lead to missed time for students lunch. Therefore, the protocol team decided to organize by selecting only 7 representative students in each capital-province.
This decision made Ms. Te Sokly not on the list to receive the prize and take a photo with Samdech. After receiving such information, Te Sokly was heartbroken again because she could not fulfill her father's wishes before her death.
Ms. Sokly sought the coordination of the Samdech Techo Hun Sen Protocol Team so that she could take a photo with Samdech Techo to fulfill her father's wishes. Out of compassion for the body and as well as Ms. Sokly, the protocol team provided this information to Samdech Techo. After receiving this information, Samdech Techo was also lonely for a long time and immediately responded by allowing Ms. Sokly to take a photo to fulfill her father's wishes.
After arriving at the venue and giving a short talk, Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked for Miss Te Sokly and invited her to the podium to give her a prize and allow her to take a photo with him. Samdech Techo also donated about 5 million Riels. After that, Samdech Techo also assigned two of Samdech's bodyguards to Miss Te Sokly to return to the explosion first to participate in the cremation of her father.
Receiving the sublime mercy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen moved Miss Te Sokly to tears on the stage without realizing it.
She continued, "May you go to hell and leave all the sorrows for you to go in peace, because I have worked hard to raise, take care of my children, provide food, stay, study in a pious manner, as well as the education and advice of Dad who pushed the baby to have this day. "I have fulfilled the role of a good father, but now I have left for the next world and let me go in peace."
