The National Assembly unanimously approved the draft law on construction by a vote of 106 to 106.
(Phnom Penh): Out of the four agendas included in the third session of the 6th legislature, this morning, October 7, 2019, the National Assembly approved only one agenda, the draft law on construction.
The draft law has 22 chapters and 111 articles, which were unanimously approved by the National Assembly by 106 out of 106 members of the National Assembly. The other three agendas, namely: the draft law on e-commerce, the draft law on consumer protection and the draft law on social security will be taken up by the National Assembly on the morning of October 8. 2019 tomorrow.
Ms. Nin Saphon, Chairwoman of the Public Commission on Transport, Telecommunications, Post, Industry, Mining, Energy, Trade, Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, said that the draft law on construction approved by the National Assembly today is an important draft. In a context where the construction sector is growing and is a pillar supporting the national economy.
Please be informed that the draft law on construction was approved by the Council of Ministers in the plenary session on August 30, 2018. The Cambodian Human Rights Committee will hold a workshop to disseminate and implement the third round of UPR recommendations in 2019
The workshop will be held for one and a half days, on October 9 and 10, 2019 from 8:00 am at Himawari Hotel, Phnom Penh. This is according to the press release of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee on October 7, which was received by Fresh News.
This workshop was organized with the participation of all stakeholders, including: representatives of ministries, state institutions, representatives of national and international civil society diplomats, as well as development partners, a total of about 200 people and for the following purposes:
2: Distribute and determine the 173 recommendations to the ministries and institutions in charge to implement
3. Provide a forum for civil society groups and relevant development partners to participate and provide advice on the distribution and implementation of these 173 recommendations.
