For more than 32 years, while Russia and the United States have been busy implementing the INF Nuclear Treaty, China has been heavily involved in the production and development of missiles in a context that many US military officials consider a potential rival and enemy of the United States. The United States is no longer Russia, but China, the number one power in Asia.
