What a pity! A deer in Preah Vihear province died despite the efforts of the authorities to rescue
(Preah Vihear): A parrot died on the way while the rescue team transported it by cart to release it back into the forest. The death of this rare species of prey occurred in the early morning on October 7, 2019 in Po village, Po commune, Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province.
Lieutenant Colonel Rith Sona, police inspector of Tbeng Meanchey district, said that at 5 am this morning, a male deer ran into the commune village with injuries. Seeing this, the villagers reported to the authorities and wildlife conservation officers to check and pick up to be treated and released in the forest.
The district inspector continued that after receiving information from the people, the police and wildlife conservation officers went to transport the animals to be treated, but due to the long wait for doctors from Siem Reap, the police also transported the animals. He was taken by cart to be released back into the jungle, but unfortunately he died on the way.
Mr. Rith Sona said that after the animal died on the way, the authorities took it back to the district inspector.
He said that due to the superstitious villagers, they went to invite the monks to pray for the blessing of the beast and buried it, which caused the people and the authorities as well as the local authorities to regret the loss of the beast. This is a rare one.
Japanese patrol boat sinks North Korean fishing boat illegally fishing in Japanese waters!
TOKYO: A Japanese patrol boat and a North Korean fishing boat collided in the waters off Japan near one of the most popular fishing areas, but no casualties were reported. In that incident yet. This is according to the news release by Japanese TV NHK on Monday morning, October 7, 2019.
The report said that after the collision, a North Korean fishing boat sank and at least 20 people fell into the sea. Japan claims the accident happened in waters nearly 300 kilometers from the Noto Peninsula, which means that the North Korean fishing boat that sank above entered the wrong fishing activities. Laws in Japan's exclusive economic waters.
No further details have been released, but the incident comes after Japan launched a hot campaign to crack down on illegal fishing activities in its exclusive economic zone in the Sea of Japan. Many North Korean fishing boats have been reported to have entered the area. For both countries, Japan and North Korea have no diplomatic relations.
