Campaign to protect fish species during the closed season in Stung Treng province has ended
(Stung Treng): The campaign to protect fish species during the closed season in Stung Treng province has been successfully closed by the Fisheries Administration of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Stung Treng province in 2019. Full congratulations from the people of Stung Treng.
Speaking to Fresh News in Stung Treng province, Mr. Tum Niro, Director of Fisheries Administration, confirmed that the closed fishing season in Stung Treng waters is from May 1 to September 30 every year. During the closure, fishing with long nets and nets of all kinds is prohibited to prevent all species of squid from having the opportunity to travel safely to the breeding and spawning grounds.
During the five-month campaign, the conservation group has promoted 1725 fishermen and confiscated 413 gillets, fishing nets and 100,000 nets, and cracked down on illegal fishing. In fact, in 15 cases, 7 perpetrators were sent to court.
Apart from this, there is also the crackdown on many other fishery crimes, such as the lure of mosquito nets, the use of one hundred chips. In particular, cut off the network of fishery transport groups from the crime of catching fish.
"It is estimated by the Fisheries Administration that no less than 3,000 tons of all species of fish have been rescued by safely breeding and laying eggs, leaving millions of young fish in the wild," said Tum Niro. That child. "However, climate change, especially this year's low water regime, may not improve the reproduction of the species."
