Borey Sambath Mean Heng 3 Brings Gratitude, Gratitude, Destroys Temperament! Samdech Techo Hun Sen Returns to Cambodia After a Two-Day Visit to Vietnam (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia At 6 pm on October 5, 2019, led a delegation of senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia to return to Cambodia after concluding a two-day visit to Vietnam with high results.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, at the invitation of Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung, led a delegation of high-ranking officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia to visit Hanoi, Vietnam on October 4. Samdech Techo's visit to Vietnam was warmly welcomed by the Prime Minister of Vietnam and other senior Vietnamese leaders.
During his visit to Vietnam, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung, Secretary-General of the Communist Party of Vietnam (CPP) and Head of State of Vietnam Nguyen Phu Trong, and Speaker of the National Assembly Nguyen Thi Kim Ngin. .
In these meetings, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Vietnamese leaders noted the excellent development of relations between the two countries. In an atmosphere of friendship, mutual understanding and trust, the two leaders had in-depth discussions and reached important joint positions on Cambodia-Vietnam bilateral relations and coordination between the two countries in the regional forum. And international.
Samdech Techo and Vietnamese leaders agreed to deepen political ties by enhancing exchanges and high-level contacts, maintaining existing bilateral cooperation mechanisms, strengthening people-to-people exchanges and strengthening cooperation. Important friendship and assistance between the relevant ministries / institutions and provinces of the two countries, as well as continue to organize various celebratory events together.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen was very pleased with the achievements made in demarcating the border posts of the two countries. Samdech considers this achievement as an achievement in the history of border affairs between Cambodia and Vietnam, and also an achievement leading to the end of the nation's problems on this border work.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc, called on the authorities and the people to jointly maintain the border posts that have already been erected and to jointly build a border of peace, friendship and cooperation to bring development to the country and People of both countries.
It should be noted that during this visit, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc presided over the Cambodia-Vietnam Conference on Investment and Trade Promotion. In this forum, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the excellent development of trade and investment between the two countries.
Samdech Techo pointed out that in 2018, the total trade volume between Cambodia and Vietnam reached more than 4.7 billion US dollars, an increase of about 24% compared to 2017. In the first six months of 2019, the total trade volume between the two countries reached 2.72 billion US dollars, with an expectation of reaching more than 5 billion US dollars by the end of this year.
As for the investment sector, from 1994 to August 2019, Cambodia approved 84 investment projects of Vietnamese companies with a total investment of about 2.5 billion US dollars.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also supported the establishment of the Cambodia-Vietnam Special Economic Zone along the border between the two countries.
During his current visit to Vietnam, Samdech Techo and his delegation laid flowers in honor of the Vietnamese heroes who sacrificed their lives in the national liberation movement from the colonies, and also laid wreaths in honor of Ho Chi Minh. Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, October 5: 1,210 Illegal Vehicles Found and Fined
