The Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Statement issued by the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs on the evening of October 5, 2019 stated that the two sides reiterated ASEAN's position on the South China Sea issue as stated in the declaration. More recently, especially the Joint Statement of the 52nd ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting.
"Both sides stressed that recent tensions must be resolved peacefully as soon as possible in accordance with international law, including the 1982 United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea," the statement said.
Disputes in the South China Sea between Beijing and four countries, including Brunei, Malaysia, Vietnam and the Philippines, have escalated after China poured land to build an artificial island in the South China Sea.
Brunei, Malaysia, Vietnam and the Philippines claim parts of the 3.5 million-square-kilometer overlap with China. China claims about 90 percent of the sea. However, the South China Sea issue seems to have calmed down for some time. Hong Kong Mayor Carrie Lam is preparing a special plan to end the problem completely ...
