The full text of the joint statement between Cambodia and Vietnam is as follows:
At the invitation of Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc, Prime Minister of Vietnam, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to pay an official visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on October 4-5. 2019.
During the visit, Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen met with Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc, Prime Minister of Vietnam and paid a courtesy call on Mr. Nguyen Phu Trong, Secretary General of the Communist Party and President of Vietnam and paid a courtesy call on Ms. Nguyen Thi Kim Ngin, President of the National Assembly of Vietnam, pays his respects at the National Heroes Memorial and Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum.
Prime Minister Hun Sen and Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung co-chaired a conference on trade and investment promotion between Cambodia and Vietnam and presided over the signing ceremony of a number of bilateral agreements, including:
5. The two sides reaffirmed their commitment to fully review the demarcation treaties and border agreements signed between the two countries. The two sides also agreed to promote cooperation on border management based on existing mechanisms and legal frameworks to build border lines, peace, stability, friendship, cooperation and sustainable development.
6. In an atmosphere of friendship, mutual understanding and trust, the two leaders had in-depth discussions and reached an important joint position on Cambodia-Vietnam bilateral relations and coordination between the two countries in Regional and international forums.
9. The two sides agreed to deepen political ties by enhancing exchanges and high-level contacts, maintaining existing bilateral cooperation mechanisms, strengthening people-to-people exchanges and strengthening friendly cooperation. And significant assistance between relevant ministries / institutions and provinces of the two countries, as well as to continue to organize various celebratory events together.
14: The Cambodian side expresses its gratitude and appreciation for the assistance of the Vietnamese side in training, capacity building and grant assistance for the past several years. The two sides agreed to implement assistance projects in a timely manner and continue to find ways and means to improve the effectiveness of Vietnamese aid to Cambodia.
16. The Vietnamese side expressed its gratitude to the Kingdom of Cambodia for its continued support and non-discrimination against the people of Vietnamese descent in Cambodia.
19. The two sides agreed to coordinate under the framework of the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Development Triangle and the relevant Mekong Sub-region Cooperation Mechanism to promote the effective implementation of the Action Plan for the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Economic Linkage. 2030, adopted at the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Summit in March 2018.
20. The two sides agreed to work with relevant countries to conclude the negotiations on comprehensive regional economic cooperation as soon as possible, which will harmonize the interests and fully consider the differences in the level of development among Member countries.
21. The two sides reiterated ASEAN's position on the South China Sea issue as stated in the recent Joint Declaration, in particular the Joint Statement of the 52nd ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting. Both sides stressed that recent tensions must be resolved peacefully as soon as possible in accordance with international law, including the 1982 United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea.
