Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on Cambodian-Vietnamese authorities and people to maintain border posts and turn the border into a zone of peace and sustainable development (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, calls on Cambodian authorities and citizens Cambodia-Vietnam maintain the border post and turn the border into an area of peace and sustainable development for the peace of the people and our two countries forever.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's appeal during the Cambodia-Vietnam signing of two documents during his visit to Hanoi on the morning of October 5, 2019, namely: the Supplementary Treaty on the State Boundary Treaty 1985 and 2005 Supplementary Treaty between the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and the Kingdom of Cambodia;
During the ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "Please call on the local authorities as well as the people of the two countries to join together to maintain the border post to be stable and together to turn the border area. "As a border of peace, friendship, cooperation and sustainable development for the peace of our people and our country forever."
Cambodia and Vietnam share a land border of about 1,270 kilometers. So far, both sides have erected 84% of the posts and boundaries, with only 16% remaining to be resolved in the near future.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered that the signing ceremony of the two historical documents today clearly confirmed that the border settlement between our two countries has taken a very proud step forward.
Samdech sincerely commended the heroism, hard work and dedication of the Joint Border Technical Team and the territorial authorities along the Cambodia-Vietnam border, the Engineering Command and the leaders of the Joint Boundary Committees of our two countries for their hard work. Successfully completed this historic work.
