Cambodia and Vietnam share a land border of approximately 1,270 km, as defined in the 1 / 100,000 scale carbon map left over from the colonial period and deposited at the United Nations. The two countries also signed a joint treaty demarcating the two countries' borders in 1985, and signed a supplementary treaty in 2005 leading to the demarcation and demarcation of the border.
The demarcation of the border between the two countries began in 2005 and so far only 84 percent of the demarcation has been completed. Although the demarcation of the border post has not been completed yet, Cambodia and Vietnam on the morning of October 5, 2019 agreed to sign to recognize the results of this work.
The signing ceremony was held under the presidency of the Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Vietnam and officials of the Joint Boundary Commission of the two countries. Two and many other stakeholders.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc expressed their pleasure and satisfaction with this achievement. In his speech before the signing ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that this achievement confirms that the border settlement between the two countries has taken a very proud step forward.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized, "This great achievement that our two countries have achieved is due to the search for a common solution of brotherhood and mutual understanding in the past as a friendly brotherhood for decades." And.
The border issue between Cambodia and Vietnam is a complex one for both countries due to the remnants of the historical crisis. Some Cambodians still remember the pain and accuse Vietnam of stealing their territory, creating a psychological conflict between the two nations. Politicians in Cambodia also often use this issue as a stepping stone to seek their political popularity.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered the achievements of the border demarcation and demarcation between the two countries as contributing to the end of disputes and conflicts between the people of the two countries.
"Indeed, if we do not work to end this border issue, our two countries will continue to have unresolved border disputes for generations to come, easily becoming political rivals and security and development along the border. "It will not happen." Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasizes further.
At the ceremony, both Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc also committed to resolving the remaining 16 percent of border issues on the basis of national and international law and international practice on recognition. The principle of the unaltered border line, which the colony left behind, continues to be a strong, leading base to resolve the border issue between the two countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc called on the local authorities and the people of the two countries to maintain the border post and work together to turn the border area into a border of peace, friendship, cooperation and development. Sustain for the peace of the people and the two countries.
