(Hanoi, Vietnam): On the morning of October 5, 2019, the second day of the official visit to Hanoi, Vietnam, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia Flowers pay homage to the fallen soldiers of the Vietnamese People's Army and lay a wreath at the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum.
With the deepest gold inscription, Samdech Techo Hun Sen bowed with the deepest respect to the heroes of the Vietnamese People's Army who sacrificed their physical, mental, and spiritual strength. In the cause of liberating the country and the people of Vietnam from colonial rule until the country gained full national independence and developed to the present.
