Mr. Sar Sokha: "Please continue to crack down on the online gambling business, even if the perpetrators use the name of any person as a backbone."
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, urged all relevant authorities to continue to crack down on all forms of online gambling, regardless of the name of the perpetrator or any child.
Mr. Sar Sokha noted that the perpetrators may associate or use the names of the children of leaders or individuals with positions of power in state institutions as a backbone to intimidate the authorities. In such cases, he insisted that the authorities apply strictly and effectively on those individuals.
"Please continue to crack down on the online gambling business, no matter who the perpetrators use!"
On behalf of the people, I would like to express my appreciation to all the forces and authorities at all levels who have been implementing the Royal Government's circular on strengthening the management of the electronic gambling business through the Internet, online and abroad. All kinds and all images in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Once again, I fully support the Royal Government of Cambodia's measures to ban online and domestic online betting. I would like to support and encourage all kinds of authorities who have been implementing the Royal Government's decision to crack down on all illegal businesses.
It is clear that the perpetrators may associate or use the names of the children of leaders or individuals with positions of power in state institutions as a backbone to intimidate the authorities. In such cases, please insist on the authorities to implement strictly and effectively on those individuals.
I would like to emphasize that even if the perpetrators use my name Sar Sokha or my team, I strongly reject and condemn and ask the authorities to follow the circular of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen. Seriously.
"Let the authorities increase prevention and enforce the law, regardless of who or what child is the person who uses the name of the leader or the son of any leader, which affects the honor and dignity of the leadership."
