A company invests $ 150 million in mango cultivation and processing in Sihanoukville
In the afternoon of October 4, 2019, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, allowed Mr. Ung Kim, General Manager of this company to pay a courtesy call and discuss and make recommendations related to agricultural investment projects. Industry (mango processing) in Cambodia in the near future.
This industrial zone is used for agricultural exhibitions, procurement, processing of tropical fruits and vegetables, agricultural trade with leading international partners, as well as for the implementation of agricultural techniques, group assembly, seed production and organic fertilizer processing, etc. Overall, it is a multi-purpose area serving Cambodia's agro-industrial sector. This is a further confirmation of Mr. KIM.
The Minister welcomed and supported the long-term investment willingness in the agricultural sector in Cambodia, because it is at the same time that the Ministry as well as the Royal Government has set a policy to increase the value added on the production of agricultural processing. 12% by 2025, as well as incentives for investors in the agro-industrial sector, which are the main priorities set out in the Cambodian Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025.
He said that the Ministry is always looking forward to and welcome all investment projects in all production lines from A-Z (production, processing and marketing) that meet the requirements of the agricultural processing process in all aspects. "If we incorporate a suitable technology for producers, including this processing plant, we hope that mango products will have a higher value added, and this is what our farmers expect," he added.
The Ministry will provide all kinds of cooperation to facilitate all kinds of administrative, legal and technical documents to make the project successful, in order to improve the capacity to supply processed agricultural products in the domestic and foreign markets, compete, promote consumption and cut Reduce the export of mango raw materials, increase value added, create jobs, increase income and sustain the national economy. This is the emphasis of Minister Veng Sakhon.
Apart from mango products, Minister Veng Sakhon also told the company to be interested in cassava, pepper, cashew and freshwater fish, which are potential raw materials for processing and export.
