The Prime Minister of Cambodia announces to hold a meeting with Vietnamese investors in Cambodia every year (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): During his visit to Vietnam today, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, announced a meeting with Vietnamese investors in Cambodia every year. Chinese-Vietnamese New Year every year to be able to talk about business issues together and take the opportunity to wish investors.
The announcement of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia was made on the occasion of Samdech and Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc, Prime Minister of Vietnam, attending the Cambodia-Vietnam Conference on Investment and Trade Promotion in Hanoi on the evening of October 4, 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "We will have a meeting once a year before the Vietnamese New Year between Vietnamese investors and the Prime Minister of Cambodia to wish the New Year, because then we can talk about the issue. "Doing business together and taking that opportunity, I can also wish investors who go to invest in Vietnam."
On this occasion, the Prime Minister of Cambodia also welcomed the wise decisions of all foreign investors, especially Vietnamese investors who have chosen and intend to select Cambodia as a potential investment destination to start or expand business. Its.
"I would like to appeal to Vietnamese businessmen and investors who have visited Cambodia and businessmen and investors who have not yet come to Cambodia to learn more about the potential and investment opportunities in Cambodia and to decide whether to invest or not," he said. "Joint investment with Cambodian investors to get the most out of bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has shown that this special economic zone can be established in the area where Samdech used to travel to Vietnam to liberate Cambodia from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, in the area of Koh Thmor in Tonlong commune, Memot district. Tbong Khmum Province. Samdech Techo also claimed that the reason why Samdech supported the establishment in this area is because this is an important memorial site 42 years ago.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia said, "If His Excellency Nguyen Suon Phuc encourages this, I would very much support it. Made in Cambodia because it is easy to know that the product comes from Cambodia, but Vietnamese investors.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the area where Samdech used to fight for national liberation now also has factories and some markets, and it is very appropriate to change from the area where the beginning of the struggle process started to the area of development. To turn into a special situation.
However, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia asserted that the prince did not force the establishment immediately, as this was an economic venture that required a clear and detailed study. Okay.
As of now, there are 19 special economic zones in Cambodia that produce and export products, including 377 factories, creating 114,173 jobs for Cambodians. Of the nearly 400 factories, 90 are from Japan operating in the SEZ.
The first special economic zone in Cambodia was established in Bavet city, Svay Rieng province, bordering Vietnam, and the first factory in the special economic zone was a bicycle assembly plant, and now Cambodia has become the third largest exporter in the world. Bicycles sell the most.
It should be noted that in the bilateral meeting on the morning of October 4, 2019, the two leaders expressed satisfaction over the significant increase in bilateral trade volume, which increased by 24% in 2018 with more than 4,700 million US dollars and is expected to reach more than 5 billion US dollars in 2019.
The two sides agreed to boost economic ties between the two countries through the early completion of the Cambodia-Vietnam Economic Connectivity Master Plan to 2030 and the implementation of the signed agreement on connectivity. Transport, including a Memorandum of Understanding on the Transport Cooperation Strategy for 2018-2025 with the Vision 2030.
