(Hanoi, Vietnam): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has told his Vietnamese counterpart Nguyen Phu Trong that he will work to complete the demarcation work between Cambodia and Vietnam while he is still Prime Minister of Cambodia. Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his willingness to complete the border demarcation with Vietnam during his tenure as Prime Minister. Hanoi, Vietnam on the evening of October 4, 2019.
Cambodia and Vietnam share a land border of about 1,270 kilometers. At present, the two countries have completed about 84 percent of the border demarcation work, leaving only 16 percent. During his current visit to Vietnam, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will also sign an agreement with his Vietnamese counterpart to recognize the completed border post.
Regarding the erection of border posts between the two countries, Vietnamese Head of State Nguyen Fu Chung expressed his satisfaction with the results as well as the signing of the border posts. Nguyen Fu Chung also urged the two countries to complete the remaining 16 percent of the border demarcation.
It should be noted that in this courtesy call, Vietnamese Head of State Nguyen Fu Chung warmly welcomed the official visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the delegation in Vietnam. Mr. Nguyen Fu Chung stressed that he closely followed the results of bilateral meetings, press conferences as well as the Cambodia-Vietnam Conference on Investment and Trade Promotion.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his pleasure to pay an official visit to Vietnam as well as to meet with the President of Vietnam.
The Prime Minister also noted Vietnam's prominent role in the region as well as in the international arena in mediating or resolving issues.
Regarding the issue of economic development, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is a country in the middle of Vietnam and Thailand. So the growth of Vietnam as well as Thailand also led to the progress of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo thanked Vietnam for its contribution to the development of Cambodia and mobilized Vietnamese investors to do business in Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the Vietnamese head of state to consider Cambodia as a close and loyal friend of Vietnam.
In this meeting, Mr. Nguyen Fu Chung also praised the progress in all areas of Cambodia and play various roles to facilitate and solve problems in the region as well as on the international stage.
