Cambodia, Vietnam support Timor-Leste's ASEAN membership
(Hanoi, Vietnam): The Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Vietnam have expressed their joint support for Timor-Leste to become a member of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) in the near future.
The support of the two ASEAN member states was expressed through the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Prime Minister of Vietnam Nguyen Suon Phuc at a joint press conference on October 4, 2019 on the occasion of the Supreme Leader. The Royal Government of Cambodia visits Vietnam.
"We agree to support Timor-Leste to join ASEAN in the future," Hun Sen said. "Due to Timor-Leste's efforts, it is time for ASEAN leaders to decide whether Timor-Leste will become a member of ASEAN in the future, and perhaps the most appropriate time for Timor-Leste to meet in the Socialist Republic. Vietnam in 2020. "
Timor-Leste has been seeking ASEAN membership for many years. Cambodia is one of the ASEAN member countries and has made great efforts to help Timor-Leste become an ASEAN member.
The Cambodian leader, who had a difficult history when Cambodia applied for ASEAN membership, was eager to help Timor-Leste. Samdech Techo Hun Sen once said that only countries that have experienced the same difficulties understand Timor-Leste's difficulties.
This statement was made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Cambodia-Vietnam Conference on Investment and Trade Promotion in Hanoi on October 4, 2019, with the participation of Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung.
Vietnam's imports to Cambodia include steel, gasoline, textiles and clothing, and agricultural products such as fish, meat and vegetables, fruits, as well as consumer goods, while Cambodia's exports to Vietnam include cashew nuts, rubber, wood and wood products, fruits and vegetables. And many other products.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the field of investment, according to the records of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, from 1994 to August 2019, Cambodia has approved 84 investment projects of Vietnamese companies with a total investment of about 2. $ 5 billion, of which agriculture accounts for about two-thirds of all investment projects.
The Prime Minister said that in addition to the investment projects registered with the Council for the Development of Cambodia, there is also the presence of Vietnamese investment in areas such as banking, insurance, services and wholesale and retail.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on Vietnamese businessmen and investors who have visited Cambodia and businessmen and investors who have not yet come to Cambodia to learn more about the investment potential and opportunities in Cambodia and decide to invest. Invest or co-invest with Cambodian investors to get the most out of bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam.
Senior Minister Kun Kim Attends ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Disaster Management in Myanmar
Nay Pyi Taw, Myanmar: General Kun Kim, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions and First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, on October 4, 2019, attended the ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Disaster Management. The seventh disaster was held in Nay Pyi Taw, Myanmar.
The meeting was attended by Ministers and senior officials of ASEAN Member States in charge of Disaster Management, as well as ASEAN Secretary-General Dato 'Lim Chok Huy and other stakeholders.
Welcoming the meeting, Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his congratulations and gratitude to the Government of Myanmar and the organizers for their excellent organization and warm hospitality to the Cambodian and other delegations.
Mr. Kun Kim said that this meeting is very important for Cambodia and ASEAN member countries. He strongly believes that the meeting is a major cause of disaster risk reduction and resilience building in the region.
