Fifteen Cambodian Officials Selected for Training on "Capacity Building on Monitoring and Evaluation for Cambodia"
(Phnom Penh): An additional 15 Cambodian government officials have been selected to study in the Republic of Korea for the second year of a three-year training course (2018-2020) on "Capacity Building on Monitoring and Evaluation for the Country. Cambodia ”from 14 to 26 October 2019 (13 days).
According to a press release from the Office of Customs in Cambodia, obtained by Fresh News on the evening of October 4, 2019, it is confirmed that all participants are scheduled to leave Cambodia for the Republic of Korea on October 13, 2019. The coming 2019.
To facilitate this training, KOICA Office in Cambodia organized a pre-departure orientation program for all participants on October 4, 2019 in order to provide some necessary information related to life training in Korea. Of the Cambodian-Korean Alumni Association, as well as the ethics of the training program.
With a mission to support human resource development in partner countries, KOICA-KOICA invites talented trainees from Cambodia and helps them acquire skills and knowledge systems that will play an important role in the country. Cambodia.
The second year training program aims to enhance professional capacity for developing monitoring and evaluation systems that apply to specific areas. The second year of training will focus on specialists in each field.
All government officials selected for the training thanked KOICA and the Korean government for their commitment to the training. This is to promote capacity building and broad awareness related to various development projects, especially monitoring and evaluation.
