Mr. Neth Pheaktra: Encourage all circles to implement environmental friendliness to ensure the quality and sustainability of the environment in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, urged all circles to implement environmental friendliness to ensure the quality and sustainability of the environment in Cambodia.
Mr. Net Pheaktra's promotion was made on October 4, 2019, when he was invited to the opening ceremony of the workshop on "Encouragement of Environmental Peace" organized by the Department of Rewards and Incentives. General Department of Environmental Knowledge and Information of the Ministry of Environment with the participation of more than 100 youth and students in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that it is not difficult to have good habits for the environment or to act in an environmentally friendly manner, but what is difficult is to have a negative attitude towards our environment. Therefore, changing negative attitudes and attitudes towards the environment into environmentally friendly action is a necessary factor, starting with each of us, continuing to spread to many other individuals.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said: "It is important to start having good environmental habits, starting from the pain of cleaning the environment, the packaging of waste that we create properly, that is, know how to take care of waste. "Garbage in bins, do not throw garbage in the open, save energy at home and at work, save water, plant trees and other plants for a green environment."
Mr. Neth Pheaktra also called on all stakeholders, especially young people, students, who are the strong pillars of the nation, to participate in the practice of good habits, love and care for the environment more and more to turn Cambodia into a country. Clean environment, fresh air in the cause of socio-economic development, environmental protection and the promotion of sustainable living in Cambodia.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized: "The participation of the people is necessary to achieve a common goal: to regain national pride and to build a vibrant modern nation, quality and sustainability, environment and resource heritage." "Cambodia's nature is protected and preserved for the benefit of all Cambodians."
