CamControl officers found expired goods for sale at O'Chamnar market, Preah Sihanouk province and confiscated and burned them
(Preah Sihanouk): For food safety as well as the health of the people, CamControl Preah Sihanouk Branch, with Mr. Bun Chamroeun, Acting Branch Manager, in collaboration with the Provincial Department of Commerce, the Market Commission and the local authority, continued on October 2, 2019. Disseminate the quality of food safety, inspect food products and pre-packaged goods at O'Chamnar Market, Preah Sihanouk Province, and found 9.08 kg of expired goods.
Sihanoukville CamControl officials said that the purpose of the inspection is to prevent the traffic of defective goods, counterfeit labels, expiration dates and contain banned chemicals that affect people's health.
During the inspection, the officers took some food samples for preliminary testing, including fresh shrimp, pickled fish paste, cauliflower pickle, and cabbage pickle to find banned chemicals that could affect people's health.
