This statement was made by General Nem Sovath on the morning of October 4, 2019, on the occasion that the General led a team to inspect the construction site of the Victory Monument in Chroy Changvar District, Phnom Penh.
The general said that the site of the win-win monument is quietly stockpiling in its historical meaning, invading the hearts, minds and souls of the Cambodian people in all walks of life, including national and international researchers. Also. After the inauguration of the past 9 months, with the political meaning of the win-win of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, peace has attracted the attention of all people curious to see this huge monument.
It should be reminded that the construction of the Victory Monument started in February 2016 on an area of 8 hectares in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, north of Phnom Penh, a symbol of peace that Cambodia received after the end of the civil war. Decades ago, this monument has become a legacy for future generations.
On December 29-30-31, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the inauguration of a win-win political memorial and celebrated the 20th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian Civil War.
There are five main goals for the construction of this monument, including:
* First: Recall the importance of peace, achievements and processes that have led to peace through win-win policy and national unity. Demonstrates the harmonization of Cambodian society through religion, epoch, history and achievements.
* Second: Respect and record the dedication, leadership and creativity of Cambodia's leading guides and operators who have brought national reconciliation and an end to the bloodless civil war that has brought prosperity and peace to Cambodia. .
* Third: Establish a center that provides learning for all generations to continue to study and gain an understanding of the true history of Cambodia and continue to implement Techo Sen's win-win policy and values of integration. In the process of building, leading and developing the country in the future.
* Fourth: Demonstrate the values of Khmer culture, civilization and architects in the style of art, symbols, symbols, sculptures and other infrastructure for people of all generations to understand.
* Fifth: Establish a tourist destination in Phnom Penh that has the characteristics of tourism, history, culture, as well as targets for research visits.
