Recall that Cambodia and Vietnam established diplomatic relations on June 24, 1967 and were severed in March 1970. The two countries reconnected in January 1979. Vietnam and Cambodia are countries with villages and fences with a common border of about 1,270 km.
2018 marks the 51st anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries. On the occasion of the 51st anniversary of the relationship, the two countries' senior leaders have frequently exchanged relations and visited each other, highlighting the ties of friendship and solidarity based on the principles of mutual trust and mutual respect. And supported each other economically, socially, politically and diplomatically.
In terms of trade relations, the two countries' total trade in 2017 reached about 2.13 billion US dollars, an increase of about 30% compared to 2016. But Cambodia's exports to Vietnam are still small. In fact, Cambodia's exports to Vietnam in 2017 amounted to 342 million US dollars, compared to Cambodia's imports from Vietnam in 2017 was about 1.8 billion US dollars.
