Cambodian Derivatives Exchange and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia continue to hold workshops on strategies for successful investment in Kampot
(Kampot): Cambodian Derivatives Exchange and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia continue to co-organize workshops to increase investment knowledge, reduce investment risk, investment trends and strategies for successful investment in Kampot. .
This workshop is a new achievement in addition to the workshops of the two institutions in six provinces, including: Sihanoukville, Kampong Cham, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Siem Reap and Takeo. In fact, this workshop in Kampot province was held on October 3, 2019 in order to increase knowledge related to investment, reduce investment risk, investment trends and strategies for successful investment.
This workshop was organized with the participation of Mr. Sok Dara, Deputy Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia. Mr. Sok Dara emphasized the mission of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia in strengthening regulations for the derivatives market in Cambodia and encouraged investors to increase their knowledge and readiness, as well as to select companies licensed by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to avoid risks.
He also praised Cambodian Derivatives Exchange as a leading and active company in upholding derivatives trading standards and enforcing investor regulations and protections.
He said that since the presence of provincial workshops, Cambodian Derivatives Exchange Company has been the only central counterparty partner of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia in organizing this event.
