The Minister of Agriculture told the President of the International Fund for Agricultural Development about the vision and direction of the development of Cambodia's agricultural sector to become modern agriculture
He called on all actors to strengthen and expand this culture even better in order to serve and protect the national interest to be more active, lively and interconnected in the socio-economic development of the country and to speak specifically for the agricultural sector. To make progress by taking advantage of the IFAD Fund in a transparent manner to meet the real needs of the people in the current context.
1. Promote the growth of agricultural production through potential diversification and increase exports by strengthening and expanding agricultural modernization to increase productivity and competitiveness by applying smart farming techniques and adaptation to climate change.
2. Increase animal production to 3% per year and increase commercial breeding to 22% and promote good breeding to 30% by 2023.
3. Increase the management of fisheries resources effectively and sustainably by strengthening the implementation of the law on fisheries, maintaining the stability of natural products within 600,000 tons per year, increasing aquaculture production by 20% per year.
4: Continue to manage forest resources and wildlife in a sustainable manner, contribute to the better maintenance of forest cover and increase the income of community forestry by 20% per year through agricultural diversification and forest reforestation. And continue to implement the necessary measures to contribute to the sustainability of the ecosystem.
The Minister also highlighted a number of challenges that hinder the development of the agricultural sector, both now and in the future. Therefore, taking this opportunity, he suggested that all stakeholders work together to address these issues in an effective inter-sectoral manner, including the private sector, which is the driving force of economic growth in line with the "public-private-partnership" approach. Development and community. ”
