(Phnom Penh): Golden FX Link Capital participated in a provincial workshop in Takeo organized by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and its central counterpart, Cambodian Derivatives Exchange.
This workshop, held in Takeo province, is the sixth provincial workshop where the company shares knowledge, experience as well as successful methods for investors after Kampong Cham, Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang and Sihanoukville.
The theme for 2019 is "Derivatives Trading, Investment Preparation and Related Awareness", focusing on promoting and expanding derivative investment awareness across the country and increasing Confidence for investors and allow investors to be ready for investing in derivatives.
Mr. Sok Dara, Deputy Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, announced the opening of the 2019 Provincial Workshop and confirmed the direction of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia in strengthening regulations for the derivatives market in Cambodia and encouraging investors to increase their knowledge. It is ready to select companies that are licensed by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to avoid risk.
He also praised Golden FX Link Capital for always being proactive in raising derivatives trading standards and implementing investor protection principles.
Mr. Long Samnang, Chief Financial Officer of Golden FX Link Capital, expressed his pleasure to participate in the 2019 Provincial Workshop with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia.
He gave a presentation on "Derivatives Trading Strategies" which focused on knowledge of derivatives trading, one of the most popular financial products, prevention and mitigation of investment risk, and Good strategies to get the most out of your investment.
After attending the workshop in Takeo, the company will continue to attend workshops in Kampot, Kep and other provinces throughout Cambodia. The results of the provincial workshops in Takeo province showed remarkable success, with not only the large number of participants, but also the support and growth of the participants' skills.
