(Takeo): The Cambodian Derivatives Exchange Co., Ltd., in collaboration with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, has organized a workshop to increase investment-related knowledge, reduce investment risk, investment trends and strategies for successful investment in Takeo provinces. Successful.
The workshop, held in Takeo province, attracted more than 100 participants from various fields to increase their knowledge related to investing, risk reduction, investment trends and strategies for successful investment.
This workshop was organized with the participation of Mr. Sok Dara, Deputy Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia.
Mr. Sok Dara confirmed the intention of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to strengthen regulations for the derivatives market in Cambodia and encouraged investors to increase their knowledge and readiness, as well as to select companies licensed by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to avoid risks.
He also praised Cambodian Derivatives Exchange as a leading company and has always been active in raising derivatives trading standards and enforcing investor regulations and protections.
Cambodian Derivatives Exchange Co., Ltd. is the only central counterparty that cooperates with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to organize provincial workshops for 2019. The company has also allowed its outstanding derivatives brokers to participate in the event.
In addition to providing investment expertise, Cambodian Derivatives Exchange offers a wide range of investment opportunities to the public, especially investors across Cambodia.
