(Siem Reap): On October 3, 2019, the Association of Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils of Siem Reap Province organized the 3rd General Assembly with the election of Mr. Sam Lam, Sangkat Chief of Sala Kamroeuk as the Chairman and 8 other Vice-Chairmen. 262 votes in favor and 4 abstentions.
The General Assembly was chaired by Mr. Ung Hoeun, Chairman of Siem Reap Provincial Council, Mr. Nak Neron, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap and Mr. Soy Kosal, Chairman of the National League for Local Councils.
A total of 347 participants in the General Assembly, including 295 delegates from municipal, district, commune and sangkat councils from 12 districts and 100 communes.
The Association of Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils of Siem Reap Province was established in order to promote the status, develop the capacity and protect the legitimate interests of the Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils, which are members of the Association: 1 city, 11 districts, 88 communes and 12 communes.
The 15th ASEAN Environment Ministers' Meeting will discuss regional cooperation in the field of environment, including issues related to climate change, urban sustainability, biodiversity conservation, coastal environment, environmental education, water resources management, and the environment. Management of chemicals and hazardous wastes, pollution control, cross-border haze and environmental friendship school.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Environment, three important documents will be reviewed and approved, including:
1: Draft ASEAN Joint Statement on Climate Change at the 25th Summit of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (COP25-UNFCCC) 2: Draft ASEAN Strategic Plan on Environment 3: Request for inclusion A total of five national parks of Thailand, Vietnam, Myanmar become ASEAN Heritage Parks.
In addition, Cambodia will host the 3rd ASEAN Environmental Peace School Award Ceremony and the 1st ASEAN Environmental Friendship Youth Excellence Award for all ASEAN Member States through the ASEAN-Japan Integration Fund. Within the framework of the 15th ASEAN Environment Ministers' Meeting and related meetings, there will also be a cardamom planting ceremony in front of Angkor Wat.
Please be informed that the ASEAN Environment Ministers' Meeting is held every two years for the purpose of discussing environmental cooperation in the region. The 14th ASEAN Environment Ministers' Meeting and related meetings, including meetings with dialogue partners, were held in September 2017 in the host country Brunei.
