Dissemination and consultation forum in Boeung Keng Kang district, many requests related to public works and garbage, ask Phnom Penh authorities to help solve
(Phnom Penh): The Dissemination and Consultation Forum of the Capital Council held at BELTEI Hall, Boeung Keng Kang District this morning, October 3, 2019, the people raised many requests and suggestions related to public works and garbage issues. Phnom Penh authorities help solve them.
The forum was held in the presence of Mr. Pa Socheatvong, Chairman of Phnom Penh Capital Council, Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, on behalf of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Sam Heng Boros, Chairman of Boeung Keng Kang District Assistance Team, Mr. Theam Sam An, Governor of Boeung Keng Kang District, The district inspector will be joined by councilors, officials under the administration of the capital and hundreds of people.
He added that the outreach and consultation forum of the Capital Council will provide people to participate in the process of good governance and as a tool for enhancing accountability and transparency in the process of reviewing the provision of public services of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration in order. To ensure that all priority issues of local people are examined, addressed and responded to.
He added that all local stakeholders are integrated into the environment in the process of democratic development at the sub-national level. In addition, the Phnom Penh Capital Council aims to promote a culture of dialogue and democratic accountability.
Mr. Pa Socheatvong further stated that for the outreach and consultation forum held this morning, October 3, 2019, the people raised many requests and suggestions related to public works and garbage issues for the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority to help solve. They include: 16 oral requests and requests equal to 19 issues and 72 written requests.
He said that most people want the authorities to help them, including urging the cutting of branches that block public street lighting poles, repairing damaged roads at the local level and other high-risk issues. Most of all, it is a problem of garbage that causes serious disorder and the environment.
He added that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, always advised the sub-national administrative authorities to solve three congestion problems: traffic congestion, sewage congestion and garbage congestion. These three issues are the concern of the people every day, because in Phnom Penh, we now have a very developed development, which leads to an increase in vehicles and people.
Mr. Pa Socheatvong continued that so far, the population of Phnom Penh has reached 3.5 million, of which 2.3 million people are registered to work in Phnom Penh has 800,000 people, along with tens of thousands more tourists.
On that occasion, Mr. Pa Socheatvong also encouraged everyone to eat ambok at Wat Phnom resort, while Sam Rainsy used the 9-finger campaign to create a color revolution against the Royal Government.
As for the garbage problem, Mr. Keut Chhe also stated that garbage is a problem for all of us to face and this problem would not have been successful without the participation and awareness of the people. He said that educating people, it is important that all relevant authorities must work together to educate people to know how to properly dispose of garbage and increase awareness of the impact of garbage.
