(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, expressed his great satisfaction with the good relations between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea, which began in 1997. The Minister saw that the good relations between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea increased the trade volume between the two countries.
Minister Pan Sosak made the remarks while attending the National Day of the Republic of Korea on the night of October 2, 2019.
On the occasion, the Minister commended the Government and people of the Republic of Korea for their remarkable achievements in overcoming many obstacles to achieve progress in the country and enhancing Korea's reputation on the international stage.
The Minister further noted that with the continuous progress in the fields of education, science, technology and social welfare, the Republic of Korea has become a global industrial leader and has made significant contributions to international peace and security as well as development. Environmentally and sustainably in the region, including Cambodia.
Regarding the Cambodia-Korea bilateral relations, the Minister expressed his satisfaction with the increase in friendly relations and fruitful cooperation in various fields between our two countries since we re-established diplomatic relations in 1997.
The Republic of Korea has assisted Cambodia in many important areas, including human resource training, health, infrastructure, rural development, agriculture, information and communication technology. Within the framework of economic cooperation, bilateral trade is growing from about 600 million US dollars in 2017 to more than 700 million US dollars in 2018 and about 450 million US dollars in the first half of 2019.
The Minister also highlighted President Moon Jae-in's state visit to Cambodia last March and the upcoming visit of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the Republic of Korea for the upcoming summit. Commemorating the ASEAN-ROK Anniversary and the first Mekong-ROK Summit in November.
