General Secretariat of the National Council for Social Protection Disseminates and raises awareness about the process of building a social protection system in Cambodia
The purpose of this workshop is to disseminate and raise awareness of the process of building a social protection system in Cambodia, with the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025 as the basis for ensuring income security and reducing economic vulnerability and People's finances to promote welfare and social unity, as well as reduce poverty to the maximum.
The National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025 is designed to focus on two main pillars: the social assistance system and the social security system in order to achieve the vision and efforts of the Royal Government to transform the status and image of Cambodia. It will be a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
Social assistance systems are designed to manage programs that include interventions for the benefit of the poor and vulnerable. This system has four main components: 1- Disaster response, 2- Human capital development, 3- Vocational training and 4- Welfare for vulnerable people.
The main goal of this policy framework is to consolidate and strengthen existing programs to increase the efficiency, transparency and consistency of programs in the social protection system as a whole, as well as to expand the scope to meet the needs of the people in line with the growth of the national economy. And establish a governance framework to ensure effective management and increase budget efficiency.
Through this policy, Cambodians, especially the poor and vulnerable, receive protection under various forms of social protection, such as the establishment of orphanages, maternal and child health centers, and support for the poor. Who come for treatment or childbirth and the provision of education, such as the provision of benefits, pensions, health care, occupational risks, disabilities and so on.
