Court orders 're-investigation' of former RFA staffer
(Phnom Penh): The case of two former RFA staff members, Mr. Oun Chhin and Mr. Yeang Sophearin alias Yeang Socheameta, was not announced by the court this morning, October 3, 2019. In this regard, Trial Judge Im Van: issued a "ruling" to re-investigate the relevant evidence.
The court ordered another investigating judge to analyze the evidence in more detail, such as data, equipment, computers, and other messengers in the Studio, where the two defendants had gathered evidence. Prior to the verdict, the court considered that the previous evidence was not clear enough to make a judgment.
The Phnom Penh Municipal Court has not yet confirmed the verdict, pending the outcome of the investigation.
Mr. Oun Chhin and Mr. Yeang Socheameta were arrested on November 14, 2017, after RFA, which illegally opened an illegal office in Cambodia, withdrew and closed the office on its own. Both were detained by the court for almost a year and then released on bail on August 21, 2018.
Defendants Uon Chhin and Yeang Sophearin alias Yeang Socheameta were charged in connection with providing to a state or foreign agency that could jeopardize national defense. On August 9, 2019, the two were also charged in another case, producing pornographic videos. Ratanakkiri Deputy Chief of Bureau of Minor Crimes Shot Dead in Banlung Caf
