Saudi Arabia to boost trade and tourism cooperation with Cambodia
The assertion of the Ambassador of Saudi Arabia to Cambodia was made during a courtesy call on Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia at the National Assembly this morning, October 3, 2019.
Mr. Saud al-Sowleim informed the National Assembly President that during his diplomatic mission, he will work to deepen the cooperation between the two countries. In particular, he will act as a bridge to bring Cambodia's proposed project to the Government of Saudi Arabia and from the Royal Government of Saudi Arabia to the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The Ambassador hoped that the leaders of the two countries' Ministries of Commerce, Ministry of Tourism or Ministries of the two countries would have the opportunity to meet directly to promote relations and cooperation between the two countries in the areas mentioned above. .
In response, Samdech Heng Samrin was pleased to welcome and congratulate Mr. Saud al-Sovelim on his remarks. He said that bilateral cooperation between the two countries has established a number of agreements, especially mutual support in the UN forum, and that these cooperation have also significantly contributed to Maintaining stability, security, peace and development, both regionally and globally.
Samdech thanked the Royal Government of Saudi Arabia for providing scholarships to Cambodian students to study in Saudi Arabia and requested that Saudi Arabia continue and increase the number of scholarships for Cambodian students.
