(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for October 2, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 5,961 vehicles and found 1,846 illegal vehicles, including motorcycles 1,530 units. This is according to the official report of the General Commission of the National Police.
For the results of the two-day inspection from October 1 to 2, 2019, the police inspected 6,745 vehicles and found 2,630 offending vehicles, including 2,206 motorcycles and 2,630 vehicles were fined, including 2,206 motorcycles. Police crack down on timber trucks with police license plates in Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province
