Report: Alcohol use causes more than 200 diseases
(Phnom Penh): According to a press release mentioned at the award ceremony of the short video competition "Tragedy caused by the use of alcohol" on October 2, 2019, claimed that the use Alcohol causes more than 200 diseases.
"Alcohol use causes more than 200 diseases such as esophageal cancer, liver cancer, hypertension, coronary heart disease, cirrhosis, cirrhosis, dementia and so on," the statement said. "Apart from the health consequences, alcohol use causes traffic accidents, violence, economic losses and many other social problems."
A statement from Fresh News quoted the World Health Organization as saying that about 3 million people die each year as a result of the effects of alcohol use. In Cambodia, alcohol consumption is the second leading cause of death and injury in traffic accidents.
Meanwhile, according to the report on traffic accident victims in 2017 of the National Road Safety Committee, 250 people died due to driving under the influence of alcohol. And about $ 44 million was lost due to damage to public property.
The Cambodian Movement for Health has organized a short video contest to encourage young people to participate in promoting the effects of alcohol and to support effective measures to control alcohol products in order to prevent further casualties. This competition program is made to see that the average alcohol consumption of the Cambodian people has risen to an alarming level.
According to the video submitted to the contestants, the use of alcohol caused many tragedies, including: traffic accidents, violence, illness, failure to study, abuse and so on.
