Human resources are the main principles, there are two: health and knowledge, education and health. Knowledgeable but unhealthy people do not exist and healthy people without knowledge we can not develop. Therefore, the national budget is growing in both areas to improve living standards and improve the quality of education for our Cambodian students because we live in an open competition. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. HUN Manet.
* First: Provide self-confidence, knowledge, make us confident in their abilities * Second: as a basis to build additional capacity and success * Third: Create an advantage for competition with others.
Senior Cambodian officials highlight the Royal Government's efforts to provide investment facilitation for sustainable development
(Phnom Penh): Senior Cambodian officials have highlighted the Royal Government's efforts to facilitate investment in order to contribute to Cambodia's economic growth.
Speaking at the opening ceremony, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, warmly welcomed and highly appreciated the participation of stakeholders in this important seminar.
He thanked the World Economic Forum, especially Dr. Matthew Stephenson, for co-organizing the seminar, which focused on providing investment facilitation for sustainable development, especially in agriculture.
The Delegation Minister requested all participants to have a lively discussion to find key inputs for improving the provision of better investment facilitation.
Dr. Matthew Stephenson expressed his pleasure to work with the Council for the Development of Cambodia and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and other stakeholders to organize today's workshop.
Dr. informed the workshop that the selection of Cambodia as a partner in discussing the provision of investment facilitation for sustainable development is based on the strong foundation of Cambodia with a good policy on open investment.
In addition, there are three main reasons why the World Economic Forum decided to select Cambodia as a partner in this process:
1. Cambodia has achieved great success in attracting foreign direct investment in a proud growth of an average of more than 50% from 2005 to the present, and investment facilitation measures can play an important role in achieving Achieved this success.
2: While Cambodia needs development, while the average economic growth rate of about 7% since 2011, Cambodia's experience in modernizing investment for development can help other countries to learn key aspects of development. Development related to investment facilitation in Cambodia.
3. Cambodia embraces cooperation between the Royal Government and the private sector through the Royal Government-Private Sector Forum.
The 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum in March 2019 expressed the active support of the Royal Government for public-private partnerships in providing additional investment facilitation, which is in line with Mission of the World Economic Forum.
In addition, Cambodia played a key role in the World Trade Organization as the guest of honor at the Global Trade Assistance Review in July 2019 in Geneva, Switzerland. Share the experience with the world of Samdech Techo Prime Minister at that time.
Based on the above, the World Economic Forum and Cambodia can work together to share their findings and best practices on providing investment facilitation with other countries within the framework of the World Trade Organization and other regional frameworks.
It should be noted that the World Economic Forum noted that Cambodia has introduced a number of key measures related to investment facilitation to attract successful investment, including investment incentives and insurance, transparency and feasibility. Predictability, coordination and cooperation, ICT solutions and single stand, etc.
The measures are of a similar nature to what the World Forum has prepared for discussion in this workshop. The workshop was a resounding success, with lively discussions on the necessary measures to provide investment facilitation for sustainable development.
Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, delivered the closing remarks, emphasizing the Royal Government's commitment, especially the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to promote investment for sustainable development in accordance with the principles of "Green Development. "And create new agricultural entrepreneurship to contribute to the growth of efficient and environmentally friendly agriculture by providing better investment facilitation."
The Senior Minister also stated that the workshop also reflected the willingness to work together to continue the fight against corruption from all stakeholders in addition to past cooperation, such as participation in respecting the law, participation in various anti-corruption initiatives. Launched by the Anti-Corruption Unit, Participating in the preparation and publication of the Handbook on Anti-Corruption Programs for Business in Cambodia and other collaborations.
BEIJING (Reuters) - During a massive military parade on the occasion of the 70th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China on Tuesday, China unveiled a variety of new sophisticated weapons to the public and the international community. This is according to a quote from the BBC on Wednesday evening, October 2, 2019.
According to the Chinese Ministry of Defense, the march was attended by about 15,000 military officers, a total of 580 military equipment and weapons, as well as 160 fighter jets and helicopters, more than in previous years.
Experts say that if we all look back at these marches 20 years ago, most of the military equipment and weapons that China showed were bought only from Russia and Ukraine, but now modern weapons. All of these are made by China itself. Overall, the technological advances that China has achieved in just the last few decades are almost unprecedented.
Mr. Tun Pov, Chief of Ka Chanh Commune, was elected by the General Assembly as the President of the Association of Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils of Rattanakiri Province.
(Rattanakiri): On October 2, 2019, the Association of Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils of Rattanakiri Province organized the 3rd General Assembly by electing Mr. Tun Pov, Chief of Kachanh Commune, Banlung City, as the President of the Association of Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils of Rattanakiri Province. And 6 other vice presidents, receiving 105 votes in favor and 2 abstentions.
The General Assembly was chaired by Mr. Nab Bunheng, Chairman of Ratanakkiri Provincial Council, Mr. Muong Pang, Acting Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, and Mr. Kieng Sengky, Vice Chairman of the National League for Local Councils.
More than 136 participants in the General Assembly, including 107 delegates from municipal, district, commune and sangkat councils from 9 districts and 50 communes.
The Association of Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils of Rattanakiri Province was established in order to enhance the status, develop the capacity and protect the legitimate interests of the Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils, which are members of the Association: 1 city, 8 districts, 46 communes and 4 Sangkats.
Senior Minister Kun Kim Chairs a Meeting on Flood Impact and Disaster Management in Kampong Cham
(Kampong Cham): The National Committee for Disaster Management, in collaboration with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, together with the authorities of Kampong Cham and Tbong Khmum provinces, held a meeting this morning, October 2, 2019. Flood in Kampong Cham province.
The meeting was chaired by Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, accompanied by Mr. Lam Heng Huot, Deputy Chairman (NCCC), Mr. Sin Vuthy, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorologist, Mr. Mam Amnath, Secretary of State and with the participation of the leadership of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, as well as relevant authorities in Kampong Cham and Tbong Khmum.
Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, said that the impact caused by floods in the past, Kampong Cham province has 5 districts affected by floods affecting a total of 5,209 hectares of rainy season rice. Improved after the water receded by 41,134 hectares and damaged 1,075 hectares.
The governor said that 12 hectares of mixed crops were affected after the water receded, 0.4 hectares were improved, while another 0.8 hectares were damaged and 414 hectares of long-term crops were affected but did not cause any damage. That is still 100% better.
In response, the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management and Prime Minister of Cambodia, decided to provide 107 tons of rice seeds to Kampong Cham province for 5 districts and 152 tons to Tbong Khmum province for immediate distribution. Farmers to plant and rehabilitate in time during the dry season.
Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked the local authorities and the armed forces for their good cooperation during the evacuation and timely rescue of people during the floods.
Senior Minister Kun Kim said that in the past, on behalf of the National Committee for Disaster Management, which was a good staff for Samdech Techo Hun Sen, he requested the relevant ministries and institutions to cooperate and provide technical support to help solve the needs of the affected people. Timely, both during and after the disaster.
Taking this opportunity, the Senior Minister inspected the situation of river bank collapse and past prevention work and found ways to continue this work after the water receded in Rokar Thom village and Kampong Russey village in Chiro 1 commune, Tbong Khmum district. Chroy then continued to inspect the situation affected and damaged by the recent floods in Chroy Sralao village, Tonle Bit commune to provide rice seeds for rehabilitation.
On behalf of the local authorities, on behalf of the people, I would like to thank Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for always thinking about the well-being of the affected people and providing timely donations and working hard to help. Rescue the victims in time. More than 20 workers in Chum Kiri district, Kampot province, were seriously injured while driving to work at the factory
Colonel Mey Sokhom, police inspector of Chum Kiri district, said that there was a case of a Samsung truck transporting workers from Chum Kiri district to work at the Boeung Trakoun factory in Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province, overturning, causing serious and minor injuries to 24 people. Of course, there were three men.
Immediately after the incident, people near the scene reported to the authorities. The force also arrived at the scene to rescue the 24 victims, 16 of whom were sent to Takeo Provincial Hospital for treatment. The other eight were sent to Chhouk District Referral Hospital in Kampot Province.
The inspector also confirmed that the 24 victims, among the other passengers who were not injured, were all residents of Sre Cheng commune, Chum Kiri district, Kampot province, who went to work at the factory in the above geographical location. This is Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province.
After receiving information about the accident as above, Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Kampot Province, together with relevant officials, visited the victims in both Takeo Province and Chhouk District, Kampot Province this morning.
