(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia has partnered with the Asian Development Bank under the Mekong Business Initiative and the Australian Embassy in Cambodia has organized a Cambodian Financial Technology Program.
This program was organized with the participation of Mrs. Neav Chanthana, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia.
The Cambodian Financial Technology Program aims to provide an opportunity for government representatives, policy makers, authorities and all stakeholders to discuss the importance of financial technology in contributing to the development of Cambodia's financial and economic sector, as well as opportunities and challenges. Promoting financial technology.
The Cambodia Financial Technology Program is a platform that allows all stakeholders to share knowledge and experiences related to the latest developments in financial technology in their institutions and countries, which contribute to increasing knowledge and cooperation in financial technology.
Ms. Neav Chanthana highlighted the significant progress made by the National Bank of Cambodia after the first Financial Technology Forum was held in 2017 and the importance of financial technology being used to provide more financial services. Improved today.
She stressed the important role that innovation plays in improving the efficiency of the payment system and maintaining the balance between innovation and stability that the National Bank of Cambodia regulators have to play to protect customer interests and maintain public confidence in the financial sector.
The Deputy Governor added that the information and knowledge gained from this program will be an important input for policy makers and authorities to better understand the state of financial technology development in the world and in Cambodia. And develop better policies and regulations to support the development of financial technology in Cambodia.
