(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that the "Board of Study, Marketing and Promotion of Tourism in Cambodia", chaired by the Ministry of Tourism, has been preparing new strategic plans to attract more international tourists to visit Cambodia. While some destinations have been changing during the trade war.
To achieve this, on October 2, 2018, the Board of Tourism Marketing and Promotion of Cambodia convened a meeting of its members at the Ministry of Tourism under the chairmanship of Minister Thong Khon on behalf of the Board.
After the meeting, Minister Thong Khon told Fresh News that the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Tourism Marketing and Promotion Board, after approving the bylaws and internal regulations, will continue to discuss the development of new marketing strategies for sector development. Cambodia's tourism is recovering as the world faces a trade war crisis caused by the United States and China.
The Minister said that the trade war crisis has caused some destinations in the tourism market to change, and Cambodia must strive to capture the market or any potential tourism destination, that is, to develop strategies, means and budget to promote. The main goal is to attract more tourists to Cambodia with quality and efficiency.
Mr. Thong Khon stressed that for the Chinese tourism market, Cambodia needs to be further strengthened because China is a large global tourism market, but must go deep into any important potential goals and that Cambodia needs to organize well in It is the same with the markets in ASEAN, Asia, Europe and the United States, with the need to target and use all means of budgeting effectively.
Please be informed that in front of today's meeting, the Board of Study, Marketing and Tourism Promotion of Cambodia discussed in detail on three important points, including:
First. Statute of the Cambodia Tourism Marketing and Promotion Board.
Second. Internal Rules of the Cambodia Tourism Marketing and Promotion Board.
Third. Decision on the Establishment of 5 Expert Working Groups: Overseas Tourism Marketing and Outreach Working Group, Local International Tourism Event Management Working Group, Tourism and Digital Publishing Management Working Group, Study Tour Organizing Working Group (Fam Trip) and a working group to organize overseas tourism representatives, as well as the establishment of the Secretariat of the Board of Study, Marketing and Promotion of Cambodia.
