(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of October 2, 2019, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries issued a press release clarifying the case of Facebook users posting pictures and messages criticizing the management of the Phnom Tamao Zoo and Wildlife Rescue Center. The Ministry of Agriculture's forest, accusing the emaciated animals of lack of food, but the ministry dismissed the criticism.
"A small number of emaciated wild animals at Phnom Tamao Zoo are not due to lack of food, but because the animals are sick or injured due to illegal trapping, or there are breeders who do not want to raise or have health problems, they fall ill and become emaciated," the ministry said. It has been handed over to the Forestry Administration and partner organizations to take care of it and treat it, and then some of the wildlife there is emaciated, which seems to lack food.
The ministry said that in 2018, Phnom Tamao Zoo and Wildlife Rescue Center rescued 1,893 new wildlife, treated 257 wildlife and was taking care of 1,586 wildlife (birds). 54 species of mammals, 41 species of mammals and 12 species of reptiles) and restored 1,484 species of wildlife and released all species into the wild.
In the first nine months of 2019, Phnom Tamao Zoo and Wildlife Rescue Center rescued 767 new wildlife, treated 207 wild animals and maintained 1625 wildlife (53 birds, 41 mammals). 13 species and reptiles) and restored 674 species of wildlife and released all species into the wild.
At the same time, the Ministry of Agriculture is committed to the care and protection of wildlife, Cambodia's precious natural resources, by continuing to pay attention to strengthening law enforcement, disseminating laws, regulations and care. Preserve as well as treat all kinds of wildlife as an inheritance for our children, this generation and the next.
