PRASAC provides green loans to improve people's livelihood and protect the environment
(Phnom Penh): PRASAC is the largest financial institution that has been actively involved in improving the financial environment in Cambodia, especially providing green loans to improve people's livelihoods and contribute to social and environmental protection.
PRASAC Green Credit was created to contribute to reducing energy consumption savings by at least 20%, enabling people to increase productivity, employment and household income. The green loans that PRASAC provides include loans for the construction of biogas plants, loans for tractors and energy-saving bulldozers.
Mr. Say Sony, President of PRASAC, said that PRASAC has been participating in the National Biodigester Program of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries since 2007 in providing loans for the construction of biodigesters and loans for the purchase of tractors and bulldozers. Power since 2016. Giving green loans for the purpose of increasing family income and contributing to environmental protection.
Mr. Sony added that PRASAC provides this loan at low interest rate, long term, easy and flexible repayment, which facilitates the use of loans of customers. PRASAC continues to expand the scope and promote the importance of using green credit more widely.
Please also note that PRASAC not only provides green loans, but also provides loans for agricultural business, purchasing equipment and many other businesses.
