Professor Saphon Vattanak, Rector of the University of Health Sciences, said that since becoming a public administration institution in 2001, the university has prepared and implemented two strategic plans. 2008 to 2012 and the second strategic plan is implemented from 2014 to 2018.
As for the third strategic plan to be implemented from 2019 to 2023, in order to prepare the strategic plan for 2019-2023 of the university to be of good quality, the university has organized the process with 4 stages of consultation and consultation.
* Phase 1: Orientation in strategic planning
* Phase 2: Consultation at the faculty, school and university level
* Phase 3: Further consultation with partners and other stakeholders of the University of Health Sciences.
* Phase 4: Submit the draft strategic plan to the University Board for review and decision before compiling the Strategic Plan Book 2019-2023.
He added that this workshop is the third phase of the strategic plan 2019 to 2023, with the participation of the leadership of the Ministry of Health, the leadership of the University from the Deputy Director and Ms. in charge. At the university, there are about 90 representatives of hospitals, national centers, institutes, national and international partners.
