NetGuardians and First Cambodia hold seminar on risk management of data fraud through banking system
(Phnom Penh): The winner of the Swiss Financial Technology Award, NetGuardians, who has been recognized as an expert in enterprise risk management systems to combat fraud through the banking system, has partnered with First Cambodia to organize Roundtable and its second successful in Cambodia.
In addition, Tang Borath, CEO of First Cambodia, said that cyber fraud will reach 6 billion US dollars by 2021, and this is the main problem for both banks. All over the world, including banks in Cambodia.
With a business partner that is a world-class company specializing in data fraud risk management, NetGuardians is extremely proud to be able to contribute information and advice on banking security solutions. In Cambodia, as well as the recent roundtable.
The parties discussed in an open, honest manner and described in detail the current threats facing the Bank and the rapidly changing Banking Landscape. In addition, learn as much as we can about the trends of technology fraud and information sharing, which is the best way to ensure that all banks are protected from fraud. Data when the bank is equipped with a risk mitigation system
He expressed confidence that the roundtable would benefit the entire banking industry, not just the presence of participating banks, as companies that develop software that applies to what has been researched.
NetGuardians is an award-winning Swiss financial technology company. Founded in 2007, it facilitates the management of 50 banks around the world, including banks from Tier 1 to Tier 3, in the fight against financial crime.
