The new generation of schools is a new curriculum that the Ministry of Education has implemented in the pilot phase in 2015. This practice is done in both primary and secondary schools in order to improve education in Cambodia. As with some countries in the region and in the world. There are currently 10 schools and are implementing this new generation school curriculum.
There are 4 primary schools and 6 secondary schools. These schools include: Preah Sisowath High School, Hun Sen High School, Kampong Cham High School, Prek Leap High School, Samdech Chea Sim High School, Prek Anchanh High School, Hun Sen Peam Chi Kang High School, Kork Pring Secondary School, Hun Sen Primary School, Kampong Cham Primary School, Preah Reach Akka Mohesey Primary School, Angkor Ban Primary School and Prohot Primary School.
The curriculum focuses on integrating technology into the education of both learners and instructors, as well as providing a wide range of learning tools. In particular, the study time is longer than the old curriculum.
