Representatives of 161 families involved in land dispute for about 15 years in Sen Sok district thanked the leaders and relevant officials for resolving it completely
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 2, 2019, 161 families came out to thank the leaders of the Royal Government, professional officials and the authorities of Sen Sok district for resolving their land successfully after the conflict. Fifteen years ago, there were only two families who refused to move out of their land, despite being settled with full funding.
Representatives of the 161 families came out and explained that some crooks always cheated others that more than 2 hectares of land in Factory Village, Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok is still a land dispute. "The land above has been inhabited by 163 families for a long time," they said. And more than 2 hectares of land was sold to Mr. Banh Uyta with all the money, while the two families living in the land also received all the money but did not leave this location.
Representatives of 161 families also claimed that the land they won by the power of the Court of Appeal Judgment No. 01 dated 08 February 2018 was also sold to Mr. Banh Uyta and Mr. Kim Subut as representatives. That's it.
The press conference was held on the morning of October 2, 2019, with people's representatives holding documents to present to reporters on the land located in Factory Village 1, Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok.
Ms. Houy Daravy, a representative of 161 out of 163 families, said that the land case has been going on for more than 15 years, which they have won against Ms. Keo Nam, Mr. Kim Kao and Ms. Chea Sarom and has been brought before the court. Mr. Kol Bun, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and an officer in charge of bailiffs, and with the participation of the authorities and authorities of Sen Sok district to implement the judgment to hand over the land to them.
After receiving the land, the people's representatives made a title deed and divided the land into 4 meters by 18 meters. As they could not afford to develop the land, 161 families agreed to sell it to Banh Uyta and Kim Subut as representatives.
The people's representative said that the press conference was held to thank and inform the leaders at all levels and the authorities, and the land dispute case of 163 families has ended.
As for the two individuals who own the land and do not sell it and continue to live on the company's land, it is the individual who committed the crime and now the company is suing the court for legal action.
It should be noted that the disputed land is 10,750 square meters, which has been sued for about 15 years, and 163 families have won. They still remember that April 18, 2018 was the day of the execution of the judgment to return the land to the people.
