HONG KONG (Reuters) - A Hong Kong police officer shot and killed a protester in the chest after he and other police officers were attacked by protesters during a protest rally in Hong Kong on Tuesday. This is according to the release by CNA on Tuesday, October 1, 2019.
Speaking to the media on condition of anonymity, witnesses at the scene said a Hong Kong police officer had decided to pull out a gun and shoot a protester in the chest in Tsuen Wan after he was attacked. Police also claimed that the police used guns to protect themselves, but this was the first time the protesters were in the real bullet in several months.
According to local media, the protester was an 18-year-old man, while more than 30 others were being treated in hospital after clashes with police. Police.
