Acting Head of State wants Cambodia-Germany to expand cooperation in all fields in the new ambassadorial term
(Phnom Penh): Acting Head of State of Cambodia Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum expressed his desire for Cambodia-Germany to expand cooperation in the fields of economy, trade, investment, culture, tourism, education and increase people-to-people exchanges. More people and people during the tenure of the new Ambassador of Germany to Cambodia.
The Ambassador stated that through his diplomatic mission in Cambodia, he will strive to further enhance the friendly relations and good cooperation between the governments, peoples and countries of Germany and Cambodia, especially Germany. Want to help Cambodia have further economic development.
At the same time, he will work to promote the friendly relations and cooperation between Cambodia and the European Union to be better. In this regard, he will strive to help resolve all possible issues between Cambodia and the European Union well.
The Acting Head of State is confident that as the Ambassador of the Federal Republic of Germany to Cambodia, he will continue to deepen the friendship and cooperation between the two countries and strive for change. Mutual economic, trade, investment, culture, tourism, education, people-to-people exchanges to bring greater benefits for both peoples and countries.
