Tomorrow's program In addition to the distribution of certificates and diplomas, there will also be an announcement ceremony for the book "Hun Sen Cambodia". According to Ly Chheng, the book "Hun Sen Cambodia" was started in August 2015 and completed in May 2019.
18 rural roads in six provinces with a length of nearly 120 km will be built under a grant from the Chinese government this year
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chan Darong, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Rural Development, confirmed that in 2019, the Ministry of Rural Development plans to build 18 rural roads with 2 layers of rubber (DBST) with a length of nearly 120 km. In six target provinces with Chinese government assistance.
Speaking to Fresh News on October 2, 2019, the senior official confirmed that the project to build nearly 120 km of rural roads is part of the second phase of rural road improvement project under a grant from the Chinese government. Signed in August 2019.
The six target provinces are: Kampong Speu, Kampong Chhnang, Kandal, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng and Tbong Khmum.
For this rural road construction project, Mr. Chandarong confirmed that "We are currently in the process of selecting Chinese companies to start implementation, which we can hope to start in December 2019."
Separately, for the second phase of the rural water supply project, which is also a grant from the Chinese government, the Ministry will have to drill 964 pump wells, dig 12 community ponds and dig 42 stone ponds in the target provinces. 10: Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Pursat, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Speu, Kampot, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng and Kampong Cham.
The launch of the second phase of the Rural Water Supply and Rural Road Improvement Project under a grant from the Chinese government comes after the Ministry of Rural Development successfully completed the first phase of the Rural Water Supply and Rural Road Improvement Project.
The first phase of rural water supply project was completed 100% on July 9, 2018, drilling 846 water wells, digging 45 community ponds and digging 28 stone community ponds in the province. The targets of the six projects are: Kampong Speu, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Thom, Kandal, Tbong Khmum and Svay Rieng provinces.
