Especially during the recently closed Kan Ben and Pchum Ben festivals, people participated in this traditional Khmer celebration with great fun with maintaining good security and order under the shade. Peace of the society. Letter to readers: "Pchum Ben 2019 shows that the Cambodian people are happy to support peace and a curse for Sam Rainsy!"
(Phnom Penh): The Pchum Ben festival, which has just ended, is another very important and practical discipline for measuring the joy and happiness of the Cambodian people for their achievements.
What is noteworthy is that this year the Pchum Ben festival is busier than previous years. Obviously, in many resorts, traffic jams occur everywhere. It takes hours to reach the destination. At the entrance to the capital, there is heavy congestion for tens of kilometers, both before and after Pchum, when people leave the city and rush back to the city.
Who has seen such a situation in Cambodia before? Certainly not.
Are there any Cambodians who wish to see Pchum Ben, New Year, Independence Day or Water Festival turn into chaos, violence, bloodshed according to the coup plots of a handful of extremist politicians? The answer is definitely no.
Unlike the Cambodian people throughout the kingdom who are rejoicing and supporting the peace and tranquility they have all benefited from, there is a group of wandering political groups led by Sam Rainsy who do not recognize sin and take advantage of it. This happy and pure religious tradition to incite separatism according to its dark coup plan without shame and without fear of going to hell.
I think that Mr. Sam Rainsy and his colleagues should be aware of the series of failures that they have been trying to achieve in recent years.
Sam Rainsy's second major defeat was the announcement of the "Sleep, Win, Clean" campaign during the July 29, 2018 election. More than 83% of eligible Cambodians went to the polls and gave a landslide victory to the party led by Prime Minister Hun Sen, who stood firm in defending the peace and security of the people. .
Therefore, all these failures, combined with the participation of people all over the country to celebrate the Pchum Ben 2019, is really a curse for Mr. Sam Rainsy and his partner.
