(Banteay Meanchey): Authorities temporarily suspended traffic for heavy vehicles on Provincial Road 268A from National Road 6 to Ang Trapeang Thmor, Phnom Srok District, Banteay Meanchey Province due to the flood situation. This is according to the announcement of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Banteay Meanchey Province, which was received by Fresh News on the evening of September 30, 2019.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Public Works confirmed that due to the flood from the upper part of Thmor Puok district, Svay Chek district and Poipet city, the water flooded the road with a total length of 1,350 meters, so to protect and maintain the road for a long time. In order not to cause serious damage, the department would like to temporarily stop the traffic on this section of the road, wait for the water level to recede and improve, then resume normal traffic.
