(Phnom Penh): Mr. Som Komsan, Deputy Principal of Sisowath High School in charge of the new generation of schools, confirmed the results of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to establish a new generation of schools by the rate of students who study in this school to pass the high school diploma exam (Bakdup). Annual growth.
Speaking in an interview on the weekly special guest program, a program of Fresh News TV, Mr. Sam Komsan said that the new generation school is the initiative of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, and this school is a school States with higher investment than regular public schools.
He added that the new generation of schools has been piloting since 2016 until now for 5 years.
He added that the goal of this high investment is to get the quality of higher education to meet the actual market needs of some countries such as Singapore, Thailand, Japan and Korea, which we recognize that the education and high standards. We also want such human resources, so we have researched teaching methods, so the Ministry has organized such education.
He added that the new learning reform gives students more opportunities to compete and have more motivation to learn. By participating in both national and international competitions, the students of the new generation of schools can win a total of gold, silver and bronze medals, which increase every year.
Please be informed that New Generation School is a new curriculum that the Ministry of Education has implemented in the pilot phase in 2015. This implementation is for both primary and secondary schools in order to improve education in Cambodia. Better as some countries in the region and the world. There are currently 10 schools and are implementing this new generation school curriculum.
(Siem Reap): The team of APSARA Authority will open the renovation of Kandal Srah Srong temple next year, while on the morning of September 30, 2019, they organized a Krong Pali ceremony to ask for permission from the owner of the water, the owner of the sacred objects that take care of the area. Angkor in repairing the central temple of Srah Srang to escape the risk as a legacy for future generations.
Mr. Yit Chanda, Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority, said that the project to renovate the Kandal Srah Srong temple was the second achievement after the water exercise donated by Ms. Seang Chanheng.
Please note that the central temple Srah Srang was built during the reign of King Jayavarman VII in the 12th century, which represents Mount Sumeru. Currently, the temple has been severely damaged by natural factors, and in order to enhance the history, construction of the temple and the cultural landscape of Srah Srang, the APSARA Authority and the private sector have joined forces to renovate the temple.
The repair process is scheduled to begin in the dry season as the water dries up, making it easier to dig, research and repair.
