(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia, stated that the banking and financial institutions in Cambodia are in good health and have contributed to the development of the national economy.
He added that the National Bank of Cambodia has strengthened its oversight and regulation with the subsequent introduction of macro-prudent policies, the issuance of financial stability reports and the strengthening of the Bank Stability Protection Network in line with international standards.
Please be informed that Article IV mission is conducted annually by the International Monetary Fund for member countries to monitor the economic situation in Cambodia and make recommendations for the implementation of economic policies.
The governor also informed the delegation about the economic growth in the past, especially in 2018, which Cambodia achieved at a rate of 7.5%. In 2019, the Royal Government expects growth to continue at around 7.1%, the highest level in the region.
At the same time, he said, the macroeconomic situation has improved, with inflation in the first half of 1.9 percent and expected to reach 2.2 percent in 2019. The Royal Government has set out strategies to support economic growth in the face of uncertain global economic growth, especially the diversification of growth, strengthening exports and imports, and increasing the investment climate.
The Governor-General thanked the IMF for supporting the Royal Government's policy on economic development in Cambodia, capacity building and technical assistance to Cambodia.
France provides technical assistance to Cambodia to support the implementation of the national budget reform strategy
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance and the French Ministry of Activities and Public Accounts this morning held a meeting on September 30, 2019 to announce the implementation of technical assistance to support the implementation of the 2018 budget reform strategy. -2025.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and Ms. Eva Nguyen Binh, Ambassador of the French Republic to Cambodia, with the participation of representatives from relevant ministries, institutions and development partners.
The purpose of the meeting to announce the implementation of this technical assistance is to:
1: Announcing the completion of the first phase to determine the concept and scope of cooperation based on two major principles: Cambodia's ownership and the application of the experience of French budget management reform in line with the Cambodian context, As well as the start of the implementation of technical assistance to support the implementation of the strategy of budget reform 2018-2025.
2: Establishing a schedule for a series of short-term missions of French experts until the end of the project.
Ms. Eva Nguyen Binh said that the technical assistance project is a highlight of economic and financial cooperation between France and Cambodia. This technical assistance project aims to help draft a new public financial system law and related regulations, budget management and accounting, to improve public financial management and efficiency of public expenditure with value, accountability and efficiency.
He added that the new cooperation will focus on the amendment of the Law on Public Financial System 2008, the preparation of Sub-Decree No. 81 on the establishment of financial controls on state budget expenditures and Sub-Decree No. 82. On the General Regulations of Public Accounts, as well as the development of the Cambodian Public Accounting Standards Framework.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth also said that due to historical factors, Cambodia and France have many similarities, especially in the public sector.
At this point, he emphasized that the principle of Cambodia is that we learn from the experience of other countries, but we will not copy them completely, that is, we will take the knowledge of the best practices in accordance with the Cambodian environment to ensure that the budget system. Ours can be realistic and can achieve our goals.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth also mentioned that in the past 15 years, the Royal Government of Cambodia has been working hard to reform public financial management, in which we have achieved some important progress and achievements as follows:
At the same time, it is more cost-effective, both at the allocation level and at the operational and technical level, especially at a faster and cost-effective operation. From 2013 to 2018, the total expenditure of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports was more than tripled, the Ministry of Health was nearly two-and-a-half times increased, and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries was nearly tripled.
Third: The gradual implementation of the Information Technology System for Public Financial Management (FMIS), which was officially implemented in 20 ministries / institutions and 25 Departments of Economy and Finance, Capital-Province, Ry The other 17 ministries / institutions will be officially announced in 2020.
Fifth, increasing the provision of more resources to sub-national administrations to meet the actual needs at the local level. The sub-national budget, which in 2014 accounted for only 4% of total budget or 1% of GDP, will increase to 10% of total budget or 2.8% of GDP by 2020.
Sixth, the participation of ministries / institutions in public financial management reform activities has been steadily increasing, especially in revenue management, budgeting, program budgeting, implementation of information technology budget and state property management. .
Mr. Vongsey Visoth also mentioned that in the past, we have been working to reform the management of public finances based on the old legal law, namely the Law on Public Financial System 2008, Sub-Decree No. 81 on Financial Supervision. Expenditure of the State Budget and Sub-Decree No. 82 on General Regulations of Public Accounts, which are 24 years old.
"Therefore, it is time for us to begin reviewing and modernizing the legal system and the legal basis in order to support the process of reforming the public financial system and the financial system in a comprehensive manner and enable us to push for reform," he said. The more effective and clearer the legal character.
At the same time, the vision and approach to budget reform is still based on four principles in one package:
