Brigadier General Ven Sovin, Deputy Police Commissioner of Kandal Province in charge of traffic planning, told Fresh News Agency in Kandal province on September 29 that the people have been rushing back to Phnom Penh, passing through Kandal province, it seems very busy. Very since the afternoon.
He said that until this evening, the traffic seems to be more and more busy, which indicates that the flow of people from their hometowns seems to be gaining momentum, especially at night, because tomorrow is the day they have to enter. Work or eat according to their respective skills.
Mr. Ven Sovin added that big and small cars, all series of modern motorcycles are driving on each national road, happily following each other, coming to Phnom Penh with a smiling face, it seems that our country is peaceful and happy.
Along with such incursions into Phnom Penh, the Deputy Commissioner continued that the law enforcement forces in each district around Kandal province were well organized to maintain traffic order, prevent and resolve any congestion that occurs in their respective localities.
At the same time, the Deputy Commissioner also asked all citizens to respect the traffic law "Today, tomorrow, do not have a traffic accident" Driving, please have good understanding, tolerance, respect the traffic law, respect the right to drive without alcohol on motorcycles. Wear a hat for small and large cars, wear a seat belt, do not overtake each other in dangerous situations.
