Please be informed that this traffic accident case compared to Pchum Ben 2018 has decreased 1 time, the number of deaths decreased 2 people and 5 people were injured.
Family members of journalists in Pursat province seek humanitarian assistance for Veteran journalist Nao Thoeun
(Pursat): After receiving information from a veteran journalist of Rasmei Kampuchea and the Cambodian News Agency AKP in Pursat province, Mr. Nao Thoeun had a difficult time, that is, he was seriously ill and was being treated at Lok Sang Hospital in Phnom Penh. .
Mr. Som Chea Ty also posted a message: "In a democracy, journalists have played an important role in informing the public and the government in a transparent, accurate and timely manner, especially in Cambodia today. Fully implement democracy under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Day by day, the freedom of the Cambodian press has increased positively, although sometimes slow, sometimes fast, but always forward. And the problem of journalists is helping to expand the freedom of the press in Cambodia.
Looking back on the life of a veteran journalist in Pursat province, Mr. Nao Thoeun has been working as a journalist since the 1980s, until now he is in a very difficult situation because he is getting older. He has no wife or children, no income to support his daily life and has a chronic illness. If you want to help him, please contact him at 011 700907. Thank you! "
