Wat Kang Meas organizes a local boat race to celebrate Pchum Ben!
(Kampong Thom): On September 28, 2019, the elders and the people, especially the youth, organized a boat race at Wat Kang Meas, Tnaot Chum commune, Baray district, Kampong Thom province.
The boat race, which has been missed for more than a decade, is now being re-organized for the first time under the support and presidency of Mr. Ny Phally, Chairman of the CPP Working Group to assist Tnaot Chum Commune and Ms. Heng Pisey; Representing Mr. Thong Khon, Chairman of the Party Working Group to help Baray and Taing Kork districts, as well as many colleagues and philanthropists.
He added that, however, today's activities are a show of solidarity and participation in promoting the traditional culture and identity of the nation as a whole and of the village as a whole.
Please note that the boat race to celebrate this year's Pchum Ben festival was attended by 16 pairs of boats with a capacity of 6 to 10 people and a total of more than 1,000 people.
Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign on September 28: 131 illegal vehicles were found and 131 fines were imposed.
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for September 28, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 131 vehicles, found 131 vehicles violated the law and fined 131 vehicles. This is according to the official report of the General Commission of the National Police.
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the leadership of the Inter-Ministerial Minister and the Cambodian delegation on an official visit to the Federal Republic of Germany, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, addressed the Cambodian people living there. Opposition parties have always sought to overthrow the legitimate Royal Government of Cambodia.
To begin with, all Cambodians welcomed Samdech Krala Hom and the high-level Cambodian delegation with warm respect and affection and declared their support for the current policy of the Royal Government, especially the anti-group policy. Want to create a new national war in Cambodia.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng spoke to Cambodians living in the Federal Republic of Germany about the political situation in Cambodia, citing the endless attempts of former opposition leaders in plotting to overthrow the Royal Government of Cambodia. Legal.
Addressing the event, Deputy Prime Minister Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng outlined the objectives and activities of the visit, which focused on strengthening bilateral cooperation with the German Federation and exploring the process of German sub-national administrative reform. Discuss some other related topics.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng continued that currently, the Royal Government of Cambodia has organized a national working group to visit the grassroots by holding public forums in all localities to collect opinions, concerns and suggestions from the people, and through this mechanism, the authorities The national and sub-national levels have solved a lot of people's problems effectively.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng added that in relation to the warning to withdraw the preferential tariff system from the European Union and from the United States, Cambodia is still trying to open talks to maintain this preferential tariff and to maintain a good diplomatic relationship with Europe and the United States.
The meeting between Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Minister of Inter-Ministerial Affairs and the Cambodian delegation with the Cambodian people living in the Federal Republic of Germany was held in a very friendly and happy atmosphere. People in Pursat Province Receive Free Medical Examination from Intercontinental Doctors
(Pursat): Mr. Kao Im Ron, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Information, representing Mr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions and Chairman of the Cambodian Muslim Development Foundation, led a group of Intercontinental Volunteer Doctors (PAC) from Arab countries such as Saudi Arabia. Udid Jordan Tunisia provides free medical check-ups to people in Pursat and other provinces across the country.
This program was held on the morning of September 27, 2019 until October 3, 2019 at Pursat Provincial Hospital with the cooperation of provincial health officials and doctors of provincial hospitals and volunteer doctors. Of the Muslim Development Foundation of Cambodia and also coordinated the work of the youth group of the Cambodian Muslim Youth League (CMYA) Pursat branch.
According to Mr. Kao Im Ron, this treatment program focuses on general surgery, such as cysts, tumors, tumors and other tumors, hernias, cosmetic surgery, all kinds of gynecology. Diseases of children, infants with problems or disabilities, common medical diseases such as diabetes, high blood pressure and infectious diseases.
